window.LL_MATS_CET4=[{"id":"cet2312s2-1","group":"2023年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"News Report 1 · 五岁男孩开车上高速要去买兰博基尼","material":"2023年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 1（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目与解析：仓库真题PDF/解析PDF + 新东方真题页；答案：解析详解逐题核对","sentences":[{"en":"A police officer in the U.S. stopped a large SUV car that was going very slowly and drifting across lanes on a highway.","zh":"美国一名警察拦下一辆在高速公路上行驶极慢、来回漂移跨车道的大型SUV。"},{"en":"He expected to find a driver who was either very drunk or having a medical emergency.","zh":"他以为会发现司机要么喝得酩酊大醉，要么正突发疾病。"},{"en":"Instead, the officer discovered a five-year-old boy sat on the edge of the driver’s seat.","zh":"结果，警察发现坐在驾驶座边缘的是一个五岁男孩。"},{"en":"His feet could barely reach the brake, and his head was only just high enough to see out of the windows.","zh":"他的脚勉强够到刹车，头也只刚好高到能看见窗外。"},{"en":"The child had taken the keys to the family car while his teenage sister was napping.","zh":"这孩子是趁十几岁的姐姐打盹时拿走了家里汽车的钥匙。"},{"en":"He then drove three kilometers across town before getting on the highway.","zh":"他开车穿过了三公里的城区，然后上了高速公路。"},{"en":"The boy later told confused officers that he was planning to travel to California and buy a Lamborghini sports car.","zh":"男孩后来告诉一头雾水的警察们，他打算去加利福尼亚州，买一辆兰博基尼跑车。"},{"en":"Although he only had three dollars in his wallet, at least he was driving in the right direction.","zh":"虽然他钱包里只有三美元，但至少他开的方向是对的。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why did the police officer stop the SUV car?","opts":["He noticed the driver was too young to drive","He found there was no one sitting at the wheel","He thought something must be wrong with the driver","He saw the driver changing lanes much too frequently"],"answer":2,"expl":"He expected to find a driver who was either very drunk or having a medical emergency——以为司机出了问题才拦车。A、B 都是拦车之后才发现的事，D 是拦车前看到的表象不是动机。","signal":"expected 一词点明拦车动机","syn":[["expected to find a driver ... having a medical emergency","thought something must be wrong with the driver（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did the boy tell the police officers he was planning to do?","opts":["Buy a sports car","Drive across town","Leave California","Visit his sister"],"answer":0,"expl":"he was planning to travel to California and buy a Lamborghini sports car——买跑车。B 是已做的事、C 方向相反、D 无中生有。","signal":"told ... he was planning to 目的句","syn":[["buy a Lamborghini sports car","Buy a sports car（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2312s2-2","group":"2023年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"科普","level":"四级","title":"News Report 2 · 低头玩手机，头后会长\"骨刺\"","material":"2023年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 2（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目与解析：仓库真题PDF/解析PDF + 新东方真题页；答案：解析详解逐题核对","sentences":[{"en":"Mobile phones have changed the way we live, how we read, work, communicate, and shop.","zh":"手机改变了我们生活、阅读、工作、交流和购物的方式。"},{"en":"But we already know this.","zh":"但这我们已经知道了。"},{"en":"What we have not yet understood is the way the tiny machines in front of us are changing our skeletons, possibly altering not just the way we behave but even the very shape of our bodies.","zh":"我们还不了解的是，这些眼前的小机器正在改变我们的骨骼——可能不仅改变行为方式，甚至改变身体的形状。"},{"en":"New scientific research at the University of the Sunshine Coast in Queensland, Australia, suggests that young people are developing extra pieces of bone at the backs of their heads.","zh":"澳大利亚昆士兰阳光海岸大学的新科学研究表明，年轻人的后脑勺正在长出额外的骨块。"},{"en":"These pieces of bone are caused by the way people bend their heads when they use the phone.","zh":"这些骨块是人们用手机时低头的方式造成的。"},{"en":"This shifts weight onto the muscles at the back of the head and causes the bone to grow in a way that is not normal.","zh":"这使重量转移到后脑的肌肉上，导致骨骼以不正常的方式生长。"},{"en":"This process can be compared to the way the skin hardens in response to constant rubbing or pressure.","zh":"这一过程可以比作皮肤因持续摩擦或压迫而变硬。"},{"en":"The result is a piece of bone like a horn that sticks out from the head by the neck.","zh":"结果就是脖子上方长出一块像角一样的骨头。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the report say we have not yet understood about mobile phones?","opts":["How they change the way we shop","How they alter human skeletons","How they cause increased headaches","How they affect our communication"],"answer":1,"expl":"the tiny machines ... are changing our skeletons——改变骨骼。其余三项都是手机常见影响的编造。","signal":"What we have not yet understood 设问","syn":[["changing our skeletons","alter human skeletons（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What happens to the skin when rubbed or pressed constantly?","opts":["It loosens","It brightens","It hardens","It softens"],"answer":2,"expl":"the skin hardens in response to constant rubbing or pressure——皮肤会变硬。类比说明，考的是 harden。","signal":"类比句 can be compared to","syn":[["the skin hardens","It hardens（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2312s2-3","group":"2023年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"News Report 3 · 橘猫 Wilbur 的十岁生日派对","material":"2023年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 3（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目与解析：仓库真题PDF/解析PDF + 新东方真题页；答案：解析详解逐题核对","sentences":[{"en":"A village is going to throw a birthday party for an orange cat named Wilbur, who has become famous for making a regular appearance at local shops.","zh":"一个村庄将为一只名叫威尔伯的橘猫举办生日派对，这只猫因经常出现在当地商店而小有名气。"},{"en":"Wilbur has his own Internet pages as he approaches his 10th birthday on July, 7.","zh":"威尔伯即将在7月7日迎来10岁生日，还有自己的网页。"},{"en":"Wilbur is both bold and friendly.","zh":"威尔伯胆子大又友好。"},{"en":"He spends most of his time in shops and businesses around the village.","zh":"它大部分时间都待在村里的商店和店铺里。"},{"en":"He’ll just take himself into any shop, anywhere.","zh":"不管哪家店，它说进就进。"},{"en":"There was one time when the doctor’s receptionist came back and he was sitting on her chair.","zh":"有一次诊所的前台回来，发现它正坐在人家的椅子上。"},{"en":"Among his favorite haunts are a local hairdresser, two pubs, and the Nottingham Primary School.","zh":"它最爱去的地方包括一家理发店、两家酒吧和诺丁汉小学。"},{"en":"Lesley Harper, who runs one of the pubs, said the cat has been a big hit with their customers.","zh":"经营其中一家酒吧的莱斯利·哈珀说，这只猫很受顾客欢迎。"},{"en":"“He’s been a regular visitor for most of this year,” she told the Press Association.","zh":"「今年大半年它都是常客，」她对英国新闻联合社说。"},{"en":"“He’s a very relaxed cat, happy for customers and villagers young and old to come in and say hello.”","zh":"「它非常放松，不管男女老少进来打招呼它都乐意。」"},{"en":"She also said he is a cat of expensive tastes who likes his high priced cat food.","zh":"她还说这只猫口味讲究，爱吃高价猫粮。"},{"en":"Sarah Godfrey, who is organizing Wilbur’s party, told the local newspaper, “Wilbur is part of our lives, as he is for everyone who lives in the village.”","zh":"组织威尔伯生日派对的萨拉·戈弗雷对当地报纸说：「威尔伯是我们生活的一部分，就像它属于村里每一个人。」"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the report say the village is going to do for the cat Wilbur?","opts":["Create Internet pages for him","Ask a local pet shop to adopt him","Name an orange tree after him","Hold a birthday party for him"],"answer":3,"expl":"throw a birthday party——办生日派对，D 对应。","signal":"首句即答案","syn":[["throw a birthday party","Hold a birthday party for him（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do we learn from the report about the cat?","opts":["He is a bold and aggressive pet","He pays regular visits to village shops","He once bit a doctor's receptionist","He likes to sit on the hairdresser's chair"],"answer":1,"expl":"making a regular appearance at local shops / He spends most of his time in shops——常逛商店。A 的 aggressive 与 friendly 相反。","signal":"细节对应","syn":[["regular appearance at local shops","pays regular visits to village shops（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the pub owner Lesley Harper say about the cat?","opts":["He is fond of luxury cat food","He likes to stay in villagers' houses","He knows everybody in the village","He often seeks food around her pub"],"answer":0,"expl":"a cat of expensive tastes who likes his high priced cat food——口味讲究，爱吃贵价猫粮。","signal":"引语处设题","syn":[["expensive tastes ... high priced cat food","He is fond of luxury cat food（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2312s2-4","group":"2023年12月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"生活","level":"四级","title":"Conversation 1 · 午饭去哪儿吃？意大利新餐馆走起","material":"2023年12月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 1（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目与解析：仓库真题PDF/解析PDF + 新东方真题页；答案：解析详解逐题核对","sentences":[{"en":"So, where do you want to go for lunch?","spk":"M","zh":"M：那么，午饭你想去哪儿吃？"},{"en":"I don’t know.","spk":"W","zh":"W：不知道。"},{"en":"Do you have anything in mind?","spk":"W","zh":"W：你有想法吗？"},{"en":"What about the Sandwich Place on Camden Street?","spk":"M","zh":"M：卡姆登街那家三明治店怎么样？"},{"en":"Hmm...","spk":"W","zh":"W：嗯……"},{"en":"No, sorry.","spk":"W","zh":"W：不，抱歉。"},{"en":"I don’t feel like sandwiches today.","spk":"W","zh":"W：我今天不想吃三明治。"},{"en":"It’s a great place, but I think we go there too often.","spk":"W","zh":"W：那家不错，但我们去得太勤了。"},{"en":"That’s true.","spk":"M","zh":"M：倒是真的。"},{"en":"Remember that’s where we saw Brigette Clark, the famous movie star.","spk":"M","zh":"M：记得就是在那儿我们看到了著名影星布里吉特·克拉克。"},{"en":"Of course.","spk":"W","zh":"W：当然。"},{"en":"How could I ever forget?","spk":"W","zh":"W：怎么可能忘？"},{"en":"There were crowds of people around her asking for a photo with her.","spk":"W","zh":"W：当时一大群人围着她求合影。"},{"en":"What about hamburgers, then?","spk":"M","zh":"M：那汉堡呢？"},{"en":"There’s that American style diner on the way to the mall.","spk":"M","zh":"M：去商场的路上有家美式餐厅。"},{"en":"I like that place.","spk":"W","zh":"W：我喜欢那儿。"},{"en":"Their chips are great, but their service takes a long time.","spk":"W","zh":"W：他们薯条很棒，但上菜特别慢。"},{"en":"And I need to get back by 2:30 for a conference call.","spk":"W","zh":"W：而且我2点半得回来开会。"},{"en":"How about trying something new?","spk":"W","zh":"W：要不试点新东西？"},{"en":"We could try Mario’s, the new Italian restaurant on the corner.","spk":"W","zh":"W：我们可以试试街角那家新开的意大利餐馆 Mario's。"},{"en":"It looks all right.","spk":"W","zh":"W：看起来不错。"},{"en":"Have you been there?","spk":"W","zh":"W：你去过吗？"},{"en":"No, I haven’t, but I’ve noticed that it has great reviews on the Internet.","spk":"M","zh":"M：没去过，但我注意到网上对它评价很高。"},{"en":"It’s supposed to be one of the best Italian restaurants in town.","spk":"M","zh":"M：据说是城里最好的意大利餐馆之一。"},{"en":"I think Jeremy has been there and said it was amazing.","spk":"M","zh":"M：杰里米去过，说特别棒。"},{"en":"I’m up for that.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我同意去那儿。"},{"en":"Cool.","spk":"W","zh":"W：好。"},{"en":"Have you asked Jeremy if he would like to come with us?","spk":"W","zh":"W：你问过杰里米想不想一起去吗？"},{"en":"I already have.","spk":"M","zh":"M：问过了。"},{"en":"He says he can’t.","spk":"M","zh":"M：他说来不了。"},{"en":"He has brought his own lunch today, so he will stay in.","spk":"M","zh":"M：他今天自己带了午饭，就在办公室吃。"},{"en":"I think his wife made him some soup.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我想是他妻子给他做了汤。"},{"en":"Poor Jeremy.","spk":"W","zh":"W：可怜的杰里米。"},{"en":"His wife is a terrible cook.","spk":"W","zh":"W：他老婆厨艺太差了。"},{"en":"He should throw that soup in the bin and join us.","spk":"W","zh":"W：他应该把那汤扔进垃圾桶，跟我们一起去。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What are the speakers mainly talking about?","opts":["Who to order the food","Whether to have sandwiches","When to go for their meal","Where to have their lunch"],"answer":3,"expl":"整段围绕午饭去哪儿吃展开——去哪儿就餐。其余选项都只是对话里的碎片。","signal":"开头设问统领全篇","syn":[["where do you want to go for lunch","Where to have their lunch（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Where did the speakers see the famous movie star?","opts":["In the shopping center nearby","In the expensive Italian style diner","At the Sandwich Place on Camden Street","At the American restaurant they frequent"],"answer":2,"expl":"Remember that's where we saw Brigette Clark——\"那儿\"指上文卡姆登街的三明治店。","signal":"回指定位 that's where","syn":[["the Sandwich Place on Camden Street","At the Sandwich Place on Camden Street（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why does the woman need to get back by 2:30?","opts":["There is to be a conference call","She has to meet with her boss then","There will be crowds of people waiting for her","She will have a photo taken with Brigette Clark"],"answer":0,"expl":"I need to get back by 2:30 for a conference call——有个电话会议。","signal":"for 引出目的","syn":[["for a conference call","There is to be a conference call（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why does the woman say Jeremy should throw his soup in the bin?","opts":["She doesn't deem homemade soup tasty","She doesn't think his wife cooks well","When to go for their meal","Where to have their lunch"],"answer":1,"expl":"His wife is a terrible cook——她觉得他妻子做饭难吃。","signal":"前因后果句","syn":[["His wife is a terrible cook","She doesn't think his wife cooks well（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2312s2-5","group":"2023年12月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"生活","level":"四级","title":"Conversation 2 · 酒店入住：全家出游订房记","material":"2023年12月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 2（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目与解析：仓库真题PDF/解析PDF + 新东方真题页；答案：解析详解逐题核对","sentences":[{"en":"Hi, there.","spk":"W","zh":"W：您好！"},{"en":"How are you today?","spk":"W","zh":"W：今天过得怎么样？"},{"en":"Do you have a reservation with us already?","spk":"W","zh":"W：您在我们这儿预订过房间吗？"},{"en":"Good afternoon.","spk":"M","zh":"M：下午好。"},{"en":"Yes, we reserved our rooms yesterday morning on your website for three nights.","spk":"M","zh":"M：订了，昨天早上在你们网站上订的三晚。"},{"en":"The name’s Patterson.","spk":"M","zh":"M：姓帕特森。"},{"en":"Okay.","spk":"W","zh":"W：好的。"},{"en":"Let me have a look.","spk":"W","zh":"W：我查一下。"},{"en":"Yes, we have it here.","spk":"W","zh":"W：查到了，有预订。"},{"en":"You brought the whole family with you, I see.","spk":"W","zh":"W：您带全家一起来了啊。"},{"en":"Yes, the two kids, my wife and I, and her parents too.","spk":"M","zh":"M：是的，两个孩子、我和我太太，还有她父母。"},{"en":"Great.","spk":"W","zh":"W：好。"},{"en":"So we have a family room for you and your wife and the kids, and another double room for your parents-in-law.","spk":"W","zh":"W：给您和太太孩子安排一间家庭房，给岳父母一间大床房。"},{"en":"They are right next to each other on the ground floor, since you mentioned in your message that they have trouble with stairs.","spk":"W","zh":"W：两个房间在一楼相邻，因为您留言说他们爬楼梯不方便。"},{"en":"That’s wonderful.","spk":"M","zh":"M：太好了。"},{"en":"My father-in-law has had terrible problems getting up and down stairs since his knee operation last April.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我岳父去年四月做了膝关节手术，上下楼梯一直很困难。"},{"en":"I’m sorry to hear that.","spk":"W","zh":"W：听到这个很遗憾。"},{"en":"And if you need any help to find transportation for the whole family, we can definitely recommend someone for you.","spk":"W","zh":"W：如果您需要为全家安排交通，我们绝对可以为您推荐可靠的人。"},{"en":"We were thinking of renting a car, but we will explore all the options available for sure.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我们本来想租车，但肯定也会把所有选择都比一比。"},{"en":"So, yes, that would be very helpful in comparing prices.","spk":"M","zh":"M：所以，是的，能帮我们比价就太有用了。"},{"en":"We’re also wondering what tours and day trips are available.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我们还想知道有什么观光项目和一日游。"},{"en":"We have bunches of brochures here.","spk":"W","zh":"W：我们这儿有很多宣传册。"},{"en":"I would recommend getting out on a boat trip.","spk":"W","zh":"W：我推荐坐船出游。"},{"en":"The kids will love it and there are so many islands nearby to explore.","spk":"W","zh":"W：孩子们会喜欢的，附近有好多岛屿可以探索。"},{"en":"There’s also a great night market further into town that has all kinds of food and cool little shops selling souvenirs and local jewelry and clothing made by hand.","spk":"W","zh":"W：镇中心还有个很棒的夜市，各种美食都有，还有卖纪念品、本地首饰和手工服装的小店。"},{"en":"That all sounds marvelous.","spk":"M","zh":"M：听起来都太棒了。"},{"en":"Now, all I need is to photocopy your passports and then I can get you all checked in and show you to your rooms.","spk":"W","zh":"W：现在只需要复印一下你们的护照，就能给您们办理入住、带您们去房间了。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Who is the man talking to in the conversation?","opts":["A landlady","A waitress","A receptionist","A saleswoman"],"answer":2,"expl":"办预订、复印护照、办入住——女士是酒店前台接待员。landlady（房东太太）是干扰。","signal":"职业推断题，抓关键词 reservation / check in","syn":[["get you all checked in","A receptionist（语义对应）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do we learn about the man's father-in-law from the conversation?","opts":["He was involved in a terrible car accident last April","He has much difficulty getting up and down stairs","He is expected to undergo a knee operation","He prefers to stay next door to the children"],"answer":1,"expl":"has had terrible problems getting up and down stairs since his knee operation——上下楼梯很困难。C 时态偷换：手术已经做完，不是\"预计要做\"。","signal":"健康细节定位","syn":[["terrible problems getting up and down stairs","He has much difficulty getting up and down stairs（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why does the man say they will explore all the options available?","opts":["To please his parents-in-law","To find the best trip for his kids","To satisfy his curiosity","To compare prices"],"answer":3,"expl":"that would be very helpful in comparing prices——为了比价。","signal":"目的问答","syn":[["comparing prices","To compare prices（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the woman suggest the man and his family do near the end of the conversation?","opts":["Visit a local art gallery","Go on a boat trip","To satisfy his curiosity","He prefers to stay next door to the children"],"answer":1,"expl":"I would recommend getting out on a boat trip——乘船出游。","signal":"建议句 I would recommend","syn":[["getting out on a boat trip","Go on a boat trip（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2312s2-6","group":"2023年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"科技","level":"四级","title":"Passage 1 · 让 AI 替你谈判？你可能更容易使诈","material":"2023年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 1（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目与解析：仓库真题PDF/解析PDF + 新东方真题页；答案：解析详解逐题核对","sentences":[{"en":"Artificial intelligence agents play ever more influential roles in our lives.","zh":"人工智能代理在我们的生活中扮演着越来越有影响力的角色。"},{"en":"They do everything from suggesting new friends to recommending purchases.","zh":"从推荐新朋友到推荐购买，无所不做。"},{"en":"They’re even beginning to drive our cars.","zh":"它们甚至开始驾驶我们的汽车。"},{"en":"Another role that they are expected to take over is negotiating on our behalf in commercial transactions or legal disputes.","zh":"人们还期待它们接管的另一个角色，是在商业交易或法律纠纷中代表我们谈判。"},{"en":"So, it’s important to know whether using an artificial intelligence agent might affect how we negotiate.","zh":"所以，重要的是要知道：使用人工智能代理是否会影响我们的谈判方式。"},{"en":"Research indicates that it does.","zh":"研究表明，会的。"},{"en":"In a new study, participants were told to imagine that they were negotiating for something important to them, like a house.","zh":"在一项新研究中，参与者被要求想象自己在为重要的东西谈判，比如一栋房子。"},{"en":"Next, they were told either that they would negotiate for themselves, or they would program an artificial intelligence agent to negotiate for them.","zh":"然后，他们被告知要么亲自谈判，要么编程让人工智能代理替他们谈判。"},{"en":"Participants then completed a survey indicating how tough, deceptive and pleasant or otherwise they wanted to be, or wanted their agent to be, in the negotiations.","zh":"参与者随后完成一份问卷，表明在谈判中他们想让自己（或代理）表现得多强硬、多狡猾、多友善或不友善。"},{"en":"For example, participants could choose to be tough by making an opening demand far greater than what they’d be willing to accept.","zh":"比如，参与者可以选择表现强硬：开出一个远高于自己心理价位的要价。"},{"en":"They could also choose to express sympathy with their opponent to appear pleasant.","zh":"他们也可以选择对对手表达同情，以显得友善。"},{"en":"But they could also indicate that they—or their agent—would strategically express anger toward the opponent to gain advantage, or they could opt to convey dissatisfaction with the encounter so that the other party would think they were losing interest.","zh":"但他们也可以表明——自己或代理——会策略性地向对手发怒来获取优势，或者表达对谈判的不满，让对方以为自己快没兴趣了。"},{"en":"These are both examples of deceptive strategies.","zh":"这两者都是\"欺骗策略\"的例子。"},{"en":"Participants were more willing to employ deceptive strategies when assigned an agent to negotiate on their behalf.","zh":"当被安排由代理代为谈判时，参与者更愿意使用欺骗策略。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the passage say about artificial intelligence agents?","opts":["They are more intelligent than many of us","They have already become our new friends","They have begun to affect our social behavior","They play increasingly more important roles"],"answer":3,"expl":"play ever more influential roles in our lives——扮演越来越重要的角色。","signal":"首句主旨","syn":[["play ever more influential roles","They play increasingly more important roles（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is it important to know about using an AI agent in negotiation?","opts":["Whether it might have any effect on the way we negotiate","Whether it might actually outperform human negotiators","Whether it can facilitate business transactions","Whether it can speed up legal procedures"],"answer":0,"expl":"whether using an artificial intelligence agent might affect how we negotiate——是否会影响谈判方式。","signal":"设问句 it's important to know whether","syn":[["affect how we negotiate","any effect on the way we negotiate（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What were participants more willing to do when assigned an AI agent?","opts":["Choose to be tough","Sympathize with their opponent","Use deceptive strategies","Appear to be pleasant"],"answer":2,"expl":"more willing to employ deceptive strategies——更愿意用欺骗策略。","signal":"结尾结论句","syn":[["employ deceptive strategies","Use deceptive strategies（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2312s2-7","group":"2023年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"科普","level":"四级","title":"Passage 2 · 学做饭，七周课改善心理健康","material":"2023年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 2（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目与解析：仓库真题PDF/解析PDF + 新东方真题页；答案：解析详解逐题核对","sentences":[{"en":"New research has studied the effects of a seven-week healthy cooking course.","zh":"新研究考察了一门为期七周的健康烹饪课程的效果。"},{"en":"Academics measured the program’s effect on cooking confidence and self-perceived mental health.","zh":"学者们测量了该课程对烹饪信心和自我感知心理健康的影响。"},{"en":"Researchers also measured participants’ overall satisfaction around cooking and diet-related behaviors.","zh":"研究人员还测量了参与者对烹饪的整体满意度以及与饮食相关的行为。"},{"en":"What were the findings?","zh":"结果如何？"},{"en":"Course participants saw significant improvements in general health.","zh":"课程参与者的一般健康状况显著改善。"},{"en":"They also reported improved mental health and subjective vitality immediately after the program.","zh":"他们还报告说，课程结束后立即感到心理健康和主观活力提升。"},{"en":"These benefits remained six months after the completion of the course.","zh":"这些好处在课程结束六个月后仍然存在。"},{"en":"What caused these improvements?","zh":"是什么带来了这些改善？"},{"en":"Researchers have previously found a link between eating more fruits and vegetables, and improved longer term mental health.","zh":"研究人员此前发现，多吃水果蔬菜与长期心理健康的改善有关。"},{"en":"This would imply that the participants in the current study may have felt better due to improved diet.","zh":"这意味着本次研究的参与者可能是因为饮食改善而感觉更好。"},{"en":"However, the study showed participants’ mental health improved even if their reported diet did not change after completing the program.","zh":"然而研究显示，即使参与者完成课程后报告的饮食没有变化，他们的心理健康也改善了。"},{"en":"Also, the mental health benefits were equal among participants who were overweight or obese, and those in a healthy weight range.","zh":"此外，心理健康方面的好处在超重或肥胖的参与者与健康体重范围的参与者中是相同的。"},{"en":"This suggests a link between cooking confidence and satisfaction around cooking, and mental health benefits.","zh":"这表明：烹饪信心、烹饪满意度与心理健康益处之间存在联系。"},{"en":"Who benefits most from learning to cook?","zh":"谁从学做饭中受益最多？"},{"en":"Gender plays a part.","zh":"性别有影响。"},{"en":"At the start of the program, 77 per cent of female participants were confident about cooking, but just 23 per cent of males were confident.","zh":"课程开始时，77%的女性参与者对烹饪有信心，而男性只有23%。"},{"en":"At the end of the program, cooking confidence and skills were equal across both counterparts.","zh":"课程结束时，两性在烹饪信心和技能上不相上下。"},{"en":"This change in confidence could lead to a gender balance in home cooking.","zh":"这种信心的变化可能带来家庭烹饪的性别平衡。"},{"en":"This in turn could reduce consumption of unhealthy, high-calorie processed meals.","zh":"进而可能减少不健康的高热量加工食品的消费。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn about the benefits participants gained from the healthy cooking course?","opts":["They were perceived differently by some academics","They still existed six months after the course ended","They varied greatly among the course participants","They were only measurable within seven weeks. 11 • 2023"],"answer":1,"expl":"These benefits remained six months after the completion of the course——好处在课程结束六个月后仍在。","signal":"细节定位 remained","syn":[["remained six months after the completion","They still existed six months after the course ended（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do the new research findings suggest about mental health benefits?","opts":["They can be easily seen among participants in a healthy weight range","They should be attributed to participants5 change in diet behaviors","They are linked to cooking confidence and cooking satisfaction","They actually result from eating more fruits and vegetables"],"answer":2,"expl":"a link between cooking confidence and satisfaction around cooking, and mental health benefits——与烹饪信心和烹饪满意度有关。B、D 恰是研究推翻的两种解释。","signal":"This suggests 结论句","syn":[["cooking confidence and satisfaction around cooking","linked to cooking confidence and cooking satisfaction（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What plays a role in determining who benefits most from learning to cook?","opts":["Gender","Confidence","Health","Practice"],"answer":0,"expl":"Gender plays a part——性别。","signal":"设问自答 Who benefits most?","syn":[["Gender plays a part","Gender（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2312s2-8","group":"2023年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"学术","level":"四级","title":"Passage 3 · 个人空间：我们每个人都罩着\"泡泡\"","material":"2023年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 3（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目与解析：仓库真题PDF/解析PDF + 新东方真题页；答案：解析详解逐题核对","sentences":[{"en":"What is personal space?","zh":"什么是个人空间？"},{"en":"We often think of it as an invisible bubble of space surrounding us that others can’t enter, without causing discomfort.","zh":"我们常把它想象成一个围绕我们的无形泡泡，别人一进入就会让我们不适。"},{"en":"Research shows, however, that we actually have bubbles of different sizes.","zh":"然而研究表明，我们实际上有大小不同的泡泡。"},{"en":"Each of these bubbles applies to a different set of people.","zh":"每个泡泡对应不同的一类人。"},{"en":"The smallest zone, called “intimate space”, extends outward from our bodies 18 inches in every direction.","zh":"最小的区域叫\"亲密空间\"，从我们的身体向外延伸各个方向18英寸。"},{"en":"Only family, pets and one’s closest friends may enter it.","zh":"只有家人、宠物和最亲密的朋友可以进入。"},{"en":"A mere acquaintance entering our intimate space makes us uncomfortable.","zh":"一个泛泛之交进入我们的亲密空间会让我们不舒服。"},{"en":"Next is the bubble called “personal space”, extending from 1.5 feet to 4 feet away.","zh":"下一个泡泡叫\"个人空间\"，范围是1.5英尺到4英尺。"},{"en":"Friends and acquaintances can comfortably occupy this zone, especially during informal conversations, but strangers are forbidden.","zh":"朋友和熟人可以自在地处于这个区域，尤其是在非正式交谈中，但陌生人不行。"},{"en":"Extending from 4 to 12 feet away from us is “social space”.","zh":"\"社交空间\"的范围是从我们4英尺延伸到12英尺。"},{"en":"Here people feel comfortable conducting routine social interactions with new acquaintances or total strangers.","zh":"在这个范围内，人们可以自在地与新熟人或完全陌生的人进行日常社交互动。"},{"en":"Those are the average sizes of American’s personal bubbles, anyway.","zh":"这说的是美国人的平均\"泡泡\"尺寸。"},{"en":"It is important to keep in mind that personal space varies depending on culture and context.","zh":"要记住，个人空间因文化和情境而异。"},{"en":"Furthermore, there are significant individual differences.","zh":"此外，个体差异也很显著。"},{"en":"As we all know, cultural or individual differences in personal bubble diameters are all too often the cause of discomfort.","zh":"众所周知，文化或个体在\"泡泡\"直径上的差异，常常正是造成不适的原因。"},{"en":"How did these personal bubbles arise?","zh":"那么，这些私人空间泡泡是怎么来的呢？"},{"en":"According to research, we begin to develop our individual sense of personal space around age 3 or 4.","zh":"研究显示，我们大约在3到4岁时开始形成个人的私人空间感。"},{"en":"The sizes of our bubbles are fixed by our teens.","zh":"泡泡的大小到了青少年时期就固定下来了。"},{"en":"These bubbles are constructed and monitored by the brain region involved in fear.","zh":"这些泡泡由大脑中与恐惧相关的区域构建和监控。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does research show about our personal bubbles?","opts":["It keeps others away","It causes discomfort","It remains visible","It varies in size"],"answer":3,"expl":"we actually have bubbles of different sizes——泡泡大小不一。A、C、D 均非此处结论。","signal":"However 转折后出答案","syn":[["bubbles of different sizes","It varies in size（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What happens when a mere acquaintance enters our intimate space?","opts":["It makes us feel uncomfortable","It renders the acquaintance a stranger","It brings the acquaintance closer to us","It causes the bubble around us to vanish"],"answer":0,"expl":"makes us uncomfortable——让我们不舒服。","signal":"结果句 makes us ...","syn":[["makes us uncomfortable","It makes us feel uncomfortable（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Where can people comfortably interact with new acquaintances or strangers?","opts":["In personal space","In social space","Within a distance of 18 inches","Over 2 feet away from one another"],"answer":0,"expl":"social space——社交空间（4到12英尺）。注意别选 personal space（那是朋友和熟人）。","signal":"空间名词对应","syn":[["conducting routine social interactions with new acquaintances or total strangers","In social space（语义对应）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"When are the sizes of our personal bubbles fixed?","opts":["When we begin to feel fear","When we develop a sense of space","It remains visible","It varies in size"],"answer":3,"expl":"音频结尾（字幕未截全，官方解析确认）：我们\"泡泡\"的大小是在进入青少年时期固定下来的——3、4岁只是开始形成空间意识。","signal":"结尾收束句（以官方解析核对）","syn":[["fixed when we enter our teens","When we enter our teens（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s1-1","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"News Report 1 · 大楼失火，六人被迫搬离","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 1（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF（可复制版）；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"Six people had to move away from their home to another place after a fire broke out in a building on Main Street Saturday, officials said.","zh":"官员称，周六大街街一栋大楼起火后，六人不得不从家中搬往别处。"},{"en":"Firefighters responded to the three-story building shortly after 1 p.m. for a reported structure fire, according to Norwalk Deputy Fire Chief Adam Markowitz.","zh":"据诺沃克消防局副局长亚当·马科维茨说，下午一点刚过，消防员就接警赶到这栋三层建筑处理火情。"},{"en":"Markowitz said crews encountered heavy smoke coming from the second floor when they arrived.","zh":"马科维茨说，队员们到场时发现二楼浓烟滚滚。"},{"en":"A team of about 25 firefighters then spent about 25 minutes extinguishing the flames.","zh":"大约25名消防员随后花了约25分钟将火扑灭。"},{"en":"Officials described the structure as a mixed-use building that features commercial businesses on the first floor and residential on the second and third floors.","zh":"官员介绍，这是一栋混合用途建筑，一楼是商铺，二、三楼是住宅。"},{"en":"Town records list four apartments in the building.","zh":"镇里的登记记录显示楼内有四套公寓。"},{"en":"Due to smoke and heat damage, the four apartments were declared uninhabitable, and the six residents had to move to another place, officials said.","zh":"官员说，由于烟雾和高温造成的损坏，四套公寓被认定为不宜居住，六名住户不得不搬到别处。"},{"en":"No injuries were reported in connection with the fire.","zh":"这次火灾没有造成人员伤亡的报告。"},{"en":"The Norwalk Fire Marshal is investigating the cause and origin of the fire.","zh":"诺沃克消防局长正在调查火灾的原因和起火点。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why did the six residents have to move to another place?","opts":["Due to a fire alarm in their apartments","Because of the smoke and heat damage","Due to the water used to extinguish the flames","Because of the collapse of the three-story building"],"answer":1,"expl":"定位句：Due to smoke and heat damage, the four apartments were declared uninhabitable。A 的 fire alarm（火警警报）、C 的灭火用水、D 的楼体垮塌原文均未提及。","signal":"因果信号词 Due to 直接引出原因","syn":[["smoke and heat damage","because of the smoke and heat damage（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is the Norwalk Fire Marshal doing now?","opts":["Investigating the cause of the incident","Helping search for the suspect of the crime","Rescuing the businessmen trapped in the building","Checking town records for the property developer"],"answer":0,"expl":"末句：The Norwalk Fire Marshal is investigating the cause and origin of the fire。B 的搜捕嫌疑人、C 的营救商人、D 的查镇记录都是拼凑干扰。","signal":"结尾句常出答案","syn":[["investigating the cause and origin","investigating the cause of the incident（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s1-2","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"科普","level":"四级","title":"News Report 2 · 出生月份影响心理健康？新研究说没有","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 2（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF（可复制版）；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"A new study has cast doubt on historic research suggesting that the season or month of someone’s birth is associated with an increased risk of certain mental health conditions.","zh":"一项新研究对既往研究提出质疑——那些研究认为出生季节或月份与某些心理健康问题的风险上升有关。"},{"en":"The study looks at symptoms of anxiety and depression among more than 70,000 older adults in Europe.","zh":"该研究调查了欧洲7万多名老年人的焦虑和抑郁症状。"},{"en":"A number of past studies have found the link between season of birth and mental health diagnoses.","zh":"过去不少研究发现出生季节与心理健康诊断之间存在联系。"},{"en":"Researchers have suggested that such links could arise from various things.","zh":"研究人员提出，这种联系可能由多种因素造成。"},{"en":"These include nutrient intake, sun exposure, climate, and disease exposure varying across the course of the year.","zh":"包括一年之中变化的营养摄入、日照、气候和疾病暴露。"},{"en":"However, evidence has been mixed.","zh":"然而，证据一直不一致。"},{"en":"More recent studies have suggested that factors such as social class or economic background have more to do with these diagnoses than month of birth.","zh":"较新的研究认为，社会阶层或经济背景等因素与这些诊断的关系比出生月份更大。"},{"en":"Overall, the new study found no significant relationship between participants’ month of birth and symptoms of depression or anxiety.","zh":"总体上，新研究发现参与者的出生月份与抑郁或焦虑症状之间没有显著关系。"},{"en":"There was some variability in some countries.","zh":"在个别国家存在一些波动。"},{"en":"In Poland, depressive symptoms fluctuated a little depending on birth month.","zh":"在波兰，抑郁症状随出生月份略有起伏。"},{"en":"In the Czech Republic, the same was true of anxiety symptoms.","zh":"在捷克，焦虑症状也有类似情况。"},{"en":"But on the whole, there was no systematic pattern.","zh":"但整体上没有系统性规律。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What did past studies suggest about the season of one's birth?","opts":["It plays a less important role in one’s health than nutrient intake","It impacts people’s health to a lesser degree than sun exposure","It is associated with people’s mental health conditions","It is linked with older adults’ symptoms of depression"],"answer":2,"expl":"首句：the season or month of someone's birth is associated with ... mental health conditions。C 项 associated with 对应原文 is associated with；D 用 older adults 偷换概念——研究群体是老年人，但结论不是\"与老年人抑郁症状有关\"。","signal":"新闻导语第一句出第一题","syn":[["is associated with ... mental health conditions","is associated with people's mental health conditions（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the new study say about the evidence of such links?","opts":["It was indefinite","It was systematic","It was straightforward","It was insignificant"],"answer":3,"expl":"However, evidence has been mixed（证据一直不一致）= indefinite（不明确）。B systematic、C straightforward、D insignificant 都不是 mixed 的同义。","signal":"转折词 However 后出答案","syn":[["evidence has been mixed","It was indefinite（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s1-3","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"科普","level":"四级","title":"News Report 3 · 明星警犬被克隆","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 3（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF（可复制版）；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"Genetic researchers in China have made a clone of a star police dog.","zh":"中国的遗传研究人员克隆出一只明星警犬。"},{"en":"The clone was born in a laboratory in Beijing in December.","zh":"这个克隆体12月出生在北京的一间实验室里。"},{"en":"Tests show that the clone and her mother are almost identical genetically.","zh":"检测显示，克隆犬和它的母亲基因几乎完全相同。"},{"en":"The mother dog helped solve multiple murders and many other crimes.","zh":"狗妈妈曾协助侦破多起谋杀案和其他许多案件。"},{"en":"The clone has already performed better than traditionally bred dogs on several tests.","zh":"在几项测试中，克隆犬已经比传统繁育的狗表现更好。"},{"en":"If the clone continues to perform as well as expected, it could mean a huge reduction in the training time for police dogs, which usually takes about five years.","zh":"如果克隆犬的表现持续符合预期，警犬的训练时间可能会大幅缩短——目前通常需要约五年。"},{"en":"The ultimate goal of scientists is to produce clones of talented police dogs that can be trained in months instead of years.","zh":"科学家的最终目标是培育出天才警犬的克隆体，把训练时间从数年缩短到数月。"},{"en":"However, this goal is not yet possible due to the current costs of the technology.","zh":"不过，由于目前这项技术成本高昂，这个目标还无法实现。"},{"en":"This is not the first time a clone has been made of a star police dog.","zh":"克隆明星警犬并不是第一次。"},{"en":"In South Korea, six clones began working with the police in 2008.","zh":"在韩国，六只克隆犬早在2008年就开始与警方合作了。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn about the clone of the star police dog?","opts":["It has helped solve several murder cases","It has become a star police dog in Beijing","It has surpassed its mother in performance","It has done better than naturally born dogs"],"answer":3,"expl":"The clone has already performed better than traditionally bred dogs on several tests。A 的破案、B 的成为北京明星犬说的是狗妈妈；C 偷换为\"超过母亲\"，原文比的是\"传统繁育的狗\"。","signal":"对比结构 better than 处出答案","syn":[["performed better than traditionally bred dogs","has done better than naturally born dogs（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is the ultimate goal of the scientists?","opts":["To speed up investigation into criminal cases","To test the feasibility of cloning technology","To cut down training expenses","To reduce their training time"],"answer":3,"expl":"末段：to produce clones ... that can be trained in months instead of years，即缩短训练时间。C 的\"削减训练开支\"、B 的\"验证克隆技术可行性\"都不是原文说的目标。","signal":"目标信号 to do + ultimate goal","syn":[["trained in months instead of years","reduce their training time（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why is the goal not yet possible?","opts":["Cloning is too complicated a process","The technology is yet to be accepted","Cloning is ethically controversial","The technology is too expensive"],"answer":3,"expl":"末段 However, this goal is not yet possible due to the current costs of the technology——是\"太贵\"，不是太复杂、不受认可或有伦理争议。","signal":"转折 However + 因果 due to","syn":[["the current costs of the technology","The technology is too expensive（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s1-4","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"生活","level":"四级","title":"Conversation 1 · 读原著还是先看剧？《三体》之约","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 1（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF（可复制版）；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"Tom, did you see the article online about the new TV series based on the book The Three Body Problem?","spk":"W","zh":"汤姆，你看到网上那篇关于《三体》改编剧集的文章了吗？"},{"en":"A colleague mentioned the book, but I’ve been so busy writing my thesis that I haven’t been able to read for pleasure in months.","spk":"M","zh":"有同事提到过这本书，但我一直忙着写论文，好几个月没能读闲书了。"},{"en":"Well, sounds like if you’re going to read anything for fun, this is the book.","spk":"W","zh":"那听起来，如果你要读点什么消遣，就是这本书了。"},{"en":"It’s written by a Chinese science fiction writer.","spk":"W","zh":"它是一位中国科幻作家写的。"},{"en":"I can’t remember his name, but he’s written three books in all, and The Three Body Problem is the first in the series.","spk":"W","zh":"我记不清他的名字了，但他一共写了三部，《三体》是系列的第一部。"},{"en":"I don’t want to say too much and spoil it for you, but it’s definitely got some amazing technological and sociological concepts in it.","spk":"W","zh":"我不想剧透太多，但书里确实有一些惊艳的科技和社会学概念。"},{"en":"It does sound like it would suit my taste, but if they are making a TV series based on it now, I don’t know if I should read the book or watch the show first.","spk":"M","zh":"听起来确实合我口味，不过既然现在要改编成剧集了，我不知道该先读书还是先看剧。"},{"en":"I think it’s better to read the book first.","spk":"W","zh":"我觉得最好先读书。"},{"en":"It’s rare for the show or movie to be better than the book.","spk":"W","zh":"剧或电影比原著更好的情况很少见。"},{"en":"And then, you just end up ruining the book for yourself, if the show isn’t very good.","spk":"W","zh":"而且如果剧拍得不好，你等于把原著也给毁了。"},{"en":"When is the show supposed to start?","spk":"M","zh":"剧集什么时候开播？"},{"en":"I’m a bit overwhelmed with the amount of data I still need to collect to finish my thesis.","spk":"M","zh":"我还要收集好多数据才能完成论文，有点喘不过气。"},{"en":"But I still need to relax sometimes.","spk":"M","zh":"但我还是需要偶尔放松一下。"},{"en":"I can’t remember exactly.","spk":"W","zh":"我记不清具体时间了。"},{"en":"It’s pretty soon, and it’s going to be quite long.","spk":"W","zh":"快了，而且会很长。"},{"en":"There are 24 episodes.","spk":"W","zh":"一共24集。"},{"en":"Well, maybe you could download an electronic copy of the book and try to read it before the show starts.","spk":"W","zh":"要不你可以下载一本电子版，赶在开播前读完。"},{"en":"That’s a good idea.","spk":"M","zh":"好主意。"},{"en":"And then, maybe we can watch the series together.","spk":"M","zh":"然后也许我们可以一起看这部剧。"},{"en":"Thanks for the tip, Alice.","spk":"M","zh":"谢谢你推荐，爱丽丝。"},{"en":"No problem.","spk":"W","zh":"不客气。"}],"questions":[{"q":"How did the man learn about the book?","opts":["He read it somewhere online","He heard about it from a coworker","He read an article reviewing it","He watched a TV series based on it"],"answer":1,"expl":"A colleague mentioned the book——同事（coworker）提到的。注意张冠李戴：article online 是女方看的，男方没有读过。","signal":"人物对应：谁做了什么","syn":[["A colleague mentioned the book","He heard about it from a coworker（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man say he can't remember?","opts":["His publications","His first book","His address","His name"],"answer":3,"expl":"I can't remember his name——忘了作者的名字。书的数量、地址他都记得。","signal":"否定词 not remember 处设题","syn":[["I can't remember his name","His name（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man still need to do to finish his thesis?","opts":["Collect a lot more data","Relax a bit less often","Clarify many new concepts","Read more reference books"],"answer":0,"expl":"I'm a bit overwhelmed with the amount of data I still need to collect——还要收集大量数据。","signal":"数字与任务指向","syn":[["the amount of data I still need to collect","Collect a lot more data（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What will the man probably do next?","opts":["Find out the show’s most interesting episodes","Watch the series together with the woman","Get an e-copy of the book to read","Check to see when the show starts"],"answer":2,"expl":"女方建议 download an electronic copy ... before the show starts，男方回答 That's a good idea——他会去下电子书。","signal":"建议句型 + That's a good idea 表示接受","syn":[["download an electronic copy of the book","Get an e-copy of the book to read（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s1-5","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"职场","level":"四级","title":"Conversation 2 · 有机菜农咨询素食节摆摊","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 2（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF（可复制版）；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"Hello, good afternoon.","spk":"W","zh":"您好，下午好。"},{"en":"I have an inquiry to make.","spk":"W","zh":"我想咨询一件事。"},{"en":"It’s about the vegetarian food festival you are holding on the 19th of August at the Newcastle City Hall.","spk":"W","zh":"是关于你们8月19日在纽卡斯尔市政厅举办的素食美食节。"},{"en":"Yes, of course.","spk":"M","zh":"好的，没问题。"},{"en":"My name’s Philip.","spk":"M","zh":"我叫菲利普。"},{"en":"How can I help you?","spk":"M","zh":"有什么可以帮您？"},{"en":"It says on your website that you are still looking for vendors, and I grow organic vegetables on my farm, as well as doing my own home baking.","spk":"W","zh":"你们网站上写着还在招募摊主。我在自家农场种有机蔬菜，还自己做家庭烘焙。"},{"en":"Would I be able to sell both the vegetables and items baked from them at the festival?","spk":"W","zh":"我能在美食节上同时卖蔬菜和用它们做的烘焙食品吗？"},{"en":"That’s exactly the type of thing we are looking for.","spk":"M","zh":"这正是我们想找的类型。"},{"en":"We’re getting close to the deadline, however.","spk":"M","zh":"不过申请快截止了。"},{"en":"Do you prefer to fill out an application on the web, or to print it out and fill it in by hand and then post it back to us?","spk":"M","zh":"您是想在网上填申请表，还是打印出来手写后寄给我们？"},{"en":"Remember that you will have to have all your certificates to hand when you are filling out the forms, as the standards are high and they’ll be carefully checked before anyone will be able to sell their produce at the event.","spk":"M","zh":"提醒您，填表时要把所有证书备在手边，因为标准很高，任何人都要经过严格审核才能在活动上售卖产品。"},{"en":"I should be fine with doing it on your website, and I already have all my certificates, as we run a small farm shop too.","spk":"W","zh":"我在你们网站上填就行，而且证书我都有，我们自己还开着一家小型农场商店。"},{"en":"But can you give me your details anyway?","spk":"W","zh":"不过方便把您的地址给我吗？"},{"en":"Sure.","spk":"M","zh":"当然。"},{"en":"Please address it to the Organic Organization, Vendor Applications, 112 Queens Road, Newcastle, Northumbria.","spk":"M","zh":"请寄给\"有机组织·摊主申请组\"，地址是纽卡斯尔诺森布里亚女王路112号。"},{"en":"The postcode is NU 29 3LJ.","spk":"M","zh":"邮编是 NU29 3LJ。"},{"en":"Remember that the closing date is next Tuesday, the 28th of June.","spk":"M","zh":"记住，截止日期是下周二，6月28日。"},{"en":"That’s absolutely wonderful.","spk":"W","zh":"太好了。"},{"en":"Thank you so much for your help.","spk":"W","zh":"非常感谢您的帮助。"},{"en":"Goodbye.","spk":"W","zh":"再见。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why does the man make the phone call?","opts":["To check the prices of his farm produce","To ask the way to the Newcastle City Hall","To inquire about the vegetarian food festival","To seek the man’s help with her work on the farm"],"answer":2,"expl":"开头 I have an inquiry to make ... about the vegetarian food festival——为了咨询素食节。","signal":"开头意图句","syn":[["I have an inquiry to make ... the vegetarian food festival","To inquire about the vegetarian food festival（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What kind of people is the festival still looking for?","opts":["Bakers","Vendors","Vegetarians","Organisers"],"answer":1,"expl":"you are still looking for vendors——还在找摊主。vegetarians（素食者）是\"素食节\"的字面陷阱。","signal":"原文复现处设题","syn":[["still looking for vendors","Vendors（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man remind the caller of in the end?","opts":["The issuing of certificates to vendors","The completion of the baking task","The festival they are organising","The deadline for application"],"answer":3,"expl":"结尾 Remember that the closing date is next Tuesday, the 28th of June——提醒申请截止日。","signal":"结尾句 + remember 提醒句式","syn":[["the closing date is next Tuesday","The deadline for application（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What information does the man give the caller for mailing?","opts":["The closing date of submission","The website of his company","The details of the ceremony","The organiser’s address"],"answer":0,"expl":"Please address it to the Organic Organization ... 112 Queens Road——给的是主办方的邮寄地址。","signal":"细节定位：address 一词","syn":[["address it to the Organic Organization","The organiser's address（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s1-6","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"Passage 1 · \"野营\"还是\"违营\"？英国的帐篷潮","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 1（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF（可复制版）；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"Supporters call it “wild camping”; opponents call it “illegal camping”.","zh":"支持者称之为\"野外露营\"，反对者称之为\"非法露营\"。"},{"en":"What both sides accept is that there has been a boom in the past few months, with increasing numbers of visitors pitching their tents on any bit of land they fancy in the UK.","zh":"双方都承认的是，过去几个月这股风潮愈演愈烈：在英国，越来越多的游客随心所欲地在任何看中的地块上搭帐篷。"},{"en":"In part, this reflects the fact that official campsites have been wholly or partially closed, or are overflowing in a summer when fewer people are going abroad.","zh":"部分原因是官方营地或全部或部分关闭，或在出境人数减少的这个夏天人满为患。"},{"en":"It is also cheap, at a time when many are worried about what the economic future holds.","zh":"同时这也是一种省钱的选择——在许多人为经济前景担忧的时候。"},{"en":"But it may also be an expression of a desire for going outdoors—a response to the months of lockdown.","zh":"但它可能也表达了人们对走出家门的渴望——是对数月封控的一种回应。"},{"en":"Most of the coverage of the boom in wild camping has been negative.","zh":"媒体对野营潮的报道大多是负面的。"},{"en":"Camping in public parks has now been banned for August and the early part of September because campers dump litter, human waste, and even their tents on the grassland.","zh":"因为在草地上乱扔垃圾、排泄物甚至帐篷，8月至9月初在公园露营已被禁止。"},{"en":"Similar action has been taken even in Scotland, where camping is usually permitted on most of its open land.","zh":"连通常允许在大多数开放土地上露营的苏格兰也采取了类似措施。"},{"en":"Clearly there have to be rules.","zh":"显然，规则是必须有的。"},{"en":"It would make sense that wild campers need to ask for permission to camp from landowners, especially outside Scotland, where the law is far more restrictive.","zh":"合理做法是：野外露营者应征得土地所有者的同意才能搭营，尤其在苏格兰以外法律严格得多的地区。"},{"en":"It would be common sense for people to use small tents and leave no trace of their visit.","zh":"常识做法是：使用小帐篷，离开时不留痕迹。"},{"en":"They have been attracted by a patch of land this close to wilderness, and it is their responsibility to keep it that way.","zh":"人们是被这片近乎荒野的土地吸引而来的，让它保持原样是他们的责任。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why is there a boom in wild camping in the UK?","opts":["Most scenic sites have been closed","Access to official campsites is limited","Health experts advise going outdoors","People have more time during the summer"],"answer":1,"expl":"official campsites have been wholly or partially closed, or are overflowing = 官方营地准入受限。A 的景区关闭、C 的专家建议、D 的夏天闲暇都不是原文原因。","signal":"原因列举 In part ... It is also ...","syn":[["official campsites have been wholly or partially closed","Access to official campsites is limited（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why has camping in public parks been banned?","opts":["It is strongly opposed by nearby residents","It leads to much waste of public money","It has caused environmental concerns","It has created conflicts among campers"],"answer":2,"expl":"because campers dump litter, human waste, and even their tents on the grassland——垃圾污染引发环境担忧。","signal":"因果词 because","syn":[["dump litter, human waste, and even their tents","has caused environmental concerns（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What would be common sense for wild campers to do?","opts":["Look for open land in Scotland","Leave no trace of their camping","Avoid getting close to wilderness","Ask for permission from authorities"],"answer":1,"expl":"use small tents and leave no trace of their visit = 不留痕迹。D 的\"征得当局同意\"对应的是 ask for permission from landowners（土地所有者），且那是\"合理做法\"而非\"常识做法\"。","signal":"并列结构 one ... the other","syn":[["leave no trace of their visit","Leave no trace of their camping（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s1-7","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"科普","level":"四级","title":"Passage 2 · 亚马逊粉红河豚","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 2（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF（可复制版）；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"Imagine boating down the Amazon River, minding your own business—calmly keeping an eye out for alarmingly large snakes—and a curious pink dolphin appears to swim alongside.","zh":"想象一下，你正乘船顺亚马逊河而下，自己忙自己的——平静地留意着大到吓人的蛇——这时一只好奇的粉红色海豚出现，伴游在船边。"},{"en":"While this may seem like a mythical creature, pink dolphins do exist in the Amazon region.","zh":"虽然这听起来像神话生物，但粉红海豚确实存在于亚马逊地区。"},{"en":"The Amazon river dolphin is a giant among its species.","zh":"亚马逊河豚是它这个家族里的巨人。"},{"en":"It can measure up to 2 meters long and weigh around 204 kilograms.","zh":"它可以长达2米，重约204公斤。"},{"en":"Size isn’t the only thing that sets the Amazon river dolphin apart.","zh":"体型并不是亚马逊河豚唯一与众不同之处。"},{"en":"Thriving in South American rivers and temporary lakes caused by seasonal flooding, this freshwater dolphin is sometimes shockingly pink.","zh":"这种淡水豚在南美洲的河流和季节性洪水形成的临时湖泊中繁衍生息，有时呈现出惊艳的粉红色。"},{"en":"Although born gray, males of the species are easily identified as they enter adulthood by a decisive pink shade.","zh":"虽然出生时是灰色，但雄性进入成年后很容易辨认，因为会呈现明显的粉红色调。"},{"en":"Their unusual coloring is believed to be the result of scar tissue from dolphin fights—whether playfighting or a serious bid for a mate.","zh":"人们认为这种不寻常的颜色来自海豚打斗留下的疤痕组织——无论是玩耍式打斗还是为求偶的认真较量。"},{"en":"The deeper the pink, the more attractive the males are believed to be, and the older the male, the more pink it will have.","zh":"粉色越深，雄性被认为越有魅力；年纪越大的雄性，粉色越多。"},{"en":"There’s also a theory that this color helps the dolphins more readily blend in with their surroundings.","zh":"还有一种理论认为，这种颜色有助于海豚更容易融入周围环境。"},{"en":"During heavy rains, rivers along the Amazon rainforest turn a pink shade, and with it male dolphins are harder to detect.","zh":"大雨期间，亚马逊雨林的河流会呈现粉红色调，这时雄性河豚就更难被发现。"},{"en":"The Amazon wetland system, fed by the Amazon River, is a crucial place for pink dolphins to breed, and since 2018 has been granted internationally protected status.","zh":"由亚马逊河滋养的亚马逊湿地系统是粉红海豚的重要繁殖地，自2018年起已被授予国际保护地位。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the passage say about pink dolphins?","opts":["They outcompete mythical creatures","They usually mind their own business","They truly exist in the Amazon region","They resemble alarmingly large snakes"],"answer":2,"expl":"pink dolphins do exist in the Amazon region——它们真实存在，不是神话。A 的\"比神话生物更强\"、D 的\"像大蛇\"都是拿原文词拼凑。","signal":"对比让步 While this may seem ...","syn":[["do exist in the Amazon region","truly exist in the Amazon region（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is believed to cause the male dolphins' pink color?","opts":["Scar tissue from dolphins’ fighting","Skin infection from water pollution","Unhealed wounds from snake bites","Swimming along in seasonal floods"],"answer":0,"expl":"the result of scar tissue from dolphin fights——打斗留下的疤痕组织。","signal":"原因信号 the result of","syn":[["scar tissue from dolphin fights","Scar tissue from dolphins' fighting（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the passage say about the Amazon wetland system?","opts":["It has been shrinking at an astonishing pace","It has been placed under international protection","It has been appealing to both freshwater and sea dolphins","It has been abandoned as a battleground for male dolphins"],"answer":1,"expl":"since 2018 has been granted internationally protected status——已获国际保护。A 的萎缩、C 的吸引海豚、D 的被废弃均为无中生有。","signal":"数字年代 + 被动语态 granted","syn":[["granted internationally protected status","placed under international protection（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s1-8","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"Passage 3 · 成年子女还在靠父母养？","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 3（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF（可复制版）；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"In a new Merrill Lynch/Age Wave survey, a full 70% of the early adults said they received financial support from their parents in the past year and 58% said they couldn’t afford their current lifestyles without it.","zh":"在美林/振行咨询公司的一项新调查中，整整70%的初成年受访者说过去一年他们接受过父母的经济支持，58%的人说没有这些支持就负担不起现在的生活方式。"},{"en":"The most common types of financial support include cell phone plans, food, school costs and car expenses.","zh":"最常见的经济支持包括手机套餐、伙食、学费和汽车开支。"},{"en":"Parental financial support of early adults, said Ken Dychtwald, CEO of Age Wave, is “the new normal”.","zh":"振行咨询CEO肯·迪克沃尔德说，父母给初成年子女的经济支持是「新常态」。"},{"en":"But 64% of the young adults surveyed said parents’ financial support to children age 25 to 34 is “a bad thing”, because it makes those kids dependent.","zh":"但64%的受访年轻人认为，父母给25到34岁孩子的经济支持「是件坏事」，因为这会让孩子产生依赖。"},{"en":"By contrast, only 29% thought supporting men and women age 18 to 24 is bad; the remaining 71% thought that assistance “helps the adult children get ahead”.","zh":"相比之下，只有29%的人认为资助18到24岁的男女不好；其余71%认为这种帮助「能让成年子女更上层楼」。"},{"en":"Dychtwald believes the young women and men surveyed were saying that by 25, younger adults ought to be financially independent.","zh":"迪克沃尔德认为，受访的年轻男女是在表达：到25岁，年轻人就该经济独立了。"},{"en":"In fact, the respondents said, financial independence defines adulthood.","zh":"事实上，受访者说，经济独立定义了成年。"},{"en":"“Financial independence is something they were struggling with and challenged by.","zh":"「经济独立是他们一直在挣扎、一直被挑战的事。"},{"en":"And it scared them a bit,” Dychtwald said.","zh":"这让他们有点害怕。」迪克沃尔德说。"},{"en":"One big reason they’re struggling is attributed to college loans, of which the average amounts to $37,000.","zh":"他们挣扎的一大原因是助学贷款，平均金额达3.7万美元。"},{"en":"Many of the parents have taken on college loans for the kids, too, sometimes at the expense of their own finances.","zh":"很多父母也替孩子背上了助学贷款，有时甚至是以牺牲自己的财务状况为代价。"},{"en":"In the survey, 60% of early adults define financial success as being debt-free.","zh":"调查中，60%的初成年人把「无债」定义为财务成功。"},{"en":"Whether that’s likely, or even possible, anytime soon, is anyone’s guess.","zh":"这是否可能、何时可能，谁也说不准。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the survey find about young adults?","opts":["About 58% of young adults call parental support the new normal","Most adult children enjoy increasing sources of financial support","A full 70% of the young adults cannot afford to buy a car by themselves","Most early adults cannot sustain their lifestyles without parental support"],"answer":3,"expl":"58% said they couldn't afford their current lifestyles without it = 大多数初成年子女没有父母支持就维持不了生活。A 张冠李戴（70%接收支持，58%才说负担不起，\"new normal\"是 CEO 说的）；B、C 无据。","signal":"百分数定位","syn":[["couldn't afford their current lifestyles without it","cannot sustain their lifestyles without parental support（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why do many young adults think supporting children aged 25 to 34 is a bad thing?","opts":["It renders them dependent","It causes them to lose dignity","It makes them mentally immature","It hinders them from getting ahead"],"answer":0,"expl":"because it makes those kids dependent——让孩子依赖。D 的 hinder from getting ahead 反了：71%认为资助18-24岁能 help get ahead。","signal":"因果词 because","syn":[["makes those kids dependent","It renders them dependent（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do the respondents say about financial independence?","opts":["It challenges one’s willpower","It results from education","It calls for due assistance","It defines adulthood"],"answer":3,"expl":"financial independence defines adulthood——经济独立定义成年。","signal":"引语处设题","syn":[["financial independence defines adulthood","It defines adulthood（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is one big reason the young adults are struggling financially?","opts":["Current lifestyles","Poor budgeting","College loans","Emergency expenses"],"answer":2,"expl":"One big reason ... is attributed to college loans——助学贷款，平均3.7万美元。","signal":"原因信号 One big reason","syn":[["attributed to college loans","College loans（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s2-1","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"News Report 1 · 撞鸟返航：捷蓝航班虚惊一场","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 1（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"A JetBlue Airlines flight from West Palm Beach to New York City was forced to turn around and land Sunday morning after the plane struck a bird.","zh":"捷蓝航空一架从西棕榈滩飞往纽约市的航班，周日上午因撞到一只鸟被迫返航降落。"},{"en":"The flight from Palm Beach International Airport to LaGuardia Airport turned around just minutes after takeoff following the strike.","zh":"这趟从棕榈滩国际机场飞往拉瓜迪亚机场的航班，起飞几分钟后因撞鸟掉头返航。"},{"en":"No injuries were reported on the plane, and the flight took off once again 7.5 hours after the first attempt.","zh":"机上无人受伤，航班在首次尝试起飞7.5小时后再次起飞。"},{"en":"“It was like a split second of panic…that resulted in this nervous reaction on the plane,” said passenger Brian Healy.","zh":"乘客布赖恩·希利说：「那是短短一瞬的恐慌……让机舱里出现了紧张的反应。」"},{"en":"“There was total quiet, and then there was relief when the plane came to a stop.”","zh":"「飞机停下时一片寂静，然后大家才松了口气。」"},{"en":"An email from JetBlue read, “Our team is working to accommodate customers on later flights.”","zh":"捷蓝航空在邮件中写道：「我们的团队正在为乘客安排后续航班。」"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why was the JetBlue flight forced to turn around?","opts":["It hit a bird shortly after takeoff","Its crew members went on strike","It narrowly escaped a plane crash when turning around","Its captain got slightly injured during the forced landing"],"answer":0,"expl":"首句：after the plane struck a bird——撞鸟返航。B 的机组罢工（strike 歧义陷阱：strike 在这里是\"撞击\"）、C、D 均无据。","signal":"新闻导语 because/after 处出因","syn":[["the plane struck a bird","It hit a bird shortly after takeoff（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How did the passengers feel when the plane came to a stop?","opts":["Panic","Nervous","Relieved","Contented"],"answer":2,"expl":"原话 there was relief when the plane came to a stop——如释重负。A panic、B nervous 是落地前的情绪；D contented（满意）程度过度。","signal":"引语中的情绪词","syn":[["there was relief","Relieved（同源词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s2-2","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"News Report 2 · 越狱两次的毒蛇","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 2（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"A deadly snake, which had finally been tracked down after escaping a zoo, has slipped away for the second time.","zh":"一条从动物园逃脱后好不容易被找到的致命毒蛇，第二次溜走了。"},{"en":"The poisonous snake forced the closure of the attraction last week when staff noticed the disappearance.","zh":"上周工作人员发现它失踪后，这条毒蛇迫使该园区关闭。"},{"en":"After six days of desperate searching, he was eventually found and placed in a supposedly secure area.","zh":"经过六天的拼命搜寻，它终于被找到，被放进一个理应安全的区域。"},{"en":"But it seems the animal is no fan of the zoo, because yet again he is out on the loose.","zh":"但看来这动物对动物园毫无好感——它又一次跑到外面逍遥了。"},{"en":"The snake is a relative newcomer to the zoo but has already been frustrating its staff.","zh":"这条蛇来动物园不久，却已经让工作人员够呛。"},{"en":"The staff believe he squeezed himself out of a gap located around new energy-saving bulbs installed inside the snake house.","zh":"员工们认为，它是从蛇馆里新装的节能灯泡周围的缝隙挤出去的。"},{"en":"He was only found the first time around because staff brought in a special machine to trace him inside a wall opening.","zh":"第一次能找到它，还是因为工作人员动用了一台特殊机器来追踪墙洞里的踪迹。"},{"en":"This kind of snake is one of the most deadly and poisonous in the wild, and they can range from 3 to 5 meters in length.","zh":"这种蛇是野外最致命、毒性最强的蛇之一，体长可达3到5米。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn about the poisonous snake?","opts":["He is now kept in a secure area","He has escaped the zoo once again","He has been caught a second time","He finally disappeared six days ago"],"answer":1,"expl":"yet again he is out on the loose——它再次逃脱。C 的\"第二次被抓\"方向反了；A 是第一次的事；D 偷换为\"六天前失踪\"。","signal":"But 转折处出答案","syn":[["yet again he is out on the loose","He has escaped the zoo once again（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How has the snake made the zoo staff feel?","opts":["Squeezed","Threatened","Disappointed","Frustrated"],"answer":3,"expl":"has already been frustrating its staff——让员工头疼懊恼。原词 frustrate 的分词形容词化。","signal":"情绪动词定位","syn":[["frustrating its staff","Frustrated（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s2-3","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"News Report 3 · 杰克逊维尔的共享电单车烦恼","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 3（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"Electric bikes have been the craze in downtown Jacksonville since they were first introduced earlier this month as a one-year pilot program.","zh":"自本月初作为为期一年的试点项目推出以来，电动自行车在杰克逊维尔市中心掀起热潮。"},{"en":"But they’re leading to safety concerns, mainly at night when some riders don’t follow the rules of the road.","zh":"但它们也带来了安全隐患，主要在夜间——一些骑车人不遵守交通规则。"},{"en":"As the night goes on, groups of riders are often seen traveling in just about every direction in the streets and on pedestrian paths.","zh":"随着夜色渐深，经常能看到成群结队的骑车人在机动车道和步道上四处乱穿。"},{"en":"That is increasing the probability of dangerous accidents.","zh":"这正在增加危险事故发生的概率。"},{"en":"Electric bike riders have to follow all the same rules as you would if you were in an automobile.","zh":"电动自行车骑行者必须遵守与汽车相同的所有规则。"},{"en":"That means no running red lights or traveling in the opposite direction of traffic on one-way streets.","zh":"也就是说，不能闯红灯，不能在单行道上逆行。"},{"en":"City Council Member Anna Cumber was instrumental in introducing the electric bikes to Jacksonville as a way to bring new life into downtown.","zh":"市议会议员安娜·坎伯是推动把电动单车引进杰克逊维尔的关键人物，目的是给市中心带来新活力。"},{"en":"And she’s aware of the concerns.","zh":"她也意识到了这些担忧。"},{"en":"Cumber said, “People can have fun, but both drivers and riders are responsible for paying attention while on the road.","zh":"坎伯说：\"大家都可以玩得开心，但驾驶者和骑行者在路上都有责任保持注意。"},{"en":"And never assume the driver is going to stop or see you.”","zh":"永远不要想当然地认为司机会停下来、会看见你。\""}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn about the electric bike program in Jacksonville?","opts":["It is condemned as a crazy idea","It is enriching the city’s night life","It is questioned by local residents","It is giving rise to safety concerns"],"answer":3,"expl":"they're leading to safety concerns——引发安全担忧。 craze（热潮）不等于被骂作疯狂主意（A），B、C 无据。","signal":"But 转折后第一句","syn":[["leading to safety concerns","It is giving rise to safety concerns（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What are electric bike riders required to do?","opts":["Avoid entering one-way streets","Ensure the safety of pedestrians","Follow all the traffic rules drivers do","Give way to automobiles at all times"],"answer":2,"expl":"have to follow all the same rules as you would if you were in an automobile——和汽车驾驶者遵守同样交规。","signal":"must/have to 义务句","syn":[["follow all the same rules as ... in an automobile","Follow all the traffic rules drivers do（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why did Anna Cumber help introduce the electric bikes?","opts":["To ease the city’s busy traffic","To bring new life into the city","To add a new means of transport","To reduce the city’s air pollution"],"answer":1,"expl":"as a way to bring new life into downtown——给市中心注入新活力。","signal":"目的信号 as a way to","syn":[["bring new life into downtown","To bring new life into the city（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s2-4","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"生活","level":"四级","title":"Conversation 1 · 教孩子管钱的门道","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 1（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"What’s the best way to teach children how to save and spend their money?","spk":"M","zh":"教孩子存钱和花钱，最好的办法是什么？"},{"en":"You should make money a regular topic of discussion.","spk":"W","zh":"你应该让钱成为日常话题。"},{"en":"It’s best to start young, so it’s instinctive rather than a scary subject.","spk":"W","zh":"最好趁早开始，这样它就会变成本能，而不是一个吓人的话题。"},{"en":"In our family, we talk openly about things like the budget for holidays, how taxes reduce your income, and how to shop around for the best deals.","spk":"M","zh":"在我们家，我们会公开聊假期预算、税怎么减少收入、怎么货比三家找最划算的买卖。"},{"en":"Indeed.","spk":"W","zh":"确实。"},{"en":"It’s also essential to make money real for children through practical examples.","spk":"W","zh":"通过实际例子把钱变得具体真实，也很关键。"},{"en":"Working out how much we save using discount pizza coupons, for example, is much more relevant than abstract sums.","spk":"W","zh":"比如算算用披萨折扣券能省多少钱，就比抽象的算术题有用得多。"},{"en":"We also give our kids pocket money, and the amount they get is linked to chores, such as putting the bins out and emptying the dishwasher.","spk":"M","zh":"我们也给孩子零花钱，数额和做家务挂钩，比如把垃圾桶搬出去、清空洗碗机。"},{"en":"We do that too, and it’s paid according to their age.","spk":"W","zh":"我们也这么做，而且按年龄付钱。"},{"en":"Two pounds for each year so they can see some progression.","spk":"W","zh":"每长一岁加两英镑，这样他们能看到成长。"},{"en":"Teaching them to save is important.","spk":"M","zh":"教他们储蓄很重要。"},{"en":"We opened a savings account when they were young.","spk":"M","zh":"他们小时候我们就开了储蓄账户。"},{"en":"After birthdays and Christmas, they would go to the branch and deposit their gift money.","spk":"M","zh":"过生日和圣诞节之后，他们会去银行网点把礼金存进去。"},{"en":"Oh, I hadn’t considered doing that.","spk":"W","zh":"哦，这个我倒没想过。"},{"en":"In our house, we have transparent money boxes for them to put small change in, so they can see their savings grow.","spk":"W","zh":"我们家给他们用的是透明存钱罐，放零钱进去，能看着储蓄一点点长起来。"},{"en":"When the time is right, I’ll start talking to our children about investing and show them how the money saved for their further education has grown.","spk":"M","zh":"时机合适的话，我会开始跟孩子们聊投资，让他们看到为他们大学教育存的钱已经涨了多少。"},{"en":"I am always talking to my elder daughter about the importance of saving into a pension.","spk":"W","zh":"我总是跟大女儿讲往养老金里存钱的重要性。"},{"en":"She’s just started a part-time job and was thinking of not contributing to her pension.","spk":"W","zh":"她刚开始做兼职，本来在犹豫要不要缴养老金。"},{"en":"Luckily, I managed to persuade her otherwise.","spk":"W","zh":"幸好我把她劝过来了。"},{"en":"Yes, it’s such an important lesson to learn.","spk":"M","zh":"是啊，这一课太重要了。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What should parents do with the topic of money, according to the conversation?","opts":["Take it seriously","Discuss it regularly","Make it sound scary","Talk about it openly"],"answer":1,"expl":"make money a regular topic of discussion = 经常讨论。A 严肃对待、C 说得吓人（原文恰恰说别吓人 scary subject）、D 是具体某家的做法。","signal":"开头建议句 You should","syn":[["make money a regular topic of discussion","Discuss it regularly（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How can money be made real for children?","opts":["By shopping around for the best deals","By making abstract sums relevant","By citing concrete examples","By visiting discount stores"],"answer":2,"expl":"through practical examples + 披萨折扣券的例子 = 举具体例子。B 的 abstract sums 是反例（原文说比抽象数字更管用）。","signal":"举例信号 for example","syn":[["through practical examples","By citing concrete examples（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do both speakers do to teach their kids about money?","opts":["Paying their kids to help with housework","Setting kids a good example by sharing chores","Giving kids pocket money according to their needs","Urging kids to deposit some of their gift money"],"answer":0,"expl":"两人都给零花钱且与家务挂钩（we give our kids pocket money ... linked to chores / We do that too）。C 的\"按需\"不对，是按年龄；B、D 只是一方的做法。","signal":"共识句 We do that too","syn":[["pocket money ... linked to chores","Paying their kids to help with housework（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man often talk about with his elder daughter?","opts":["The importance of cutting down family expenses","The need to learn important lessons from her elders","The delight in seeing their savings grow","The necessity of saving into a pension"],"answer":3,"expl":"the importance of saving into a pension——往养老金里存钱的重要性。","signal":"always 频度词定位","syn":[["the importance of saving into a pension","The necessity of saving into a pension（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s2-5","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"职场","level":"四级","title":"Conversation 2 · 采访畅销书《奖赏成功》作者","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 2（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"Welcome to Books in Review.","spk":"W","zh":"欢迎来到《书评》节目。"},{"en":"Our guest today is John Banks, the author of the best selling new book, Rewarding Success.","spk":"W","zh":"今天的嘉宾是约翰·班克斯，畅销新书《奖赏成功》的作者。"},{"en":"Glad to be here, Jane.","spk":"M","zh":"很高兴来到这里，简。"},{"en":"Your book has sold 2 million copies, but before we discuss why it’s getting so much attention, let’s talk about your background.","spk":"W","zh":"您的书卖了两百万册。不过在聊它为什么这么受关注之前，先谈谈您的背景。"},{"en":"You’re an economist and spent two decades teaching at universities?","spk":"W","zh":"您是经济学家，还在大学教了二十年书？"},{"en":"I spent 25 years as a professor, actually.","spk":"M","zh":"其实我做了25年教授。"},{"en":"And then, for the last 10 years, I’ve worked as a political consultant, advising politicians at the national level about problems in our country.","spk":"M","zh":"之后这10年，我做政治顾问，在国家层面为政界人士就国内问题出谋划策。"},{"en":"You discuss three of those problems in the book, improving public education, reducing our nation’s healthcare burden, and increasing personal savings.","spk":"W","zh":"您在书里讨论了其中三个问题：改善公共教育、减轻国家医疗负担、提高个人储蓄。"},{"en":"But your ideas about education are the most controversial.","spk":"W","zh":"但您关于教育的想法争议最大。"},{"en":"Absolutely.","spk":"M","zh":"没错。"},{"en":"A lot of people think I’m trying to punish students who aren’t doing well, when actually my goal is to give all students more incentive to succeed.","spk":"M","zh":"很多人以为我想惩罚成绩不好的学生，其实我的目标是给所有学生更多争取成功的动力。"},{"en":"I’m not sure I agree with you.","spk":"W","zh":"这一点我不太同意。"},{"en":"Your proposal to pay cash rewards to students who get good grades is a particular problem.","spk":"W","zh":"您提议给成绩好的学生发现金奖励，这是个突出问题。"},{"en":"What about students who don’t get good grades?","spk":"W","zh":"那些成绩不好的学生怎么办？"},{"en":"It seems like you’re blaming them for not succeeding, when poor performance in school isn’t a child’s fault.","spk":"W","zh":"感觉您在怪他们不成功，可在学校表现不好并不是孩子的错。"},{"en":"But my proposal is not just to reward students with good grades, but also students who show improvements.","spk":"M","zh":"但我的提议不只是奖励成绩好的学生，也奖励取得进步的学生。"},{"en":"Okay, another criticism of the plan is the cash rewards themselves.","spk":"W","zh":"好，对这项计划的另一个批评是现金奖励本身。"},{"en":"Where will the money come from?","spk":"W","zh":"钱从哪儿来？"},{"en":"If students do better, we’ll spend less on schooling.","spk":"M","zh":"如果学生表现更好，我们在教育上的花费就会减少。"},{"en":"So, in the end, the rewards will pay for themselves.","spk":"M","zh":"所以最终，这些奖励物归原主，等于自己买单。"},{"en":"What about now?","spk":"W","zh":"那眼下呢？"},{"en":"How will we fund the rewards in the meantime?","spk":"W","zh":"过渡时期的奖励资金怎么来？"},{"en":"Well, by increasing taxes or moving money from other areas of the budget into education.","spk":"M","zh":"靠加税，或者把预算中其他领域的钱挪到教育上。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn about John Banks?","opts":["He is a successful businessman","He reviews books on political affairs","He has published a new bestseller","He has worked in several banks"],"answer":2,"expl":"the author of the best selling new book——出了本畅销新书。A 商人、B 书评人、D 银行履历均无据。","signal":"开头介绍句","syn":[["the author of the best selling new book","He has published a new bestseller（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the woman say is the most controversial?","opts":["The man’s ideas about education","The man’s academic background","The man’s attempts at drawing public attention","The man’s proposals to solve economic problems"],"answer":0,"expl":"your ideas about education are the most controversial——他关于教育的观点。","signal":"最高级 the most controversial","syn":[["your ideas about education are the most controversial","The man's ideas about education（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is the man's goal with his proposal?","opts":["To reduce students’ financial burden","To motivate all students to be successful","To give students incentive to excel in economics","To provide remedies for students’ poor performance"],"answer":1,"expl":"my goal is to give all students more incentive to succeed——激励所有学生走向成功。C 偷换成\"经济学\"；A、D 与原文相悖。","signal":"goal 信号词","syn":[["give all students more incentive to succeed","To motivate all students to be successful（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How will the rewards be funded in the meantime?","opts":["Improving school budgeting","Increasing tuition fees","Seeking donations","Raising taxes"],"answer":3,"expl":"by increasing taxes or moving money from other areas——加税或挪预算，对应 D。","signal":"方式信号 by + doing","syn":[["by increasing taxes","Raising taxes（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s2-6","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"生活","level":"四级","title":"Passage 1 · 别再说\"我好忙\"了","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 1（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"I met three different people today, and each time, when I asked, “How are you?”","zh":"今天我见了三个不同的人，每次我问「最近怎么样？」"},{"en":"The reply was exactly the same.","zh":"回答都一模一样。"},{"en":"“I’m busy”.","zh":"「我好忙」。"},{"en":"Honestly, I hear the same answer from the vast majority of people I meet.","zh":"说实话，我遇到的大多数人都给我同样的答案。"},{"en":"So I started to think: “Guess what?","zh":"于是我开始想：「你猜怎么着？"},{"en":"Everybody’s busy!”","zh":"人人都忙！」"},{"en":"I’m busy, you’re busy, everybody’s busy.","zh":"我忙，你忙，人人都忙。"},{"en":"So you being busy doesn’t make me sympathetic at all.","zh":"所以你说你忙，根本不会让我同情。"},{"en":"Because “busy” is the state of the world.","zh":"因为「忙」就是这个世界的常态。"},{"en":"So I’m launching a campaign to stop people complaining about being “busy.”","zh":"所以我要发起一场运动，让大家别再抱怨「忙」。"},{"en":"It may sound harsh, but the truth is, nobody cares.","zh":"这听起来可能刻薄，但事实是：没人在乎。"},{"en":"In a busy world, “being busy” doesn’t stand out, nor does it mean productive, creative, accomplished, or professional.","zh":"在一个忙碌的世界里，「忙」并不出众，也不等于高效、有创造力、有成就或专业。"},{"en":"Steve Maraboli once said, “When someone tells you they are too ‘busy’, it’s not a reflection of their schedule; it’s a reflection of YOUR spot on their schedule.”","zh":"史蒂夫·马拉博利说过：「当有人告诉你他太『忙』，那不是在说他日程的状态，而是在说你在他日程里的位置。」"},{"en":"Donna Lynn Hope has also remarked, “Busy doesn’t mean better.","zh":"唐娜·林恩·霍普也评论过：「忙不等于更好。"},{"en":"I’ve never envied a busy person—the one who likes to point out their busy lives to others.”","zh":"我从不羡慕忙人——那种喜欢向别人点明自己生活多忙的人。」"},{"en":"The reality is, nobody is too busy—it’s just about priorities.","zh":"现实是，没人真的忙到那个程度——关键只是优先级。"},{"en":"So the next time someone asks you how you are, maybe respond differently.","zh":"所以下次有人问你最近怎么样，也许可以换个回答。"},{"en":"In my experience, the “I’m busy” response is really covering up the fact that they’re not actually accomplishing their real purpose.","zh":"据我的经验，「我好忙」这个回答，其实是在掩盖一个事实：他们并没有真正完成自己真正的目标。"},{"en":"And “being busy” is the lie they tell themselves about why they can’t achieve it.","zh":"「忙」是他们讲给自己听的谎言，用来解释为什么没能实现目标。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why does the speaker launch the campaign?","opts":["To show his sympathy towards people always being busy","To prevent people from complaining about being “busy”","To call on busy people to take care of themselves","To help busy people to sort out their priorities"],"answer":1,"expl":"to stop people complaining about being 'busy'——原文直接给出目的。A 同情（原文说不会同情）、D 帮忙理优先级都偏离。","signal":"目的信号 to do","syn":[["stop people complaining about being 'busy'","To prevent people from complaining about being 'busy'（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the speaker suggest people do when asked how they are?","opts":["Avoid saying we are busy","Reflect on their true purpose","Describe our schedule in detail","Respond as most busy people do"],"answer":0,"expl":"maybe respond differently——别再用\"忙\"来回答，即避免说\"我们很忙\"。","signal":"建议句 maybe","syn":[["respond differently","Avoid saying we are busy（语义对应）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why do people say \"I'm busy\" according to the speaker?","opts":["To show their achievements resulted from great efforts","To prove they stand out as accomplished professionals","To cover up their failure to achieve some purpose","To tell others a complete lie about their inability"],"answer":2,"expl":"covering up the fact that they're not actually accomplishing their real purpose——掩饰未能实现目标。D 说\"彻底撒谎\"太绝对；A、B 是\"忙\"想营造的假象而非说这话的动机。","signal":"动名词 covering up 处设题","syn":[["covering up the fact","To cover up their failure to achieve some purpose（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s2-7","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"科普","level":"四级","title":"Passage 2 · 极限运动为什么让人上瘾","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 2（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"More and more people are taking up extreme sports, like snowboarding, skateboarding, mountain biking, and many more.","zh":"越来越多的人开始玩极限运动：单板滑雪、滑板、山地自行车等等。"},{"en":"Why are these sports becoming so popular?","zh":"这些运动为什么越来越流行？"},{"en":"One thing that extreme sports do better than perhaps anything else is to help you stop being afraid.","zh":"极限运动比任何其他事情都擅长的一点，是帮你不再害怕。"},{"en":"It may sound strange to say that their main function is to reduce fear.","zh":"说它们的主要功能是减轻恐惧，听起来也许奇怪。"},{"en":"But after a time, your fear response to other things in life will be dramatically reduced.","zh":"但一段时间之后，你对生活中其他事情的恐惧反应会显著降低。"},{"en":"After all, if you can jump out of a plane or off a bridge, then you can face anything else easily.","zh":"毕竟，如果你能从飞机上跳下去、从桥上跳下去，那其他任何事你都能轻松面对。"},{"en":"When doing extreme sports, you have to become more focused.","zh":"做极限运动时，你必须更加专注。"},{"en":"You’ll be pushed to your limits, and if you aren’t focused you’ll make dangerous mistakes.","zh":"你会被推向极限，如果不专注就会犯下危险错误。"},{"en":"Learning to be this focused when enjoying extreme sports will help you to be focused at work, keeping you more productive and ultimately more successful.","zh":"在极限运动中学会的专注，也会帮助你在工作中专注，让你更高产，最终更成功。"},{"en":"It’s great to stay fit and healthy, but standard exercise routines and sports only work the same muscles repeatedly.","zh":"保持健康很好，但常规锻炼和运动只是重复使用同一批肌肉。"},{"en":"With extreme sports, you’ll be working entirely different muscles, and that means you get an all-over workout.","zh":"极限运动动用的是完全不同的肌肉，这意味着你能得到全身体的锻炼。"},{"en":"Extreme sports also burn a lot more calories than other sports.","zh":"极限运动燃烧的卡路里也比其他运动多得多。"},{"en":"Skateboarding, for example, can burn as many as 500 calories per hour.","zh":"比如滑板，每小时能燃烧多达500卡。"},{"en":"Basketball burns around 300 in the same time.","zh":"同样时间篮球大约烧300卡。"},{"en":"When you find that you can overcome the physical or mental challenges involved in extreme sports, you’ll feel superhuman and your self-confidence will be at an all-time high.","zh":"当你发现自己能克服极限运动中的身体或心理挑战时，你会觉得自己超凡入圣，自信心也达到前所未有的高度。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the passage say is one main function of extreme sports?","opts":["They will help one reduce fear","They should become so popular","They will be less challenging after a time","They should cover so many different types"],"answer":0,"expl":"help you stop being afraid / reduce fear——减少恐惧。C 的\"之后挑战变小\"偷换（是恐惧变小，不是挑战变小）。","signal":"设问自答 Why ... ? One thing ... is to ...","syn":[["help you stop being afraid","They will help one reduce fear（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why is focus especially important when doing extreme sports?","opts":["To break one’s ultimate limits","To stop being extremely afraid","To avoid dangerous mistakes","To enjoy the sports to the full"],"answer":2,"expl":"if you aren't focused you'll make dangerous mistakes——不专注会犯危险错误。","signal":"条件句 if","syn":[["you'll make dangerous mistakes","To avoid dangerous mistakes（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How do extreme sports benefit the body physically?","opts":["By allowing our motivation to be at an all-time high","By stopping us hurting the same muscles repeatedly","By burning as many as 300 calories per hour","By enabling us to get an all-over workout"],"answer":3,"expl":"working entirely different muscles ... you get an all-over workout——让全身都得到锻炼。C 数字张冠李戴：500是滑板、300是篮球；B 的\"不重复用同一块肌肉\"是常规运动的缺点对比。","signal":"对比与结论 that means","syn":[["you get an all-over workout","By enabling us to get an all-over workout（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2406s2-8","group":"2024年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"职场","level":"四级","title":"Passage 3 · 冲突不是坏事：团队的\"有效冲突\"","material":"2024年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 3（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕）；题目：2024年6月四级真题PDF；答案：官方答案速查 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"Most of us have been in teams or organizations where we’ve had conflict with the people that we’re working with around the ideas or decisions that we’re discussing.","zh":"我们大多数人都经历过这样的事：在团队或组织里，围绕正在讨论的想法或决策，与共事的人发生冲突。"},{"en":"Conflict is natural.","zh":"冲突是自然的。"},{"en":"We all bring different life and work experiences to the table.","zh":"我们每个人都带着不同的生活和工作经验来到谈判桌前。"},{"en":"We all have different personality preferences and tendencies.","zh":"我们有不同的性格偏好和倾向。"},{"en":"We’re not all going to have the same ideas on how to approach policies, programs or problems.","zh":"对于如何制定政策、设计项目或解决问题，我们不可能想法完全一致。"},{"en":"But too often we get caught in this place where conflict is perceived to be negative—something we want to avoid so that we can maintain the harmony of our workplace.","zh":"但太多时候我们陷入一种误区：把冲突看成负面的东西——为了维持职场和睦而想避开的东西。"},{"en":"This could be because some people want to avoid conflict at all costs, after all they still have to work together.","zh":"这可能是因为有些人不惜一切代价避免冲突——毕竟低头不见抬头见，还要继续共事。"},{"en":"But this kind of artificial harmony isn’t the answer.","zh":"但这种人为制造的和睦并不是答案。"},{"en":"Productive conflict is a vital part of teams and organizations that want to push forward and do more.","zh":"对于想要前进、想要做成更多事的团队和组织来说，有效的冲突至关重要。"},{"en":"Without conflict, we’re often stuck in this artificial harmony where people don’t express potentially innovative ideas for fear that they may start conflict with others.","zh":"没有冲突，我们常常困在这种虚假和睦里，人们害怕引发冲突而不敢表达可能有创新性的想法。"},{"en":"But if you’re in a place where you have a basis of trust, conflict can be extremely productive.","zh":"但如果你们之间有信任的基础，冲突可以极其富有成效。"},{"en":"It can lead to increased innovation and greater trust on teams.","zh":"它能带来更多创新，也能加深团队信任。"},{"en":"It may be an uncomfortable process, but good leaders and healthy teams recognize that productive and healthy conflict is an important part of how they function.","zh":"这个过程也许不好受，但优秀的领导者和健康的团队都明白：有效且健康的冲突，是他们运转机制的重要部分。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the speaker say about conflict?","opts":["It is natural","It is instrumental","It is personal","It is vital"],"answer":0,"expl":"Conflict is natural——冲突是自然的。","signal":"短判断句独立成题","syn":[["Conflict is natural","It is natural（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why do some people avoid conflict?","opts":["To guard against being perceived negatively","To prevent themselves from being isolated","To conceal personality preferences","To maintain workplace harmony"],"answer":3,"expl":"so that we can maintain the harmony of our workplace——为了维持职场和睦。","signal":"目的从句 so that","syn":[["maintain the harmony of our workplace","To maintain workplace harmony（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What can productive conflict lead to?","opts":["It helps to enhance team spirit","It stimulates innovative ideas","It helps to resolve problems","It facilitates policy-making"],"answer":1,"expl":"It can lead to increased innovation and greater trust——激发创新、加深信任。B 正确；A 偷换 team spirit；C、D 过度引申。","signal":"lead to 结果信号","syn":[["increased innovation","It stimulates innovative ideas（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is the basis for conflict to be productive?","opts":["An innovative mind","Corporate culture","Mutual trust","A healthy mentality"],"answer":2,"expl":"if you're in a place where you have a basis of trust——相互信任。","signal":"条件句 if ... basis of trust","syn":[["a basis of trust","Mutual trust（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s1-1","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"职场","level":"四级","title":"Conversation 1 · 又买新手机？同事劝你冷静","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 1（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：新东方在线答案键 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"I'm going to the city centre to buy a new phone today.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我今天要去市中心买部新手机。"},{"en":"Didn't you buy a new phone just two months ago?","spk":"W","zh":"W：你不是两个月前才买了新手机吗？"},{"en":"It was three months ago, and I already know what you're going to say.","spk":"M","zh":"M：那是三个月前，而且我已经知道你要说什么了。"},{"en":"You're thinking I shouldn't replace my phone this soon.","spk":"M","zh":"M：你是觉得我不该这么快换手机。"},{"en":"No, actually, I was wondering how you could possibly afford a new phone.","spk":"W","zh":"W：不是，其实我是好奇你怎么可能买得起新手机。"},{"en":"But, now that you mention it, I do think getting another phone so soon is wasteful, regardless of the cost.","spk":"W","zh":"W：不过既然你提了，我确实觉得这么快又买一部太浪费，先别说钱。"},{"en":"Maybe you're right, but the thing is, everyone at the office has a nice, expensive phone, and I'm a little embarrassed by mine.","spk":"M","zh":"M：也许你说得对，但问题是，办公室里人人都拿着漂亮贵的手机，我的让我有点尴尬。"},{"en":"I just got a credit card, so I thought I might as well buy a new phone.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我刚办了信用卡，就想干脆买部新手机吧。"},{"en":"I don't think buying a phone on credit is a good idea.","spk":"W","zh":"W：我觉得用信用卡买手机不是好主意。"},{"en":"Look, you've only been working for five months now.","spk":"W","zh":"W：你看，你才工作了五个月。"},{"en":"People understand that you are a recent graduate, and I doubt anyone cares about your phone other than yourself.","spk":"W","zh":"W：大家都理解你是应届毕业生，而且除了你自己，恐怕没人在意你的手机。"},{"en":"Maybe you're right, but the credit card has a very good special offer, where I don't pay any interest for six months.","spk":"M","zh":"M：也许吧，但这张信用卡有个很划算的优惠，六个月内免利息。"},{"en":"I'll be able to pay for the phone well before that period is over.","spk":"M","zh":"M：期限结束前我肯定能把手机钱还清。"},{"en":"I still think it's a bad idea to use a credit card for something you don't need.","spk":"W","zh":"W：我还是认为用信用卡买不需要的东西是个坏主意。"},{"en":"One of my colleagues bought a lot of things on credit during her first year of work, and it became a bad habit, and she accumulated a lot of debt.","spk":"W","zh":"W：我有个同事工作第一年刷了很多卡，养成了坏习惯，欠了一大笔债。"},{"en":"Well, I can see how that might happen to someone, and I'm sure she regrets it, but I know it won't happen to me.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我明白这种事可能发生在别人身上，她肯定也后悔，但我知道不会发生在我身上。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the woman wonder at the beginning of the conversation?","opts":["Why the man is so anxious to buy a new phone","How the man could possibly afford a new phone","How the man got into the habit of being wasteful","Why the man is so fond of using his credit card"],"answer":1,"expl":"I was wondering how you could possibly afford a new phone——她好奇的是他怎么买得起。注意别选成\"为什么急着买\"。","signal":"开头疑问句即第一题","syn":[["how you could possibly afford a new phone","How the man could possibly afford a new phone（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man think of his current phone?","opts":["It is not in fashion any more","It goes out of order frequently","It is not as fancy as his colleagues’","It lacks functions office work requires"],"answer":0,"expl":"everyone at the office has a nice, expensive phone, and I'm a little embarrassed by mine——他觉得自己的手机过时了、拿不出手。","signal":"评价句 I'm embarrassed","syn":[["a little embarrassed by mine","It is not in fashion any more（语义对应）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man say about the credit card's special offer?","opts":["It enables him to buy a new phone at a more favorable price","It is a special offer to recent college graduates working in offices","It is available to office workers who have a good enough credit score","It allows him to borrow money without paying interest for six months"],"answer":3,"expl":"I don't pay any interest for six months——六个月免息。","signal":"数字与优惠细节","syn":[["I don't pay any interest for six months","borrow money without paying interest for six months（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What happened to the woman's colleague during her first year of work?","opts":["She borrowed money to pay her debt","She developed a habit of overspending","She enjoys buying a lot of fancy things","She regrets ignoring the woman’s advice"],"answer":1,"expl":"it became a bad habit, and she accumulated a lot of debt——养成了过度消费的坏习惯。","signal":"例证处设题","syn":[["it became a bad habit","She developed a habit of overspending（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s1-2","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"Conversation 2 · 小房子运动：20平米也能安家","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 2（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：新东方在线答案键 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"Welcome to the Morning Show.","spk":"W","zh":"W：欢迎来到《晨间秀》。"},{"en":"Our guest today is a popular blog writer and a major figure in the tiny home community.","spk":"W","zh":"W：今天的嘉宾是一位人气博客作者，也是小住宅社区的重要人物。"},{"en":"Welcome, Bob Loinbo.","spk":"W","zh":"W：欢迎你，鲍勃·洛伊恩博。"},{"en":"Hi, Mary.","spk":"M","zh":"M：嗨，玛丽。"},{"en":"Hi, Bob.","spk":"W","zh":"W：嗨，鲍勃。"},{"en":"You're an advocate of the tiny home movement.","spk":"W","zh":"W：你是\"小住宅运动\"的倡导者。"},{"en":"A lot of people don't know about this movement.","spk":"W","zh":"W：很多人还不了解这个运动。"},{"en":"Can you tell our audience what it's about?","spk":"W","zh":"W：能跟我们的听众讲讲它是什么吗？"},{"en":"Well, it's mainly about increasing home ownership and protecting the environment.","spk":"M","zh":"M：它主要是关于提高住房自有率和保护环境。"},{"en":"Of course, those are great goals.","spk":"W","zh":"W：这两个都是好目标。"},{"en":"But I've seen your blog, and you write about houses that are as small as 20 square meters.","spk":"W","zh":"W：但我看过你的博客，你写的房子小到只有20平方米。"},{"en":"That's not a realistic size for families.","spk":"W","zh":"W：这个尺寸对家庭来说不现实。"},{"en":"I do talk about very small homes, but there's no set definition of a tiny home.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我确实写过很小的房子，但小住宅并没有固定的定义。"},{"en":"And other people include homes that are much larger, say, 60 square meters.","spk":"M","zh":"M：也有人把大得多的房子算进来，比如60平方米的。"},{"en":"And you'd be surprised.","spk":"M","zh":"M：而且你会惊讶的。"},{"en":"Many families of four are happy living in houses that are under 30 square meters.","spk":"M","zh":"M：很多四口之家住在不到30平方米的房子里也很幸福。"},{"en":"But I think most of us want spacious homes.","spk":"W","zh":"W：但我想我们大多数人还是想要宽敞的房子。"},{"en":"The average new house in this area is 150 square meters.","spk":"W","zh":"W：这个地区新建房屋的平均面积是150平方米。"},{"en":"And that's what people dream of owning.","spk":"W","zh":"W：那才是人们梦想拥有的。"},{"en":"Yes, but I think that dream needs to change, considering the cost of housing.","spk":"M","zh":"M：是的，但考虑到住房成本，这个梦想需要改变。"},{"en":"Housing costs are high, but do people really save that much by having a smaller home?","spk":"W","zh":"W：住房成本是高，但住小一点真能省那么多吗？"},{"en":"Absolutely.","spk":"M","zh":"M： absolutely，绝对能。"},{"en":"Many people who can only afford to rent a larger home are able to buy a tiny home.","spk":"M","zh":"M：很多只租得起大房子的人，是买得起小住宅的。"},{"en":"In this city, the average home costs $200,000, and a tiny home costs just $50,000.","spk":"M","zh":"M：在这座城市，普通住房均价20万美元，小住宅只要5万美元。"},{"en":"Those are huge savings.","spk":"W","zh":"W：这省的可不是一星半点。"},{"en":"So, tiny homes might not be for everyone, but they're a good option for many.","spk":"M","zh":"M：所以小住宅未必适合所有人，但对很多人来说是个好选择。"},{"en":"You mentioned the environment earlier.","spk":"W","zh":"W：你刚才提到了环境。"},{"en":"How does this benefit the planet?","spk":"W","zh":"W：这对地球有什么好处？"},{"en":"Well, if people have smaller homes, they use less land and fewer resources to build them.","spk":"M","zh":"M：如果房子更小，建造时占用的土地和资源就更少。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What is the tiny home movement mainly about according to the man?","opts":["Blog writing and natural resources saving","Joint efforts to improve the local community","Audience participation in The Morning Show","Home ownership and environmental protection"],"answer":3,"expl":"it's mainly about increasing home ownership and protecting the environment——住房自有率与环保。","signal":"问答定位 what it's about","syn":[["increasing home ownership and protecting the environment","Home ownership and environmental protection（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the woman think of a 20-square-meter house?","opts":["Not a realistic size for families","Not welcomed by most Americans","Only fit for families of four or less","Only suitable for renting to the poor"],"answer":0,"expl":"That's not a realistic size for families——对家庭不现实。","signal":"评价句 that's...","syn":[["That's not a realistic size for families","Not a realistic size for families（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man say about the dream of owning a big house?","opts":["It should be changed","It isn’t easy to realize","It will come true sooner or later","It doesn’t appeal to average families"],"answer":0,"expl":"considering the cost of housing, that dream needs to change——这个梦想应该改变。","signal":"转折 But 后观点句","syn":[["that dream needs to change","It should be changed（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man conclude about tiny homes?","opts":["They help to lower housing prices","They help to save up for larger houses","They are a good choice for many people","They are vital to reducing waste worldwide"],"answer":2,"expl":"they're a good option for many——对很多人是好选择。","signal":"结论句 So ...","syn":[["they're a good option for many","They are a good choice for many people（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s1-3","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"News Report 1 · 费耶特维尔致敬老司机","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 1（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：新东方在线答案键 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"The City of Fayetteville is making a special effort to recognize its bus drivers, ahead of the newly proclaimed Transit Driver Appreciation Day, happening Saturday.","zh":"在周六 newly 设立的\"公交司机感恩日\"到来前，费耶特维尔市正在特别表彰其公交司机。"},{"en":"As part of the event, the city is celebrating its longest serving driver on the force.","zh":"作为活动的一部分，市政府要表扬司龄最长的司机。"},{"en":"That driver is Sherry Christian.","zh":"这位司机就是雪莉·克里斯蒂安。"},{"en":"Christian has been a driver for 25 years.","zh":"克里斯蒂安开车已经25年。"},{"en":"The Fayetteville native believes driving a school bus allows her to give back to her community.","zh":"这位费耶特维尔本地人相信，开校车让她能够回馈社区。"},{"en":"She says that the best part of the job is watching the children who ride her bus grow up.","zh":"她说这份工作最好的部分，是看着坐她车的孩子们长大。"},{"en":"Transit Driver Appreciation Day has been celebrated across the country as far back as 2009.","zh":"\"公交司机感恩日\"在全国范围的庆祝最早可以追溯到2009年。"},{"en":"However, this week, the City of Fayetteville issued a proclamation for the day to take place March 18th.","zh":"不过本周，费耶特维尔市发布宣言，把这一天定在3月18日。"},{"en":"Officials said they want bus drivers to know how important they are to Fayetteville, serving almost 1.6 million riders a year.","zh":"官员们表示，他们想让公交司机知道自己对这座城市有多重要——他们每年服务近160万乘客。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn about Sherry Christian?","opts":["She is making a special effort to be recognized","She has been living in Fayetteville for 25 years","She has been driving a school bus ever since 2009","She is the longest-serving bus driver in Fayetteville"],"answer":3,"expl":"the city is celebrating its longest serving driver ... Christian has been a driver for 25 years——她是服务时间最长的司机。B 偷换：开车25年≠住在费耶特维尔25年；C 的2009年是节日历史。","signal":"人物细节定位","syn":[["its longest serving driver","the longest-serving bus driver in Fayetteville（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do officials want bus drivers to know?","opts":["The importance of their service to the city","The number of riders they serve in the city","The new proclamation issued early this week","The significance of the event to take place March 18"],"answer":0,"expl":"they want bus drivers to know how important they are to Fayetteville——他们对城市有多重要。","signal":"结尾句出答案","syn":[["how important they are to Fayetteville","The importance of their service to the city（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s1-4","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"News Report 2 · 威尔顿学区预算要涨5.99%","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 2（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：新东方在线答案键 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"The Wilton School Board has proposed a 5.99 percent spending increase.","zh":"威尔顿教育委员会提出了5.99%的支出增长方案。"},{"en":"If approved, it would be the largest jump in at least eight budget cycles.","zh":"如果获批，这将是至少八个预算周期以来最大的一次涨幅。"},{"en":"The 5.99 percent request more than doubles the highest previous year over year increase in the last eight years, which was 2.99 percent for the 2021 to 2022 school year.","zh":"5.99%的申请额是过去八年最高年度增幅（2021至2022学年的2.99%）的两倍多。"},{"en":"The biggest driver of the 91.8 million proposed budget remains teachers salaries.","zh":"9180万美元拟议预算的最大驱动因素仍是教师工资。"},{"en":"These account for 64 percent of the total request at 59 million dollars.","zh":"工资占总申请额的64%，达5900万美元。"},{"en":"The 59 million dollars is up from the 56.7 million dollars budgeted for the current school year.","zh":"5900万美元高于本学年预算的5670万美元。"},{"en":"There are some factors that could affect the budget moving forward.","zh":"有一些因素可能影响后续预算。"},{"en":"One of those is total enrollment.","zh":"其中之一是总入学人数。"},{"en":"The district will have a total enrollment of 3,742 students.","zh":"本学区总入学人数为3742人。"},{"en":"Almost all of these students will be in kindergarten through high school, but 66 will be in prekindergarten and other programs.","zh":"几乎所有学生都在幼儿园到高中阶段，另有66人在学前班及其他项目。"},{"en":"This represents 47 fewer students than the current year.","zh":"这比当前学年少了47名学生。"},{"en":"Fewer students mean less federal and state funding.","zh":"学生减少意味着联邦和州拨款减少。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the Wilton School Board propose to do?","opts":["Budgeted $56.7 million for the coming school year","Requested to raise teachers’ salaries by 3 percent","Proposed a spending increase by 5.99 percent","Kept raising funds for at least 8 budget cycles"],"answer":2,"expl":"has proposed a 5.99 percent spending increase——提议支出增长5.99%。C 与原词对应。","signal":"首句即答案","syn":[["proposed a 5.99 percent spending increase","Proposed a spending increase by 5.99 percent（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What may affect the school district's budget according to the report?","opts":["Decrease in salaries for school administrators","Reduction in federal and state funding","Firing of less qualified faculty members","Closing down of some less competitive schools"],"answer":1,"expl":"Fewer students mean less federal and state funding——联邦和州拨款减少。A 的降薪、C 的裁员、D 的关校均未提及。","signal":"结尾因果句","syn":[["less federal and state funding","Reduction in federal and state funding（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s1-5","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"News Report 3 · 苏格兰\"雷打雪\"惊动警察","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 3（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：新东方在线答案键 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"A rare thundersnow event has taken place in Scotland.","zh":"苏格兰出现了一场罕见的\"雷打雪\"天气。"},{"en":"And alarmed locals contacted police, thinking they had heard bombs going off.","zh":"受惊的当地居民打电话报警，以为自己听到了炸弹爆炸。"},{"en":"The phenomenon happens when thunder and lightning mix with a heavy snowstorm, sometimes causing loud claps that can be confused with explosions.","zh":"这种现象发生在雷电与暴雪混合之时，有时会产生巨大的炸响，可能被误认为爆炸。"},{"en":"One person described it as a loud boom, similar to a plane crash.","zh":"有人形容那声音像巨大的闷响，类似飞机坠毁。"},{"en":"Another person was woken up in the middle of the night by what he thought was early construction work starting.","zh":"还有一个人半夜被吵醒，以为是工地的活儿提前开工了。"},{"en":"The noise was powerful enough to shake buildings and set off car alarms.","zh":"声响大到足以震动建筑物、触发汽车警报。"},{"en":"The police were flooded with many calls from the public.","zh":"公众的报警电话让警方应接不暇。"},{"en":"And they sent out a message asking people to remain calm.","zh":"警方发出信息，请民众保持冷静。"},{"en":"The police assured everyone that it was just thunder and lightning rather than some military exercise.","zh":"警方向大家保证，那只是雷电，不是什么军事演习。"},{"en":"The weather was the coldest it had been for the season, so people were warned to be careful when traveling outside.","zh":"天气是当季最冷的，因此提醒人们外出时小心。"},{"en":"In particular, dangerous conditions such as icy roads or wet ground could cause difficulty for drivers.","zh":"特别是结冰路面或湿滑地面等危险状况可能给司机造成困难。"},{"en":"The rail service also announced potential disruptions to trains due to the deep snow.","zh":"铁路部门也宣布因深雪可能出现列车晚点。"},{"en":"Some roads were also closed because of the severe weather.","zh":"一些道路也因恶劣天气关闭。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the report say about thundersnow events?","opts":["They often take place in the Scottish Highlands","They usually happen in the middle of the night","Their damage can be as serious as that of bombs","Their loud claps can be confused with explosions"],"answer":3,"expl":"sometimes causing loud claps that can be confused with explosions——巨响可能被误认为爆炸。","signal":"现象解释句","syn":[["loud claps that can be confused with explosions","Their loud claps can be confused with explosions（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did the police do after receiving many calls?","opts":["They sent out a message to calm them down","They promised to stop the construction work","They told them the military exercise was over","They set off to inspect the site of the plane crash"],"answer":0,"expl":"they sent out a message asking people to remain calm——发消息让大家冷静。","signal":"动作顺序定位","syn":[["asking people to remain calm","sent out a message to calm them down（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What were people warned to do when going outside?","opts":["Keep warm","Take caution","Avoid driving","Use rail service"],"answer":1,"expl":"people were warned to be careful when traveling outside——外出要小心。A 的保暖、D 的坐火车、C 的别开车都偏了。","signal":"warn 提醒句","syn":[["warned to be careful when traveling outside","Take caution（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s1-6","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"科普","level":"四级","title":"Passage 1 · 孩子每天都需要蹦蹦跳跳","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 1（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：新东方在线答案键 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"Kids need time every day to run, jump, stretch and play.","zh":"孩子每天都需要时间跑一跑、跳一跳、伸展和玩耍。"},{"en":"These experiences have been shown to build children's confidence and pleasure in physical activities.","zh":"已有研究表明，这些经历能建立孩子对体育活动的信心和乐趣。"},{"en":"Develop their motor skills and even improve emotional well being.","zh":"发展运动技能，甚至改善情绪健康。"},{"en":"To begin with, children seem to have a natural desire to overcome challenges and take risks.","zh":"首先，孩子似乎天生渴望克服挑战、承担风险。"},{"en":"Taking healthy risks through physical movement builds children's confidence and ability to solve problems and persist through frustration.","zh":"通过身体运动承担健康的风险，能建立孩子的信心、解决问题的能力和承受挫折的韧性。"},{"en":"Secondly, movement activities build children's big body skills such as coordination and balance.","zh":"其次，运动活动培养孩子的大肢体技能，比如协调与平衡。"},{"en":"As well as the fine motor skills they need for tasks like writing, tying their shoes, or throwing and catching a ball.","zh":"以及写字、系鞋带、传球接球等任务所需的精细动作技能。"},{"en":"Thirdly, according to the American Psychological Association, regular physical activity, and especially outdoor activity, reduces children's stress and depression and improves their ability to focus and learn.","zh":"第三，根据美国心理学会的研究，规律的体育活动，尤其是户外活动，能减少孩子的压力和抑郁，提高专注与学习能力。"},{"en":"Regular exercise can significantly improve self regulation and decrease disciplinary consequences for negative behavior.","zh":"规律运动能显著改善自我调节，减少负面行为带来的纪律处分。"},{"en":"Physical activity provides a positive outlet for frustration, anxiety or anger and can become a healthy coping skill throughout life.","zh":"体育活动为沮丧、焦虑或愤怒提供了积极的出口，并能成为受益终身的健康应对技能。"},{"en":"Finally, we know that physical activity is important for our physical and mental health and cultivating the habit of physical activity starts early.","zh":"最后，我们知道体育活动对身心健康都很重要，而培养运动习惯要趁早。"},{"en":"Children are more likely to develop a lifelong love of physical activity from frequent positive early experiences.","zh":"经常性的积极早期体验，更容易让孩子养成对体育活动的终身热爱。"},{"en":"Not every child enjoys competitive sports or playing with balls, and that's okay.","zh":"不是每个孩子都喜欢竞技运动或玩球，这没关系。"},{"en":"There are plenty of other options, such as imaginative play, non competitive games, and gardening or nature experiences.","zh":"还有很多别的选择，比如想象性游戏、非竞技性游戏、园艺或自然体验。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do children seem to have a natural desire to do?","opts":["Play outdoors and enjoy themselves","Beat challenges and take risks","Take care of their well-being","Grow up strong and healthy"],"answer":1,"expl":"a natural desire to overcome challenges and take risks——克服挑战、承担风险。","signal":"Firstly 分论点","syn":[["overcome challenges and take risks","Beat challenges and take risks（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What can regular physical activity do for children according to the APA?","opts":["Enable them to develop their motor skills","Help them to conceal their frustration","Reduce their stress and depression","Prevent them from feeling lonely"],"answer":2,"expl":"reduces children's stress and depression——减少压力和抑郁。B 的隐藏挫败感曲解 persist through frustration。","signal":"Thirdly 分论点 + 机构观点","syn":[["reduces children's stress and depression","Reduce their stress and depression（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the speaker say about cultivating the habit of physical activity?","opts":["It begins early","It proves demanding","It calls for lifelong efforts","It lies in nature experiences"],"answer":0,"expl":"cultivating the habit of physical activity starts early——习惯培养要趁早。","signal":"Finally 分论点","syn":[["starts early","It begins early（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s1-7","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"Passage 2 · 求职新动向：为了多元包容可以少拿钱","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 2（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：新东方在线答案键 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"A new study finds that job seekers are even willing to explore jobs with lower salaries, when companies are more diverse.","zh":"一项新研究发现，当公司更多元时，求职者甚至愿意探索薪水更低的工作。"},{"en":"It finds that sharing information about diversity makes job postings more attractive to job seekers, even when pay is lower.","zh":"研究发现，在职位发布中提供多元信息，会让职位对求职者更有吸引力，即使工资更低。"},{"en":"To conduct the study, the team partnered with an online job listings platform, which emails postings relevant to individuals and their job search criteria.","zh":"为了开展研究，团队与一个在线招聘平台合作，该平台向用户发送与其求职条件匹配的职位邮件。"},{"en":"Thank you For the course of the 11 week study, the platform emailed job listings to some 180,000 users placed in one of two conditions.","zh":"在为期11周的研究中，平台向约18万用户发送职位列表，分成两种条件。"},{"en":"In the baseline condition, participants saw emails in the normal format, with no information on diversity.","zh":"在基线条件下，参与者收到的是普通格式的邮件，不含多元信息。"},{"en":"In the diversity condition, participants saw a diversity score for each listing, information about the race, gender, education, and language skills of a company's workforce compared to others in the same sector and location.","zh":"在多元条件下，参与者会看到每个职位的多元评分——公司员工的种族、性别、学历和语言技能构成，与同地区同行业其他公司对比。"},{"en":"Information was then gathered on whether the email was opened and which job listings were clicked on by each user.","zh":"随后收集数据：邮件是否被打开、每位用户点击了哪些职位。"},{"en":"Participants in the diversity condition tended to click on job listings from companies with slightly higher diversity scores than those in the baseline condition.","zh":"多元条件下的参与者倾向于点击多元评分略高的公司的职位。"},{"en":"That is, participants seemed to be paying attention to information about diversity.","zh":"也就是说，参与者似乎在关注多元信息。"},{"en":"And using this, when deciding whether to click on the listing.","zh":"并在决定是否点击职位时使用这些信息。"},{"en":"And the team also found that participants were willing to look at listings with lower salaries, if they came from companies with a higher diversity score.","zh":"团队还发现，如果职位来自多元评分更高的公司，参与者愿意考虑薪水更低的职位。"}],"questions":[{"q":"When are job seekers willing to take jobs with lower salaries?","opts":["When companies share their information online","When their job search criteria are met fully","When companies embrace greater diversity","When they find job postings visually attractive"],"answer":2,"expl":"when companies are more diverse——公司更多元时。","signal":"首句时间状语从句","syn":[["when companies are more diverse","When companies embrace greater diversity（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did participants in the baseline condition see?","opts":["Emails in the normal format","Major companies in one location","All companies in the same sector","Various aspects of a company’s workforce"],"answer":0,"expl":"participants saw emails in the normal format, with no information on diversity——普通格式邮件。","signal":"实验条件对照处","syn":[["emails in the normal format","Emails in the normal format（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What makes job seekers accept listings with lower salaries?","opts":["Job security","Potential pay raises","Minimum base salary","Information about diversity"],"answer":3,"expl":"if they came from companies with a higher diversity score——多元评分信息。D 正确。","signal":"also found 递进处设题","syn":[["companies with a higher diversity score","Information about diversity（语义对应）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s1-8","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"科普","level":"四级","title":"Passage 3 · 狗狗和孩子：谁在配合谁","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 3（第1套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：新东方在线答案键 + 逐题回原文核对","sentences":[{"en":"A new study from Oregon State University found that dogs tend to match their behavior with the children in their family.","zh":"俄勒冈州立大学的一项新研究发现，狗往往会模仿家里孩子的行为。"},{"en":"The findings are important because there is a growing body of evidence that dogs can help children in many ways.","zh":"这些发现很重要，因为越来越多的证据表明狗能在很多方面帮助孩子。"},{"en":"These include helping with social development, increasing physical activity, managing anxiety or serving as a source of attachment in the face of changing family structures.","zh":"包括帮助社交发展、增加身体活动、缓解焦虑，或者在家庭结构变化时成为孩子的依恋对象。"},{"en":"Yet very little research has focused on how dogs perceive and socially engage with children.","zh":"然而，关于狗如何感知孩子、如何与孩子社交互动的研究还很少。"},{"en":"The great news is that this study suggests dogs are paying a lot of attention to the kids that they live with, said Monique Oudel, the lead author of the study.","zh":"\"好消息是，这项研究表明狗非常关注和它们一起生活的孩子，\"该研究的第一作者莫妮克·乌德尔说。"},{"en":"One interesting thing we have observed is that dogs are matching children's behaviour, but less frequently than what we have seen between dogs and adults.","zh":"\"我们观察到一个有趣的现象：狗会配合孩子的行为，但频率低于狗与成人之间的配合。"},{"en":"This suggests that while dogs may view children as social companions, there are also some differences that we need to understand better.","zh":"这表明，狗虽然可能把孩子视为社交伙伴，但其中还存在一些我们需要更好理解的差异。"},{"en":"While research has found dogs can have a lot of positive impacts on a child's life, there are also risks associated with a dog child relationship.","zh":"虽然研究发现狗能给孩子的生活带来很多积极影响，但狗与孩子的关系也有风险。"},{"en":"For example, other studies have found dogs are more likely to bite children versus adults.","zh":"例如，其他研究发现狗咬伤孩子的可能性大于咬伤成人。"},{"en":"We still have a lot to learn about the dog child relationship.","zh":"\"关于狗与孩子的关系，我们还有很多要学的，\"乌德尔说，\"但研究确实表明，孩子非常有能力训练狗。\""},{"en":"ELL said, but research does show that kids are very capable of training dogs.","zh":"研究人员说，但研究确实表明，孩子完全有能力训练狗。"}],"questions":[{"q":"How does the lead author describe the findings?","opts":["Positive","Original","Important","Surprising"],"answer":2,"expl":"The findings are important because...——她认为发现\"很重要\"。","signal":"引语评价词","syn":[["The findings are important","Important（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the passage say about dogs and children?","opts":["Dogs match their behavior with kids as much as with adults","Kids and adults alike find in dogs a source of attachment","Kids’ attitude to dogs is influenced by adults","Dogs can help kids in many ways"],"answer":3,"expl":"there is a growing body of evidence that dogs can help children in many ways——狗在很多方面帮助孩子。A 与原文相反（配合孩子不如配合成人频繁）。","signal":"because 证据句","syn":[["dogs can help children in many ways","Dogs can help kids in many ways（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the new study from Oregon State University find?","opts":["Dogs pay much attention to the kids they live with","Dogs view both adults and kids as social companions","Kids differ from adults in their behavior towards dogs","Kids need to be aware of the risks in playing with dogs"],"answer":0,"expl":"dogs are paying a lot of attention to the kids that they live with——狗很关注同住的孩子。","signal":"研究结论句","syn":[["paying a lot of attention to the kids","Dogs pay much attention to the kids they live with（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does research show kids are very capable of?","opts":["Understanding dogs","Training dogs","Taking care of dogs","Associating with dogs"],"answer":1,"expl":"kids are very capable of training dogs——孩子很会训练狗。","signal":"结尾句出答案","syn":[["very capable of training dogs","Training dogs（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s2-1","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"生活","level":"四级","title":"Conversation 1 · 停用手机支付：管住冲动消费","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 1（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：逐题回原文推导 + 新东方在线答案键交叉核对","sentences":[{"en":"I need to stop at the bank to withdraw some cash.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我得去银行取点现金。"},{"en":"Why not just pay with your phone?","spk":"W","zh":"W：为什么不直接用手机支付？"},{"en":"Well, actually, I've stopped using online payments for the past three months now.","spk":"M","zh":"M：其实，我已经三个月没用线上支付了。"},{"en":"Stopped paying online?","spk":"W","zh":"W：不用线上支付了？"},{"en":"Oh, you must be worried that online payments aren't secure.","spk":"W","zh":"W：哦，你一定是担心线上支付不安全。"},{"en":"No, they are safe.","spk":"M","zh":"M：不是，它挺安全的。"},{"en":"But paying online is too convenient and I spent too much money on things I didn't need.","spk":"M","zh":"M：但手机支付太方便了，我买了很多其实不需要的东西。"},{"en":"Oh, impulse purchases can be an issue for me too.","spk":"W","zh":"W：冲动消费对我来说也是个问题。"},{"en":"I've definitely bought clothes and shoes I didn't need because they were on sale, and paying with my phone was so easy.","spk":"W","zh":"W：我确实买过不需要的衣服鞋子，就因为打折，手机一付太容易了。"},{"en":"But I've found that if I review my spending every night, that keeps me from spending too much.","spk":"W","zh":"W：但我发现，如果每晚复盘一下自己的开销，就能管住手不花超。"},{"en":"I tried that strategy, but it just didn't work, because I'd be busy studying all day.","spk":"M","zh":"M：这招我试过，没用，因为我整天忙着学习。"},{"en":"Then, when I was tired and hungry, I'd use my phone to order food, like burgers and other junk, instead of going to the canteen, where I could get a healthier meal for half the price.","spk":"M","zh":"M：等我又累又饿时，就会用手机点外卖，汉堡之类的垃圾食品，而不是去食堂——那里半价就能吃上更健康的饭。"},{"en":"Well, what do you do now then?","spk":"W","zh":"W：那你现在怎么办？"},{"en":"It seems like you'd have the same problems with cash.","spk":"W","zh":"W：用现金的话，你好像也会有同样的问题。"},{"en":"I go to the bank once a week, and the rest of the time I keep my bank card at home, so I can't get more cash out.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我每周去一次银行，其余时间把银行卡放在家里，这样就取不出更多现金。"},{"en":"And I also have a notebook where I record my expenses.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我还用一个本子记录每笔开支。"},{"en":"But what prevents you from just going to the bank and getting more money, if you want to buy something?","spk":"W","zh":"W：可如果你想买什么，去银行多取点不就行了？"},{"en":"The first month I did withdraw extra cash twice, but I felt guilty about it.","spk":"M","zh":"M：第一个月我确实多取过两次，但很内疚。"},{"en":"And after that I refused to spend more than what I had budgeted, and by now it's just a habit.","spk":"M","zh":"M：从那以后我拒绝花超预算，到现在已经成了习惯。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why did the man stop using online payments?","opts":["He found it had caused him much inconvenience","It led him to spend more money than necessary","It was much less secure than paying with cash","He wanted to be less dependent on his phone"],"answer":1,"expl":"paying online is too convenient and I spent too much money on things I didn't need——它让他多花了冤枉钱。A 的不安全被原文明确否定（No, they are safe）。","signal":"问原因：But 后的真正理由","syn":[["I spent too much money on things I didn't need","It led him to spend more money than necessary（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the woman say is an issue for her?","opts":["Living beyond her means","Lack of budgeting strategies","Fashion addiction","Impulse purchasing"],"answer":3,"expl":"impulse purchases can be an issue for me too——冲动消费。打折买鞋只是例子，根子是冲动消费。","signal":"自我承认句 ... for me too","syn":[["impulse purchases can be an issue","Impulse purchasing（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What could the man get in the canteen instead of ordering junk food?","opts":["Eat healthier food with less money","Order food like burgers and chips","Avoid getting addicted to junk food","Pay either in cash or with his phone"],"answer":0,"expl":"a healthier meal for half the price——花一半的钱吃上更健康的饭。","signal":"对比结构 instead of","syn":[["a healthier meal for half the price","Eat healthier food with less money（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What has become a habit for the man now?","opts":["Making a shopping list","Sticking to his budget","Withdrawing cash only once a month","Thinking twice before buying something"],"answer":1,"expl":"I refused to spend more than what I had budgeted, and by now it's just a habit——坚持不超预算。","signal":"结尾句出答案","syn":[["refused to spend more than what I had budgeted","Sticking to his budget（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s2-2","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"生活","level":"四级","title":"Conversation 2 · 儿子报什么运动班，爸妈有分歧","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 2（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：逐题回原文推导 + 新东方在线答案键交叉核对","sentences":[{"en":"Please hear me out.","spk":"M","zh":"M：听我说完。"},{"en":"I don't want our son to spend his afternoons doing something he hates, even if it might prepare him for the future.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我不想让儿子把下午时间花在他讨厌的事情上，哪怕它可能对未来有好处。"},{"en":"What about getting him to join a sport, like soccer?","spk":"M","zh":"M：让他去参加个运动怎么样，比如足球？"},{"en":"From all the running and training, he could become quite athletic.","spk":"M","zh":"M：通过跑动和训练，他能变得很有运动细胞。"},{"en":"Not to mention the great physical benefits from exercising outside every day.","spk":"M","zh":"M：更别说每天在户外锻炼对身体的好处了。"},{"en":"I don't think he should be doing something so challenging with all his breathing issues.","spk":"W","zh":"W：他有呼吸道的老毛病，我不觉得他该做这么有挑战性的运动。"},{"en":"What about playing an indoor sport, like badminton?","spk":"W","zh":"W：室内运动怎么样，比如羽毛球？"},{"en":"The environment is easier to control, and he can still get a good workout, in addition to improving his hand eye coordination.","spk":"W","zh":"W：室内环境好控制，他也能得到充分锻炼，还能提高手眼协调。"},{"en":"Besides, I could teach him some of the basics from my time as a badminton player.","spk":"W","zh":"W：再说，我当年打过羽毛球，可以教他基本功。"},{"en":"Um, I'm thinking team sports should be the way to go.","spk":"M","zh":"M：呃，我觉得还是团队运动好。"},{"en":"There's nothing like playing as part of a unit to accomplish a goal like winning a game or even a championship.","spk":"M","zh":"M：没有什么比作为集体一员去赢球、甚至去争冠军更能锻炼人的了。"},{"en":"He could try basketball since many of the courts are indoors now and it's a sport that could help him understand team spirit while cooperating with others.","spk":"M","zh":"M：他可以试试篮球——现在很多球场都在室内，而且篮球能帮他在与别人合作中理解团队精神。"},{"en":"Maybe he could even join the school basketball team when he's ready.","spk":"M","zh":"M：等他准备好了，说不定还能进校队。"},{"en":"Oh, oh, what about volleyball?","spk":"W","zh":"W：哦，那排球呢？"},{"en":"It's a team sport and they often have mixed gender teams so he could socialize with both girls and boys.","spk":"W","zh":"W：排球也是团队运动，而且经常男女混合组队，他能同时和男生女生社交。"},{"en":"It's not as popular as some sports, which means he has better odds of possibly getting an athletic scholarship in the future.","spk":"W","zh":"W：它不像有些运动那么热门，这意味着他将来拿到体育奖学金的几率反而更大。"},{"en":"I also believe you were a beach volleyball athlete yourself not so long ago.","spk":"W","zh":"W：我记得你自己不久前还是沙滩排球运动员呢。"},{"en":"As I've said many times before, beach volleyball and indoor volleyball are completely different.","spk":"M","zh":"M：我说过多少次了，沙滩排球和室内排球完全是两码事。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why does the woman object to soccer for their son?","opts":["He does not enjoy any ball games","He has to prepare for the future","He has breathing problems","He is not up to anything challenging"],"answer":2,"expl":"with all his breathing issues——孩子有呼吸道问题，不适合高强度户外运动。","signal":"反对理由句 I don't think","syn":[["all his breathing issues","He has breathing problems（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Which team sport does the man suggest for the boy?","opts":["Soccer","Badminton","V olleyball","Basketball"],"answer":3,"expl":"He could try basketball ... help him understand team spirit while cooperating with others——爸爸推荐篮球。","signal":"提议句 He could try","syn":[["try basketball","Basketball（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the woman say about playing volleyball?","opts":["The possibilities of joining the school sports team","The opportunities of winning some championships","The chances of getting an athletic scholarship later on","The odds of becoming a professional sportsman someday"],"answer":2,"expl":"better odds of possibly getting an athletic scholarship in the future——将来拿体育奖学金的机会更大。","signal":"比较级 better odds 处设题","syn":[["better odds of possibly getting an athletic scholarship","The chances of getting an athletic scholarship later on（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man say about beach volleyball?","opts":["It differs entirely from indoor volleyball","It appeals to both schoolgirls and schoolboys","It is less popular than indoor sports in the country","It is completely different from other outdoor games"],"answer":0,"expl":"beach volleyball and indoor volleyball are completely different——沙滩排球和室内排球完全不同。","signal":"引语强调句","syn":[["are completely different","It differs entirely from indoor volleyball（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s2-3","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"News Report 1 · 能源账单暴涨的美国家庭","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 1（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：逐题回原文推导 + 新东方在线答案键交叉核对","sentences":[{"en":"Across the U.S., families are looking to the winter with fear, as energy costs soar.","zh":"在全美各地，随着能源成本飙升，许多家庭正怀着恐惧望向这个冬天。"},{"en":"A number of factors are creating a bad situation.","zh":"多个因素正在造成糟糕的局面。"},{"en":"Global energy consumption is up, but supplies have been reduced.","zh":"全球能源消费上升，但供应减少了。"},{"en":"The Energy Department projects heating bills will jump 28 percent this winter, for those who rely on natural gas.","zh":"能源部预测，今冬依赖天然气的家庭取暖账单将上涨28%。"},{"en":"Natural gas is used by nearly half of U.S. households for heat.","zh":"美国近一半家庭用天然气取暖。"},{"en":"Heating oil is projected to be 27 percent higher and electricity 10 percent higher.","zh":"取暖油预计上涨27%，电价上涨10%。"},{"en":"That comes against inflation rates that accelerated last month, with consumer prices growing 6.6%.","zh":"与此同时，上月通胀加速，消费品价格上涨6.6%。"},{"en":"That's the fastest pace in four decades.","zh":"这是四十年来最快的增速。"},{"en":"The pain will be especially acute in parts of the country that heavily rely on heating oil to keep homes warm.","zh":"对严重依赖取暖油给房屋供暖的地区，痛苦将尤其剧烈。"},{"en":"It's projected to cost more than $2,300 to heat a typical home with heating oil this winter.","zh":"预计今冬用取暖油给一户典型住宅供暖要花超过2300美元。"},{"en":"Last month, the federal government added $1 billion in funding to Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program, bringing the total to $4.8 billion.","zh":"上个月，联邦政府为\"低收入家庭能源援助计划\"增拨10亿美元，使总额达到48亿。"},{"en":"But that represents a reduction from last year's energy assistance package of over $8 billion.","zh":"但这比去年超过80亿美元的能源援助包有所减少。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do American families fear about the coming winter?","opts":["They will see a 27% higher price to buy natural gas","They will have insufficient heating oil to keep warm","They will have a costly bill to pay to heat their homes","They will experience the coldest winter in four decades"],"answer":2,"expl":"heating bills will jump 28 percent——取暖账单要暴涨，即要为取暖付出高昂账单。A 偷换：27%是取暖油涨幅且是\"账单\"不是\"买气价格\"；B 供应不足与 D 四十年最冷冬天（四十年指的是通胀增速）都是错位。","signal":"首句 fear 处设题","syn":[["heating bills will jump 28 percent","a costly bill to pay to heat their homes（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did the federal government do last month?","opts":["Provided additional funding to Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program","Assured U.S. citizens of an increase in energy supplies by the end of this year","Predicted a 10% jump in heating bills for most U.S. households this winter","Decided on this year’s energy assistance package of $8 billion in total"],"answer":0,"expl":"added $1 billion in funding to Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program——给该计划追加拨款。","signal":"机构动作句","syn":[["added $1 billion in funding to ... Program","Provided additional funding to Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s2-4","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"科普","level":"四级","title":"News Report 2 · 你觉得自己吃得健康吗？多半是错觉","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 2（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：逐题回原文推导 + 新东方在线答案键交叉核对","sentences":[{"en":"Many Americans think they make healthy food choices, but they may be viewing their diet too optimistically.","zh":"许多美国人认为自己饮食健康，但他们可能把吃得太乐观了。"},{"en":"That's the main finding of a new study by researchers at the U.S. Department of Agriculture in Stoneville, Mississippi.","zh":"这是密西西比州斯通维尔农业部研究人员一项新研究的主要发现。"},{"en":"The study aimed to identify disconnects between how healthily Americans think they eat and how they actually do.","zh":"该研究旨在找出\"美国人自认为吃得有多健康\"与\"实际吃得有多健康\"之间的落差。"},{"en":"For the study, the researchers asked participants to rate their diet as excellent, very good, good, fair, or poor.","zh":"研究中，研究人员请参与者给自己的饮食评级：极好、很好、好、一般或差。"},{"en":"Folks also completed 24 hour food questionnaires.","zh":"参与者还填写了24小时饮食问卷。"},{"en":"Then, the researchers compared answers to see how well responses to the two exercises matched up.","zh":"然后，研究人员比对答案，看两者匹配程度。"},{"en":"Of more than 9,700 people, roughly 85 percent were off base when asked to rate the quality of their diet, and almost all overestimated how healthy it was.","zh":"在9700多人中，约85%的人在给饮食质量评级时走了样，而且几乎全部高估了健康程度。"},{"en":"Those who rated their diet as poor tended to be far more accurate.","zh":"那些给自己评\"差\"的人反而准确得多。"},{"en":"Their rating match that of the researchers more than nine times out of ten.","zh":"他们的评级十有八九与研究人员的评估一致。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What is the main finding of the new study?","opts":["They care less about their diet now than before","They may lack adequate knowledge of healthy food","They may hold too optimistic a view about their diet","They pay insufficient attention to their choice of food"],"answer":2,"expl":"they may be viewing their diet too optimistically——对自己的饮食过于乐观。","signal":"首句 main finding","syn":[["viewing their diet too optimistically","hold too optimistic a view about their diet（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Who tended to be more accurate in rating their diet?","opts":["Those who finished 24-hour food questionnaires","Those who fully understood the rating scale","Those who cared about food quality","Those who rated their diet as poor"],"answer":3,"expl":"Those who rated their diet as poor tended to be far more accurate——自评\"差\"的人最准。","signal":"对比处出答案","syn":[["rated their diet as poor","Those who rated their diet as poor（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s2-5","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"News Report 3 · 军营旁的20英尺深井大象营救","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 3（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：逐题回原文推导 + 新东方在线答案键交叉核对","sentences":[{"en":"It was a heartwarming moment that dozens of Indian rescuers rallied together to use a crane in order to save an elephant trapped at the bottom of a twenty foot well.","zh":"几十名印度救援人员齐心协力，用一台起重机救出了被困在20英尺深井底的大象——这是暖心的一幕。"},{"en":"The massive rescue effort took place last week close to an army camp.","zh":"这场大规模营救发生在上周一处军营附近。"},{"en":"The elephant wandered out of the jungle and fell into the well.","zh":"大象从丛林里走出来，掉进了井里。"},{"en":"The army officers heard a noise coming from the well and realized an elephant was trapped deep inside.","zh":"军官们听到井里传来响声，意识到有大象被困在深处。"},{"en":"The officers then threw in some food for the creature and called the local forest department for help.","zh":"军官们随后往井里投了些食物，并打电话向当地林业部门求助。"},{"en":"Video of the rescue operation shows how the team used a crane to lift up the huge animal out of the well and onto the back of a truck.","zh":"救援视频显示，团队用起重机把这头巨兽从井里吊起，放到一辆卡车的后斗上。"},{"en":"It was then taken to an examining room for evaluation of any injuries.","zh":"随后它被送到检查室，评估有没有受伤。"},{"en":"The elephant was kept under close supervision for a few days before it was successfully released back into the wild.","zh":"大象被严密看护了几天，然后被成功放归野外。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What happened close to an army camp last week?","opts":["They experienced a heartbreaking moment","They gathered together to rescue an elephant","They heard a noise from the bottom of a well","They found an elephant wandering around a well"],"answer":1,"expl":"dozens of Indian rescuers rallied together to ... save an elephant——众人协力救大象。C、D 只是过程细节，不是主事件。","signal":"首句主事件","syn":[["rallied together to ... save an elephant","They gathered together to rescue an elephant（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why did the army officers contact the local forest department?","opts":["To borrow their crane","To ask them for help","To report the strange noise","To get food for the elephant"],"answer":1,"expl":"called the local forest department for help——求援。","signal":"动作目的 for help","syn":[["called the local forest department for help","To ask them for help（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the report say about the elephant in the end?","opts":["The elephant was able to return to the jungle","The army officers were examined for injuries","The army officers were rewarded for their rescue efforts","The elephant was given medical treatment for many days"],"answer":0,"expl":"successfully released back into the wild——成功放归野外。","signal":"结尾句出答案","syn":[["released back into the wild","The elephant was able to return to the jungle（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s2-6","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"科普","level":"四级","title":"Passage 1 · 火箭发射的环保账","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 1（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：逐题回原文推导 + 新东方在线答案键交叉核对","sentences":[{"en":"Liftoff is usually the most environmentally harmful stage of any space mission, with vast quantities of fuel burnt up in a matter of minutes.","zh":"发射升空通常是所有太空任务中对环境危害最大的阶段，大量燃料在几分钟内烧掉。"},{"en":"For instance, SpaceX's Falcon 9 gets through 112 tons of refined fuel, emitting about 336 tons of CO2.","zh":"例如，SpaceX的猎鹰9号要消耗112吨精炼燃料，排放约336吨二氧化碳。"},{"en":"This is the equivalent produced by your average car driving almost 70 times around the world, as well as greenhouse gases.","zh":"这相当于一辆普通汽车绕地球行驶近70圈所产生的排放，还有温室气体。"},{"en":"Rocket engines emit particles that destroy ozone.","zh":"火箭发动机会排放破坏臭氧层的颗粒物。"},{"en":"These issues are growing more pressing with the emergence of commercial spaceflight.","zh":"随着商业航天兴起，这些问题越来越紧迫。"},{"en":"There were 114 space launches in 2020, but there may be up to 1,000 per year in future.","zh":"2020年有114次太空发射，未来可能达到每年多达1000次。"},{"en":"Sustainable fuels are the top priority to enable greener space travel.","zh":"可持续燃料是实现更环保太空飞行的头等大事。"},{"en":"Current spacecraft use a variety of fuels, but most are based on fossil fuels.","zh":"目前的航天器使用多种燃料，但大多基于化石燃料。"},{"en":"One potentially greener option is liquid hydrogen and oxygen.","zh":"一个潜在更环保的选项是液氢液氧。"},{"en":"Hydrogen can be obtained sustainably by using solar power to break water down into oxygen and hydrogen.","zh":"氢可以可持续地获得：用太阳能把水分解成氧和氢。"},{"en":"Reusable rockets can cut down on some of the waste associated with spaceflight.","zh":"可重复使用的火箭能减少航天的一些浪费。"},{"en":"Traditionally, boosters, fuel tanks, and other components are treated as expendable.","zh":"传统上，助推器、燃料箱等部件被视为一次性消耗品。"},{"en":"But guiding them back to Earth in a controlled manner opens new possibilities.","zh":"但以可控方式把它们引导回地球，打开了新的可能。"},{"en":"Most components from the Falcon 9 can be reused up to 100 times.","zh":"猎鹰9号的大多数部件可重复使用多达100次。"},{"en":"Truly environmentally friendly space travel is still some way off.","zh":"真正环保的太空旅行仍有一段路要走。"},{"en":"But we already have many of the technologies needed to start limiting its impact on our planet.","zh":"但我们已经拥有开始限制其对我们地球影响的许多技术。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the passage say about the liftoff stage of space missions?","opts":["It usually requires years of preparations","It does a lot of harm to the environment","It often burns over three hundred tonnes of refined fuel","It proves to be the most complicated stage of space missions"],"answer":1,"expl":"the most environmentally harmful stage——对环境危害最大的阶段。C 数字偷换：是112吨精炼燃料、336吨CO2。","signal":"首句判断","syn":[["the most environmentally harmful stage","It does a lot of harm to the environment（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What happens to boosters and fuel tanks traditionally?","opts":["They are burnt up in outer space","They are guided back to Earth","They are reused up to 100 times","They are treated as expendable"],"answer":3,"expl":"are treated as expendable——被视为一次性消耗品。","signal":"Traditionally 对比信号","syn":[["treated as expendable","They are treated as expendable（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do we already have, according to the passage?","opts":["New technologies for bringing back space vehicles for recycling","The technology for meeting the needs of commercial space travel","Many of the technologies to limit the impact of space travel on Earth","The technology for effectively protecting ozone from being destroyed"],"answer":2,"expl":"we already have many of the technologies needed to start limiting its impact on our planet——限制航天对地球影响的技术。","signal":"结尾 But 转折后","syn":[["many of the technologies needed to start limiting its impact on our planet","Many of the technologies to limit the impact of space travel on Earth（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s2-7","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"科普","level":"四级","title":"Passage 2 · 养宠物如何帮助孩子成长","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 2（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：逐题回原文推导 + 新东方在线答案键交叉核对","sentences":[{"en":"Helping to look after a pet can facilitate numerous aspects of a child's emotional development.","zh":"帮忙照顾宠物能促进孩子情绪发展的许多方面。"},{"en":"Research shows that reading to a loyal and nonjudgmental companion, such as a dog or cat, can encourage reluctant readers to read aloud, which will in turn boost their self confidence.","zh":"研究表明，向狗或猫这样忠诚、不带评判的伙伴朗读，能鼓励不情愿的朗读者开口读出声，从而增强他们的自信。"},{"en":"Having a companion to talk to about their feelings can also help children feel secure and develop communication skills.","zh":"有一个可以倾诉感受的伙伴，也能帮助孩子获得安全感、发展沟通能力。"},{"en":"A household pet can also cultivate a child's sense of responsibility, as their parent explains the necessary processes of keeping their pet happy and healthy.","zh":"家养宠物还能培养孩子的责任感——父母讲解让宠物保持快乐健康所需的各项事宜。"},{"en":"As a child matures, they can then take on more of the daily responsibilities, boosting their sense of independence.","zh":"随着孩子长大，他们可以承担更多日常事务，增强独立感。"},{"en":"Pets also provide a fantastic subject for research and learning.","zh":"宠物也是研究和学习的绝佳题材。"},{"en":"Parents can encourage their child to research their favorite pets at the library or during a supervised internet search.","zh":"父母可以鼓励孩子在图书馆或在受监督的上网检索中研究自己最喜欢的宠物。"},{"en":"Taking children along to the pet shop to buy food and supplies will support their cognitive development as their passion for learning flourishes.","zh":"带孩子一起去宠物店买食物和用品，能在他们的学习热情蓬勃生长时支持认知发展。"},{"en":"A child's physical development can benefit greatly from taking pets for walks in the fresh air.","zh":"在新鲜空气中遛狗能大大促进孩子的身体发育。"},{"en":"Even their fine motor skills can be utilized in taking care of a beloved animal.","zh":"连精细动作技能都能在照顾心爱动物时得到运用。"},{"en":"When responsibilities are well paced and communicated, a child can benefit greatly from involvement in bringing up a happy and healthy pet.","zh":"当责任安排得当、沟通充分时，孩子能从参与养育一只快乐健康的宠物中获益良多。"},{"en":"And of course, if a child doesn't have a pet in their own household, they can still benefit from all of the above when visiting a friend who does.","zh":"当然，如果孩子自己家没有宠物，去拜访养宠物的朋友时，同样能获得上述所有益处。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What can reading to a pet do for children according to the research?","opts":["It can help unskilled readers feel more secure","It can encourage reluctant readers to read aloud","It can strengthen children’s confidence in others","It can boost children’s interest in communication"],"answer":1,"expl":"can encourage reluctant readers to read aloud——让不愿朗读的孩子开口读。","signal":"Research shows 证据句","syn":[["encourage reluctant readers to read aloud","It can encourage reluctant readers to read aloud（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How can parents support children's research and learning with pets?","opts":["By motivating children to find out about their favourite pets","By taking children to the library to borrow books on animals","By allowing children to surf the internet about pets by themselves","By showing children how to acquire knowledge about healthy pets"],"answer":0,"expl":"encourage their child to research their favorite pets at the library or during a supervised internet search——激励孩子去探究自己最喜欢的宠物。C 缺了\"受监督\"这层限定。","signal":"方式列举处","syn":[["encourage their child to research their favorite pets","By motivating children to find out about their favourite pets（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How can a child without a pet at home still benefit?","opts":["By learning that raising pets can do much good","By watching how healthy pets are brought up","By hearing about their peers’ passion for pets","By visiting friends who have household pets"],"answer":3,"expl":"when visiting a friend who does——拜访养宠物的朋友。","signal":"结尾句出答案","syn":[["visiting a friend who does","By visiting friends who have household pets（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"cet2412s2-8","group":"2024年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"社会","level":"四级","title":"Passage 3 · 俄亥俄州新法案：把大学账单寄给准大学生","material":"2024年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 3（第2套）","source":"原文：ListenEase（listenease.online 真题字幕，含说话人标记）；题目：真题PDF；答案：逐题回原文推导 + 新东方在线答案键交叉核对","sentences":[{"en":"A new bill in the Ohio legislature would require state public colleges and universities to send prospective students a packet of information.","zh":"俄亥俄州立法机构的一项新法案将要求州立公立高校向准学生寄送一包信息。"},{"en":"This would include costs of college grants and scholarships.","zh":"其中包括大学助学金和奖学金的费用信息。"},{"en":"It would also include expected monthly loan payments and projected salary after college.","zh":"还将包括预期的每月还贷额和大学毕业后的预期薪资。"},{"en":"State Representative Adam Loinbo is one of the two legislators who proposed the bill.","zh":"州众议员亚当·洛伊恩博是提出该法案的两名议员之一。"},{"en":"He said it would give prospective students more information about what to expect once they graduate.","zh":"他说，这会让准学生更清楚毕业后能期待什么。"},{"en":"Putting that information in front of them will give them the best opportunity to match their skills and their dreams to what our schools can provide, said Loinbo.","zh":"洛伊恩博说：\"把这些信息放到他们面前，会给他们最好的机会，把自己的技能和梦想与学校所能提供的相匹配。\""},{"en":"He notes that the state can only regulate public institutions in this way, but he hopes private institutions in Ohio follow the lead of the state and post similar information.","zh":"他指出，州里只能以这种方式监管公立院校，但他希望俄亥俄的私立院校效仿州政府，发布类似信息。"},{"en":"He believes giving out this information will help Ohio's colleges and universities to be more competitive.","zh":"他相信，发布这些信息将帮助俄亥俄的高校更有竞争力。"},{"en":"The information will highlight what a great value they have for their very reasonable cost.","zh":"这些信息将凸显他们\"价格合理、物超所值\"。"},{"en":"Ohio's schools are already competitive.","zh":"俄亥俄的学校本来就很有竞争力。"},{"en":"The state attracts more undergraduate students than it sends to colleges out of state.","zh":"该州吸引来的本科生数量多于去外州上大学的本地学生。"},{"en":"Many colleges and universities currently provide similar information on their websites.","zh":"目前许多高校已在网站上提供类似信息。"},{"en":"This includes tuition, fees, graduation rates, and more.","zh":"包括学费、杂费、毕业率等等。"},{"en":"But students need to search for the information.","zh":"但学生需要自己去搜。"},{"en":"This bill would require the universities and colleges to send a packet directly to students.","zh":"该法案将要求高校把信息包直接寄给学生。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What would the new bill require state public colleges to do?","opts":["Send would-be students a packet of information","Update regularly all information on their websites","Inform prospective students of their yearly enrollment","Answer questions raised by applicants and their parents"],"answer":0,"expl":"send prospective students a packet of information——寄信息包给准学生。","signal":"首句主旨","syn":[["send prospective students a packet of information","Send would-be students a packet of information（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What can the state do with the bill, according to Loinbo?","opts":["Oversee private institutions directly","Follow other states’ example","Supervise all schools consistently","Regulate public institutions by law"],"answer":3,"expl":"the state can only regulate public institutions in this way——依法监管公立院校。","signal":"限定词 only 处设题","syn":[["regulate public institutions","Regulate public institutions by law（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does Loinbo think of Ohio's colleges?","opts":["They are resourceful","They are competitive","They provide the best opportunity to realize one’s dream","They appeal most to students from other states in the U.S"],"answer":1,"expl":"Ohio's schools are already competitive——本就很有竞争力。","signal":"评价词定位","syn":[["already competitive","They are competitive（同源词）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is the problem with the information colleges currently provide?","opts":["Some students waste much time surfing the net","Students may need to visit too many websites","Students have to search for the information","Some students may lack adequate access"],"answer":2,"expl":"But students need to search for the information——学生得自己去搜。","signal":"But 转折指出痛点","syn":[["students need to search for the information","Students have to search for the information（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506a-1","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"人物故事","level":"四级","title":"玉米小子塔里克","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 1（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Everything changed for seven-year-old Tariq when he slapped some butter on an ear of corn.","zh":"七岁的塔里克的一切都改变了。他往耳朵上抹了些黄油。玉米。"},{"en":"He knew it tasted good, but butter made it better.","zh":"他知道它味道不错，但黄油却让他……最好是这样。"},{"en":"His passion for produce got him a position as South Dakota's official corn ambassador.","zh":"他对农产品的热情为他赢得了一份工作。担任南达科他州官方玉米大使。"},{"en":"Tariq's profession of love for his favorite vegetable earned him the name The Corn Kid.","zh":"塔里克向他最喜欢的蔬菜表达了爱意他因此得名“玉米小子”。"},{"en":"This was after his online interview attracted millions of views and was made into a song.","zh":"此前，他的网络采访吸引了数百万观众。浏览量很高，并被改编成了一首歌。"},{"en":"South Dakota is one of the top corn producers in America.","zh":"南达科他州是玉米产量最高的州之一。美国生产商。"},{"en":"The corn provides nourishment across the globe.","zh":"玉米为全球各地提供营养。"},{"en":"Tariq said not everyone has to like corn, but everyone should definitely try it, especially with butter.","zh":"塔里克说，不是每个人都必须喜欢玉米。但每个人都应该尝试一下，尤其是对于……黄油。"},{"en":"Tariq and his family were invited to South Dakota to attend the honorary ceremony at the state's Corn Palace.","zh":"塔里克和他的家人受邀前往南方达科塔将出席在……举行的荣誉仪式。州立玉米宫。"},{"en":"Officials wanted to highlight South Dakota's two largest industries, tourism and agriculture.","zh":"官员们希望重点介绍南达科他州最大的两个城市。工业、旅游业和农业。"},{"en":"Tariq couldn't believe his eyes when he saw the palace made of corn.","zh":"塔里克简直不敢相信自己的眼睛。用玉米建造的宫殿。"}],"questions":[{"q":"How did Tariq make corn taste better?","opts":["By slapping some butter on it","By enhancing its nourishment","By growing it in South Dakota","By cooking it in vegetable oil"],"answer":0,"expl":"新闻开头「Everything changed...when he slapped some butter on an ear of corn」——slap butter on 原词复现，选「抹黄油」。","signal":"新闻首句即考点","syn":[["slapped some butter on","By slapping some butter on it（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why were Tariq and his family invited to South Dakota?","opts":["To introduce their corn to tourists","To attend an honorary ceremony","To share experience with other corn growers","To exhibit their corn at the state’s Corn Palace"],"answer":1,"expl":"「invited to South Dakota to attend the honorary ceremony」——attend 原词复现；干扰项「介绍玉米给游客」是把 officials 想突出旅游业的细节张冠李戴。","signal":"invited to... 定位","syn":[["attend the honorary ceremony","To attend an honorary ceremony（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506a-2","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"法治新闻","level":"四级","title":"邮箱盗窃案逮捕","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 2（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Two arrests were announced Thursday.","zh":"周四宣布了两起逮捕事件。"},{"en":"The arrests were in connection with a string of mail thefts from U.S. Post Service's collection boxes in Marion County and for the possession of a stolen postal key, according to the Department of Justice.","zh":"这些逮捕行动与一系列案件有关。美国邮政服务邮件盗窃案马里恩县及其他地区的捐款箱据称，他持有被盗的邮政钥匙。司法部。"},{"en":"Jordan Jacks and Tarrod Goodman, both 23, were arrested after evidence gathered in an investigation showed the pair stole mail on multiple occasions using a postal key, according to a news release.","zh":"乔丹·杰克斯和塔罗德·古德曼，两人均为23岁，调查中收集到的证据显示，该男子已被逮捕。两人曾多次利用……盗窃邮件。根据新闻稿，这是一把邮政钥匙。"},{"en":"Jacks and Goodman stole mail for around four months.","zh":"杰克斯和古德曼偷邮件大约四次。几个月。"},{"en":"Investigators reviewed videos of the collection boxes.","zh":"调查人员查看了募捐箱的视频。"},{"en":"The video showed the two men loading the stolen mail into Jacks' vehicle.","zh":"视频显示两名男子正在装载……被盗邮件被放入杰克的车里。"},{"en":"Investigators were also able to recover the key that was used to open the collection boxes.","zh":"调查人员还找回了钥匙。这是用来打开捐款箱的。"},{"en":"Jacks and Goodman each face up to five years in federal prison in the mail thefts and up to 10 years for possession of the postal key.","zh":"杰克斯和古德曼各自最多要面对五名对手。因邮件盗窃罪被判处多年联邦监狱监禁持有罪名最高可判处 10 年监禁邮政钥匙。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What did Jordan Jacks and Tarrod Goodman do, according to a news release?","opts":["Stole mail several times","Forged postal keys illegally","Attacked postmen on multiple occasions","Broke a number of postal collection boxes"],"answer":0,"expl":"「the pair stole mail on multiple occasions」——multiple occasions 同义替换 several times。","signal":"according to a news release","syn":[["on multiple occasions","several times（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do Jordan Jacks and Tarrod Goodman face?","opts":["A sentence for life","Loss of all their possessions","Twenty-three years’ hard labor","Up to fifteen years in prison"],"answer":3,"expl":"「up to five years in federal prison...and up to 10 years for possession of the postal key」——两项合并最长 15 年，选 up to fifteen years。","signal":"数字题：5+10","syn":[["up to five years...up to 10 years","Up to fifteen years in prison（数字相加）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506a-3","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"环保科技","level":"四级","title":"快时尚能否可持续","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 3（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Can fast fashion be sustainable?","zh":"快时尚可以做到可持续吗？"},{"en":"Researchers think yes.","zh":"研究人员认为答案是肯定的。"},{"en":"Identifying why the fast fashion business model creates waste and determining whether regulators can establish incentives for consumers and manufacturers are steps to reduce waste.","zh":"探究快时尚商业模式为何会造成浪费以及确定监管机构是否可以制定激励措施对消费者和制造商而言，减少成本的措施有很多。浪费。"},{"en":"Recently, the clothing industry has come under attack for creating a waste problem with serious environmental consequences.","zh":"近来，服装行业遭受了猛烈抨击。造成严重的环境废物问题结果。"},{"en":"In the absence of environmentally and economically feasible recycling options, fast fashion manufacturers pump out low -quality clothes produced in high volumes that are worn only a few times and then discarded.","zh":"在缺乏环境和经济上可行的方案的情况下回收选项，快时尚制造商大量生产低价产品大批量生产的高品质服装只穿过几次就丢弃了。"},{"en":"The researchers put forth policy contributions ranging from sustainable disposal of leftover stock to production tax to incentivize both manufacturers and consumers to be more waste-conscious.","zh":"研究人员提出了一系列政策建议，包括：将剩余库存可持续处置用于生产税激励制造商和消费者都这样做更注重浪费。"},{"en":"In order to devise effective policies to curb the environmental impact of the clothing industry, it is important to identify the source of the problem in the supply chain.","zh":"为了制定有效的政策来遏制服装行业对环境的影响，它确定来源很重要供应链出现问题。"},{"en":"Manufacturers, consumers, and regulatory bodies can then take an informed approach to recognize the environmental impact of fast fashion and to design an ecosystem to reduce waste, incentivize innovation, and create new business models to manage waste.","zh":"制造商、消费者和监管机构随后可以采取以知情的方式认识环境影响快时尚以及设计一个生态系统减少浪费、激励创新、创造新事物废物管理的商业模式。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why has the clothing industry come under attack?","opts":["It escapes regulation and misleads consumers","It ignores economically feasible recycling options","It creates waste and severely impacts the environment","It produces clothes affordable only to a tiny minority"],"answer":2,"expl":"「creating a waste problem with serious environmental consequences」——C 是原句压缩；under attack 原词复现。","signal":"have come under attack","syn":[["serious environmental consequences","severely impacts the environment（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why do the researchers put forth such policies as production tax?","opts":["To cut consumers’ expenses in buying quality clothes","To enable the whole fast-fashion industry to be sustainable","To incentivize manufacturers to be more consumer-friendly","To urge manufacturers and consumers to reduce waste"],"answer":3,"expl":"「to incentivize both manufacturers and consumers to be more waste-conscious」——incentivize 同义替换 urge。","signal":"incentivize 信号词","syn":[["incentivize...to be more waste-conscious","To urge manufacturers and consumers to reduce waste（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What should be done first to eliminate the harm caused by the clothing industry?","opts":["Recognizing the impact on consumers","Identifying the source of the problem","Abandoning the current business model","Establishing powerful regulatory bodies"],"answer":1,"expl":"「it is important to identify the source of the problem in the supply chain」——first/important 对应 identify the source。","signal":"it is important to","syn":[["identify the source of the problem","Identifying the source of the problem（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506a-4","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"城市生活","level":"四级","title":"高峰期通勤吐槽","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 1（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Hey Mary, you seem to be very much annoyed.","zh":"嘿，玛丽，你看起来很……恼火。"},{"en":"What happened?","zh":"发生了什么？"},{"en":"Rush hour in this city is killing me.","zh":"这座城市的交通高峰期简直要了我的命。"},{"en":"Ah yes, rush hour is terrible, especially in the morning between eight and nine.","zh":"啊，是的，高峰时段太糟糕了，尤其是在……早上八点到九点之间。"},{"en":"But what else can you expect in a city this big?","zh":"但是，你还能期待什么呢？这么大的城市？"},{"en":"Well, I think the local government could help improve things.","zh":"我认为地方政府可以提供帮助。改进现状。"},{"en":"I mean, getting rid of rush hour may be impossible, but it could be made more tolerable, don't you think?","zh":"我的意思是，取消高峰时段可能这或许不可能，但可以做得更好。还能接受，你不觉得吗？"},{"en":"Um, but I'm not sure how.","zh":"嗯，但我不太确定该怎么做。"},{"en":"Well, for example, the subway system could have air conditioning.","zh":"例如，地铁系统可能……空调。"},{"en":"I know many cities in the world have air conditioning in their subway, so why can't we?","zh":"我知道世界上有很多城市他们的地铁里有空调，为什么不能有呢？我们？"},{"en":"It gets so hot in the summer, I can hardly breathe down there.","zh":"夏天太热了，我下面几乎喘不过气来。"},{"en":"And add to that the rush hour crowds with strangers packed close together in the subway carriages.","zh":"再加上高峰时段的拥挤人群。地铁里挤满了陌生人马车。"},{"en":"The whole thing is just horrible.","zh":"整件事简直太糟糕了。"},{"en":"Ah yes, you are completely right.","zh":"啊，是的，您完全正确。"},{"en":"The trains here are too old.","zh":"这里的火车太老旧了。"},{"en":"The government should definitely invest in new ones with air conditioning.","zh":"政府绝对应该投资建设新的配有空调。"},{"en":"I guess I'm fortunate I take the bus instead.","zh":"我想我坐公交车出行真是太幸运了。反而。"},{"en":"Oh, that's much better.","zh":"哦，这样好多了。"},{"en":"Yeah, it's more convenient.","zh":"是的，这样更方便。"},{"en":"Bus number 36 goes straight from my house to the office.","zh":"36路公交车从我家直达。去办公室。"},{"en":"It's a 30 minute ride and I don't have to make any changes.","zh":"车程30分钟，我不需要需要做出任何更改。"},{"en":"That sounds nice.","zh":"听起来不错。"},{"en":"I tell you, my current commute is killing me.","zh":"我跟你说，我现在的通勤简直要命。我。"},{"en":"Maybe I should move closer to the office.","zh":"或许我应该搬到离办公室更近的地方。"},{"en":"Well, I know a great housing agent.","zh":"我认识一位很棒的房屋中介。"},{"en":"I found the flat I'm living in now through him and I love it.","zh":"我找到了我现在住的公寓。通过他，我很喜欢。"},{"en":"Hmm, could you send me his number please?","zh":"嗯，你能把他的电话号码发给我吗？"},{"en":"Sure thing.","zh":"当然可以。"},{"en":"Just tell him exactly what you are looking for and I'm sure he will find something good.","zh":"直接告诉他你想要什么就行了。我相信他一定能找到办法。好的。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why is the woman complaining?","opts":["The city’s rush-hour traffic is intolerable","She cannot avoid rush-hour traffic","The local government is inefficient","The city is too big to move around easily"],"answer":0,"expl":"「Rush hour in this city is killing me」——killing me 同义替换 intolerable。","signal":"转折前首句观点","syn":[["is killing me","is intolerable（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the woman suggest doing?","opts":["Upgrading subway carriages","Increasing the number of bus routes","Air conditioning the city’s subway","Learning from other big cities"],"answer":2,"expl":"「the subway system could have air conditioning」——could 表建议；干扰项「升级车厢」偷换成 trains too old，那是男士的话。","signal":"could 表建议","syn":[["subway system could have air conditioning","Air conditioning the city's subway（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do we learn about the man from the conversation?","opts":["He suffers from rush-hour crowding too","He is fortunate to live very near to work","He takes a half-hour bus ride to work","He is going to move closer to his office"],"answer":2,"expl":"「I guess I'm fortunate I take the bus...It's a 30 minute ride」——fortunate 幸运 + 30 分钟即 half-hour。","signal":"I guess 自我评价","syn":[["30 minute ride","half-hour bus ride（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the woman ask the man to do at the end of the conversation?","opts":["Recommend to her a good house near his office","Send her his housing agent’s telephone number","Tell her exactly what kind of property to look for","Make sure the agent finds something good for her"],"answer":1,"expl":"「could you send me his number please?」——send his number 即把中介电话发给她。","signal":"结尾请求","syn":[["send me his number","Send her housing agent's telephone number（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506a-5","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"人际关系","level":"四级","title":"约翰尼的疤痕手术","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 2（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Did you hear about Johnny?","zh":"你听说过约翰尼的事吗？"},{"en":"No, why?","zh":"不，为什么？"},{"en":"Is he okay?","zh":"他没事吧？"},{"en":"He had some plastic surgery done.","zh":"他做过整形手术。"},{"en":"What?","zh":"什么？"},{"en":"Why?","zh":"为什么？"},{"en":"Do you remember?","zh":"你是否记得？"},{"en":"He had a scar on his face.","zh":"他脸上有一道疤痕。"},{"en":"Yes, of course.","zh":"是的当然。"},{"en":"He always had that.","zh":"他一直都有那种感觉。"},{"en":"I've known him since primary school and I always remember him having that on his cheek.","zh":"我从小学就认识他了，而且我一直记得他脸颊上的那个疤。"},{"en":"Well, he had it fixed.","zh":"他已经修好了。"},{"en":"Fixed?","zh":"固定的？"},{"en":"What do you mean?","zh":"你是什​​么意思？"},{"en":"You can't fix a scar.","zh":"疤痕无法修复。"},{"en":"You know what I mean.","zh":"你知道我的意思。"},{"en":"He had an operation done on it.","zh":"他做了手术。"},{"en":"Plastic surgery, in order to cover it and make it less noticeable.","zh":"为了掩盖这一点，人们会进行整形手术。使其不那么显眼。"},{"en":"Oh, well, that's ridiculous, isn't it?","zh":"哦，那真是太荒谬了，不是吗？"},{"en":"It was noticeable, sure, but it wasn't an ugly scar.","zh":"这当然很明显，但并非……难看的疤痕。"},{"en":"It never occurred to me that he should have it taken care of like that.","zh":"我从未想过他应该就这么处理吧。"},{"en":"I agree.","zh":"我同意。"},{"en":"I can understand some scars and physical defects can be ugly and distracting, but not Johnny's.","zh":"我能理解一些疤痕和身体缺陷。可能很丑陋，令人分心，但约翰尼的不会。"},{"en":"In fact, I thought it added character, like it gave him a certain uniqueness.","zh":"事实上，我认为它增添了特色，就像这赋予了他某种独特性。"},{"en":"He must have felt differently, though.","zh":"但他肯定有不同的感受。"},{"en":"He must have felt self-conscious and insecure, perhaps.","zh":"他当时一定感到很不自在，缺乏安全感。也许。"},{"en":"No, no, that's not the reason.","zh":"不，不，那不是原因。"},{"en":"He was totally fine with his scar.","zh":"他完全不在意自己的疤痕。"},{"en":"As you said, he had had it for most of his life.","zh":"正如你所说，他早就有了。他一生中的大部分时间。"},{"en":"Then why did he have the operation?","zh":"那他为什么要接受手术呢？"},{"en":"Because his girlfriend wanted him to.","zh":"因为他女朋友希望他这么做。"},{"en":"What?","zh":"什么？"},{"en":"That's so superficial and selfish of her.","zh":"她这样做太肤浅、太自私了。"},{"en":"If Johnny's girlfriend doesn't like him for who he is, then she does not deserve to be his girlfriend.","zh":"如果约翰尼的女朋友不喜欢他，那又会是谁呢？如果他是，那么她就不配拥有他。做他的女朋友。"},{"en":"You're right.","zh":"你说得对。"},{"en":"So he is insane to give in to her like that.","zh":"所以他屈服简直是疯了。她就是这样。"},{"en":"But when I told him, he said he loves her and would just do what she wants him to.","zh":"但当我告诉他时，他说他他爱她，会做她想做的事。他希望如此。"},{"en":"What a fool he is.","zh":"他真是个傻瓜。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the man say about Johnny?","opts":["He was remembered for the scar on his cheek","He received a heart operation a few days ago","He used to wear a sad face in school","He had some plastic surgery done"],"answer":3,"expl":"「He had some plastic surgery done.」——原句照搬；plastic surgery 同义替换 operation。","signal":"对话开头直给","syn":[["plastic surgery","had an operation done（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What puzzles the woman?","opts":["The man’s deep sympathy for Johnny","The man’s use of the expression ‘fixed’","The man’s covering up of what happened","The man’s good memory of his childhood"],"answer":1,"expl":"「Fixed? What do you mean? You can't fix a scar.」——她对 fixed 这个用词感到不解。","signal":"反问表困惑","syn":[["Fixed? What do you mean?","The man's use of the word 'fixed'（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did the man think of Johnny's scar?","opts":["It gave him a noticeable smartness","It made him appear even more manly","It seemed to give him a certain uniqueness","It seemed to make up for his physical defects"],"answer":2,"expl":"「I thought it added character...gave him a certain uniqueness」——uniqueness 原词复现。","signal":"in fact 转折后","syn":[["added character","a certain uniqueness（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How could we describe the speaker's attitude towards Johnny's girlfriend?","opts":["Liberal","Hostile","Indifferent","Critical"],"answer":3,"expl":"「That's so superficial and selfish of her...does not deserve to be his girlfriend」——批评态度选 Critical。","signal":"评价句态度题","syn":[["superficial and selfish","Critical（态度推断）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506a-6","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"科普研究","level":"四级","title":"语言的起源","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 1（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Talking is unique to humans.","zh":"说话是人类独有的能力。"},{"en":"An animal might make 10 different sounds, but an adult human knows more than 20,000 words.","zh":"一种动物可能会发出 10 种不同的声音，但是一个成年人知道超过20000个字。"},{"en":"Additionally, we're the only animal that expresses thoughts in full sentences.","zh":"此外，我们是唯一会表达​​思想的动物。请用完整的句子。"},{"en":"Researchers don't think language was invented.","zh":"研究人员认为语言并非人为发明的。"},{"en":"Instead, they think it evolved.","zh":"相反，他们认为它是进化而来的。"},{"en":"How did talking evolve?","zh":"语言是如何演变的？"},{"en":"There are two main theories.","zh":"主要有两种理论。"},{"en":"The first theory is that language started with people making different sounds, mostly imitating the things around them like animal calls, nature sounds, and the sounds of tools.","zh":"第一种理论认为语言起源于人们发出不同的声音，大多是在模仿这些东西。他们周围环绕着动物的叫声、自然的声音，以及工具的声音。"},{"en":"Perhaps they made the sound of wind to comment on the weather, or imitated the sound of a bird to tell a friend that there was a bird nearby.","zh":"或许他们发出风的声音评论天气，或者模仿声音一只鸟告诉朋友附近有一只鸟。"},{"en":"Then, over hundreds of thousands of years, those sounds turned into words that people began to learn as part of their language.","zh":"然后，经过数十万年的时间，那些声音逐渐演变成词语，人们开始……学习是他们语言的一部分。"},{"en":"At some point, people started stringing the words together to form sentences.","zh":"在某个时候，人们开始把这些词串联起来。组合起来构成句子。"},{"en":"The other main theory, which is more recent, is that people started off by gesturing, pointing at things with their hands, and imitating actions using their bodies.","zh":"另一个主要理论，也是较新的理论，人们最初是通过做手势、指点来表达的。用手触摸物体，并模仿动作利用他们的身体。"},{"en":"Eventually, these gestures turned into full sign language.","zh":"最终，这些手势演变成了完整的手语。"},{"en":"This theory guesses that after developing sign languages, people eventually started making sounds along with their gestures.","zh":"这种理论推测，在发展出手语之后，人们最终开始一边唱歌一边发出声音手势。"},{"en":"At some point, they switched to mostly making sounds that became words instead of just using their bodies.","zh":"在某个阶段，他们转而主要从事生产制造。声音演变成了词语，而不仅仅是使用他们的身体。"},{"en":"The reason they switched to making sounds, the theory goes, is that talking out loud lets you communicate with someone even when you can't see them.","zh":"他们转而发出声音的原因是……理论上来说，大声说话会……即使你不能与人沟通，你也会与他们沟通。看看他们。"}],"questions":[{"q":"How did language come into being, according to researchers?","opts":["Through deliberation","Through evolution","Through invention","Through collaboration"],"answer":1,"expl":"「Researchers don't think language was invented. Instead, they think it evolved.」——instead 转折定答案。","signal":"instead 转折","syn":[["it evolved","Through evolution（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How did language start, according to the first theory?","opts":["With people imitating sounds around them","With people interacting with animals close by","With people showing each other things nearby","With people trying to string sounds together"],"answer":0,"expl":"「language started with people making different sounds, mostly imitating the things around them」——imitating 原词复现。","signal":"the first theory","syn":[["imitating the things around them","imitating sounds around them（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What advantage does making sounds have, according to the second theory?","opts":["Making sounds can free one’s hands for doing other things","Making sounds proves markedly easier than sign languages","Making sounds enables one to express their ideas more explicitly","Making sounds helps one communicate with people they can’t see"],"answer":3,"expl":"「talking out loud lets you communicate with someone even when you can't see them」——even when you can't see them 是关键限定。","signal":"the reason they switched","syn":[["communicate with someone even when you can't see them","communicate with people they can't see（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506a-7","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"社会心理","level":"四级","title":"炫富的社会代价","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 2（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Is it a good idea to display luxury brands and other signals of status?","zh":"展示奢侈品是个好主意吗？品牌和其他身份象征？"},{"en":"It depends on the situation.","zh":"这要视情况而定。"},{"en":"Studies have shown that people who appear to be wealthy tend to be considered more intelligent, disciplined, and competent than those who do not.","zh":"研究表明，那些看起来有钱人往往被认为更聪明。比那些缺乏纪律和能力的人更自律、更有能力。"},{"en":"But new research found that people believe someone who shows off their social status cares more about benefiting themselves than helping others.","zh":"但最新研究发现，人们会相信某人。那些炫耀社会地位的人更在意别人的看法。他们更注重自身利益而非帮助他人。"},{"en":"This means people are less willing to collaborate with them.","zh":"这意味着人们合作的意愿降低了。和他们一起。"},{"en":"Modesty may be key when cooperation is essential, but the researchers also found that in some cases, status signaling has advantages.","zh":"当合作至关重要时，谦逊或许是关键。但研究人员也发现，在某些情况下在这种情况下，状态信号传递具有优势。"},{"en":"Experiments showed that participants were less likely to choose someone who signals their wealth or status to join a group seeking cooperative members, but participants were more likely to choose that person when they were looking for a competitive team member.","zh":"实验表明，参与者不太可能选择那些能彰显财富或地位的人。加入一个寻求合作成员的团体，但是参与者更有可能选择那个人当时他们正在寻找一支有竞争力的队伍。成员。"},{"en":"These findings suggest that people should change how they present themselves depending on their social goal.","zh":"这些发现表明人们应该改变他们的做法他们根据自己的社会目标来展现自己。"},{"en":"This is the era of social media.","zh":"这是一个社交媒体时代。"},{"en":"People can easily share their wealth and status to large audiences, but they need to consider the consequences.","zh":"人们可以轻松地分享他们的财富和地位面向广大受众，但他们需要考虑后果。"},{"en":"Posting about luxury purchases and expensive vacations online may help you to persuade others and frighten competitors, but it could also signal to potential friends or future employers that you are unlikely to think about the needs of others.","zh":"在网上发布有关奢侈品购物和昂贵假期的信息或许能帮助你说服他人并恐吓他人但这也可能向潜在竞争对手发出信号。朋友或未来的雇主不太可能要懂得体谅他人的需求。"},{"en":"This makes things tricky for people who may want to impress others while also demonstrating that they are a team player.","zh":"这使得一些人的处境变得棘手。既想给别人留下深刻印象，又想表明……他们是团队合作者。"}],"questions":[{"q":"How would people describe someone who shows off their social status, according to new research?","opts":["Well disciplined","Quite confident","Somewhat selfish","Highly intelligent"],"answer":2,"expl":"「cares more about benefiting themselves than helping others」——benefiting themselves 同义替换 selfish。","signal":"new research found","syn":[["benefiting themselves","Somewhat selfish（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"When were participants more likely to choose someone who signaled their wealth or status?","opts":["When they wanted to have a competitive team member","When they were looking for a cooperative workmate","When they found collaboration essential to them","When they were seeking someone to help them"],"answer":0,"expl":"「more likely to choose that person when they were looking for a competitive team member」——对比结构：cooperative 不选、competitive 选。","signal":"对比：less/more likely","syn":[["competitive team member","competitive workmate（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What should people do before sharing their wealth and status online?","opts":["Avoid frightening competitors","Make clear their social goal","Adopt persuasive strategies","Consider the consequences"],"answer":3,"expl":"「they need to consider the consequences」——need to 同义替换 should。","signal":"need to 建议句","syn":[["consider the consequences","Consider the consequences（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506a-8","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"历史文化","level":"四级","title":"动物园的起源","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 3（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Human fascination with animals goes back as far as humans do.","zh":"人类对动物的迷恋可以追溯到很久以前。就像人类那样。"},{"en":"Of the oldest cave paintings discovered, some are up to 40,000 years old and there are more images of animals than humans.","zh":"在已发现的最古老的洞穴壁画中，有一些是距今可达4万年，而且动物图片比人类图片多。"},{"en":"At some point, humans began to capture and hold animals.","zh":"在某个时期，人类开始捕获和饲养动物。"},{"en":"The first known collections were held by royalty and were not open to the public.","zh":"已知最早的藏品是由皇室成员持有的。不对公众开放。"},{"en":"In Egypt, researchers have found buildings from around 3500 BC containing the remains of animals including elephants which were not native to Egypt.","zh":"在埃及，研究人员发现了来自世界各地的建筑物公元前3500年，其中包含动物遗骸，包括这些大象并非埃及本土物种。"},{"en":"But life wasn't easy for these animals.","zh":"但这些动物的生活并不轻松。"},{"en":"They probably had short lives and the remains show evidence of severe injuries.","zh":"他们可能寿命很短，遗骸也已遗失。显示有严重伤情。"},{"en":"The first public exhibit of animals may have been created by Egypt's Queen Hatshepsut around 1480 BC.","zh":"首次公开动物展览可能已经由埃及女王哈特谢普苏特于公元1480年左右建造公元前。"},{"en":"Researchers think the zoo was started with animals brought home from a far-off land known as Point.","zh":"研究人员认为，动物园最初就是以动物为主要动物而建立的。从一个遥远的国度带回家作为点。"},{"en":"It's unclear why the queen built the zoo but it might have been to show off her wealth and power.","zh":"目前尚不清楚女王建造动物园的原因。但也可能是为了炫耀。她的财富和权力。"},{"en":"Early zoos are found all over the world.","zh":"世界各地都能找到早期动物园。"},{"en":"In China, Emperor Wen Wang is said to have built a Garden of Intelligence around 1060 BC.","zh":"在中国，据说文王皇帝大约在公元1060年左右建造了一座智慧花园公元前。"},{"en":"It included deer, birds and many fish.","zh":"其中包括鹿、鸟类和许多鱼类。"},{"en":"In England, King Henry I set up a collection of animals in about 1110 as part of the royal estate.","zh":"在英国，亨利一世国王设立了一个大约在公元1110年，作为一部分收集动物皇家庄园。"},{"en":"His collection included tigers and lions.","zh":"他的藏品包括老虎和狮子。"},{"en":"This collection eventually moved to the Tower of London in 1235.","zh":"这批藏品最终被移至塔楼。1235年的伦敦。"},{"en":"The collection stayed at that location for 600 years.","zh":"这批藏品在那里保存了600年。年。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What can we see in the oldest cave paintings?","opts":["Much evidence of humans capturing animals","More images of animals than humans","Fewer images of buildings than animals","Little proof of human fascination with animals"],"answer":1,"expl":"「there are more images of animals than humans」——more...than 比较结构直接对应。","signal":"数字年代附近","syn":[["more images of animals than humans","More images of animals than humans（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do we learn about the first known collections of animals?","opts":["They were open to the public","They were primarily native","They were kept by royalty","They were hardly injured"],"answer":2,"expl":"「The first known collections were held by royalty and were not open to the public」——royalty 同义替换 royal family。","signal":"first known 定位","syn":[["held by royalty","kept by royalty（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why might Queen Hatshepsut have built the zoo?","opts":["To enable the public to watch animals close by","To introduce to Egyptians animals from Punt","To protect the endangered animals","To show off her riches and power"],"answer":3,"expl":"「it might have been to show off her wealth and power」——might 表推测与题干 might 呼应；wealth 同义替换 riches。","signal":"it's unclear...but","syn":[["show off her wealth and power","To show off her riches and power（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do we learn about King Henry I's collection of animals?","opts":["It was part of the royal estate","It was a shelter for wild animals","It was the kingdom’s best-equipped zoo","It was the first public exhibit of animals"],"answer":0,"expl":"「set up a collection of animals...as part of the royal estate」——原词复现。","signal":"人名定位","syn":[["part of the royal estate","It was part of the royal estate（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506b-1","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"体育赛事","level":"四级","title":"七英里大桥长跑","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 1（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方/易考吧答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"A Florida teenager and an Atlanta woman won the overall men's and women's divisions Saturday at the annual 7-mile bridge run.","zh":"一名佛罗里达州的青少年和一名亚特兰大的女子赢得了比赛周六将举行男子和女子组的总决赛一年一度的7英里桥梁长跑。"},{"en":"Václav Bursa, 15, of Big Pine Key, Florida, finished first overall.","zh":"来自佛罗里达州大松岛的15岁青年瓦茨拉夫·布尔萨总成绩第一名。"},{"en":"He completed the race in 41 minutes and 1 second and claimed the top spot in the men's division.","zh":"他用时41分钟完成了比赛。仅用1秒就夺得了榜首位置男子组。"},{"en":"Bursa won third place in the 20-22 race.","zh":"布尔萨在20-22届比赛中获得第三名种族。"},{"en":"He is a student at Marathon High School.","zh":"他是马拉松高中的一名学生。"},{"en":"Joanna Stevens, 28, of Atlanta, completed the course in 41 minutes and 12 seconds.","zh":"来自亚特兰大的28岁乔安娜·史蒂文斯完成了课程耗时41分12秒。"},{"en":"She won the women's division title and placed second overall.","zh":"她赢得了女子组冠军，并取得了名次。总成绩第二名。"},{"en":"The race drew competitors from 41 U.S. states.","zh":"这项赛事吸引了来自美国41个国家的参赛者。各州。"},{"en":"There were also runners from other countries, including Canada, the U.K., and Switzerland.","zh":"还有其他国家的选手参赛，包括加拿大、英国和瑞士。"},{"en":"The run closed the span between the Middle and Lower Keys to traffic for three hours Saturday.","zh":"这次跑动缩短了中部之间的距离。下基斯岛交通拥堵持续了三个小时周六。"},{"en":"The April contest is one of the most popular running events in the southeastern United States.","zh":"四月份的比赛是其中最……美国东南部地区流行的跑步赛事。"},{"en":"The race field filled within minutes after online registration opened in January.","zh":"在线比赛开始后几分钟内，参赛名额就被填满了。注册于一月份开放。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the news report say about Václav Bursa and Joanna Stevens?","opts":["They are young teenagers from Atlanta","They won this year’s 7 Mile Bridge Run","They completed the race in less than 40 minutes","They are both students at Marathon High School"],"answer":1,"expl":"「won the overall men's and women's divisions Saturday at the annual 7-mile bridge run」——两人分获男女组冠军。","signal":"新闻首句","syn":[["won the overall men's and women's divisions","They won this year's 7 Mile Bridge Run（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do we learn about the April contest?","opts":["It drew competitors from more than 40 countries","It is watched live online by fans all over the world","It closed the city of Big Pine Key to traffic for three hours","It is one of the most popular running events in the southeastern U.S"],"answer":3,"expl":"「one of the most popular running events in the southeastern United States」——popular 原词复现。","signal":"April contest 定位","syn":[["most popular running events","one of the most popular running events（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506b-2","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"人物故事","level":"四级","title":"宇航员蒂姆·皮克退役","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 2（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方/易考吧答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"British astronaut Tim Peake is stepping down permanently from his role as a European astronaut.","zh":"英国宇航员蒂姆·皮克将永久卸任。他曾担任欧洲宇航员。"},{"en":"He's going to take up a full-time position as ambassador for science and space instead, work he's been doing since 2019.","zh":"他打算全职工作转而担任科学和太空大使的职位，这是他自 2019 年以来一直在从事的工作。"},{"en":"The former British Army Air Corps helicopter pilot was selected as a European Space Agency astronaut in 2009.","zh":"这位前英国陆军航空兵直升机飞行员被选为欧洲航天局宇航员2009年。"},{"en":"He flew to the space station for a six-month tour in 2015.","zh":"他飞往空间站……2015年进行了为期六个月的巡演。"},{"en":"The tour saw him control a robot on Earth remotely from orbit.","zh":"在巡演中，他操控了一个机器人从轨道上远程操控地球。"},{"en":"He also helped dock two spacecraft.","zh":"他还参与了两艘航天器的对接工作。"},{"en":"Tim said, Being an astronaut has been the most extraordinary experience.","zh":"蒂姆说，当宇航员一直是……非常非凡的经历。"},{"en":"I've had the privilege of working with an exceptional team of individuals during the past 13 years with the agency.","zh":"我有幸与一位过去13年里，我们拥有一支杰出的团队。在该机构工作多年。"},{"en":"It has been incredibly exciting and rewarding.","zh":"这真是令人无比兴奋和收获满满。"},{"en":"By assuming the role of an ambassador for human flights to space, I'll continue to support the European and the UK space agencies.","zh":"通过担任大使的角色我将继续支持载人航天飞行。欧洲航天局和英国航天局。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn from the news report about Tim Peake?","opts":["He was once a full-time ambassador","He was soon to retire from the army","He became an astronaut in 2015","He used to be a helicopter pilot"],"answer":3,"expl":"「The former British Army Air Corps helicopter pilot」——former 同义替换 used to be。","signal":"former 信号词","syn":[["former...helicopter pilot","He used to be a helicopter pilot（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does Tim Peake say about his work with the European Space Agency?","opts":["It has been unbelievably exciting and rewarding","It has been extraordinarily tough and demanding","It has contributed a great deal to human flights to space","It has given him exceptional privilege as an ambassador"],"answer":0,"expl":"「It has been incredibly exciting and rewarding.」——原句照搬。","signal":"引语直接给答案","syn":[["incredibly exciting and rewarding","unbelievably exciting and rewarding（同义替换 incredibly→unbelievably）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506b-3","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会趣闻","level":"四级","title":"超市里的五只猫","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 3（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方/易考吧答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"An ASDA store in Wales is now home to five cats after they wandered in and made themselves comfortable.","zh":"威尔士的一家ASDA商店现在是它们闯入后，被送到了五只猫那里。他们放松下来，找了个舒服的地方坐好。"},{"en":"The supermarket is known for its loyal customers, but now has a different kind of visitor that has appeared over the last year.","zh":"这家超市以其忠实顾客而闻名。但现在访客类型有所不同了。过去一年中出现的情况。"},{"en":"Regular shoppers at the supermarket are familiar with the sight of several cats settling down in the shop aisles.","zh":"经常光顾这家超市的人都很熟悉几只猫安顿下来的景象商店的过道。"},{"en":"The unusual situation started about 12 months ago, when one cat routinely started visiting the store.","zh":"这种不寻常的情况大约始于12个月前。当一只猫开始经常光顾这家商店时。"},{"en":"Local newspapers reported that puzzled customers posted on Facebook groups to try to find out if the cat was lost.","zh":"当地报纸报道说，困惑的顾客在社交媒体上发帖求助。通过 Facebook 群组来了解情况猫走丢了。"},{"en":"But its owner assured the concerned customers it was very much loved and fed at home.","zh":"但其所有者向担忧的顾客保证在家备受宠爱和照顾。"},{"en":"It just enjoyed visiting the shop.","zh":"它只是喜欢逛这家店。"},{"en":"Staff did their best to discourage the pet from hanging around, but instead of leaving and never coming back, it invited its friends round.","zh":"工作人员尽力劝阻这只宠物与其闲逛，不如离开，它再也没有回来，于是邀请朋友们来家里玩。"},{"en":"There are now at least five different cats who come almost on a daily basis.","zh":"现在至少有五只不同的猫他们几乎每天都来。"},{"en":"They visit the store so much that staff have been forced to put up signs asking their customers not to feed them.","zh":"他们光顾这家店的次数太多了，以至于店员都……被迫竖起标语询问他们的顾客不会喂它们。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn about the five cats seen in the Asda store?","opts":["They are known for their loyalty to their owners","They are brought in by the store’s customers","They are regular visitors to the store","They are pets kept by the store staff"],"answer":2,"expl":"「There are now at least five different cats who come almost on a daily basis」——天天来即 regular visitors。","signal":"数字 five 定位","syn":[["come almost on a daily basis","They are regular visitors to the store（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did some customers think when the first cat appeared?","opts":["It might be a nuisance to the loyal shoppers","It might have been abandoned by its owner","It might be 12 months old","It might have got lost"],"answer":3,"expl":"「puzzled customers posted on Facebook groups to try to find out if the cat was lost」——find out if the cat was lost 同义替换 might have got lost。","signal":"puzzled 同义定位","syn":[["find out if the cat was lost","It might have got lost（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What are customers asked not to do?","opts":["Feed the cats","Remove any store signs","Sit in the shop aisles","Bring in pets with them"],"answer":0,"expl":"「put up signs asking their customers not to feed them」——not to feed 原词复现。","signal":"put up signs","syn":[["not to feed them","Feed the cats（否定陷阱反选）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506b-4","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"校园生活","level":"四级","title":"搬出宿舍的讨论","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 1（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方/易考吧答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"I've been thinking about moving off campus next semester.","zh":"我一直在考虑接下来搬出校园。学期。"},{"en":"Hmm.","zh":"唔。"},{"en":"I don't know if that's a good idea, as your mother and I would worry about you living all by yourself in an apartment so far from home.","zh":"我不知道这是否是个好主意。就像你妈妈和我都会担心的那样你一个人住在公寓里离家好远。"},{"en":"And then there's the expense, too.","zh":"此外，还有费用问题。"},{"en":"I'm not sure we can afford it.","zh":"我不确定我们是否负担得起。"},{"en":"Well, I wouldn't be alone, actually.","zh":"其实，我并不孤单。"},{"en":"Three of my friends from the dormitory would share the place with me.","zh":"我宿舍里的三个朋友会跟我一起住吧。"},{"en":"And with four of us, it wouldn't cost any more than living in the dorm.","zh":"我们四个人，就不会花多少钱比住在宿舍里更舒服。"},{"en":"Are you sure about that?","zh":"你确定吗？"},{"en":"Rents in big cities are high, and then there's the cost of electricity and gas.","zh":"大城市的租金很高，然后还有电费和燃气费。"},{"en":"Have you factored those in?","zh":"你把这些因素都考虑进去了吗？"},{"en":"We've budgeted for those, and for internet and transportation.","zh":"我们已经为这些费用以及网络费用做了预算。运输。"},{"en":"And, if we move far enough from the city centre, the rent is low enough for us to afford all of it.","zh":"而且，如果我们离……足够远市中心，租金足够低我们负担得起所有这些。"},{"en":"What about the commutes to and from campus?","zh":"往返校园的通勤情况如何？"},{"en":"It sounds like you'll be wasting several hours every day on the road instead of studying.","zh":"听起来你会浪费好几个小时。每天都在路上，而不是学习。"},{"en":"It's about an hour to campus, but there's no reason I can't study on the bus.","zh":"到校园大约需要一个小时，但是……我完全可以在公交车上学习。"},{"en":"After all, I did that during high school, and my commute was even longer then.","zh":"毕竟，我高中时就做过这件事。那时候我的通勤时间更长。"},{"en":"That's true, but I'm not sure why you want to leave campus and go through all that trouble when the cost is the same.","zh":"没错，但我不太明白你为什么这么说。想离开校园，经历这一切当成本相同时，就会出现这种问题。"},{"en":"For a lot of reasons.","zh":"原因有很多。"},{"en":"We'd have a kitchen, so we could cook ourselves.","zh":"我们会有一个厨房，这样我们就可以做饭了。我们自己。"},{"en":"And we'd each have our own bedroom, where we could study, instead of going to the library.","zh":"我们每个人都会有自己的卧室，在那里我们可以学习，而不是去……图书馆。"},{"en":"We'd just have more space and privacy.","zh":"我们只会拥有更多的空间和隐私。"},{"en":"I'm not convinced that the benefits are greater than the disadvantages, but I'll discuss this with your mother.","zh":"我并不认为这样做的好处更大。缺点比优点多，但我会和对方讨论这个问题。你的母亲。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What has the woman been thinking of doing next semester?","opts":["Sharing her room with friends","Cutting down her living expenses","Living off campus","Moving to the city center"],"answer":2,"expl":"「I've been thinking about moving off campus next semester」——原句压缩。","signal":"对话首句意图","syn":[["moving off campus","Living off campus（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man suggest the woman take into consideration?","opts":["The facilities available","Various costs involved","Changes in living conditions","The distance to her home"],"answer":1,"expl":"「there's the expense...Rents are high...cost of electricity and gas」——father 列举各类花费即 various costs。","signal":"列举结构","syn":[["the cost of electricity and gas","Various costs involved（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the woman say she did during high school?","opts":["Went through much trouble","Commuted to save money","Studied on the bus","Lived on campus"],"answer":2,"expl":"「I did that during high school」——that 指 study on the bus。","signal":"指代回指","syn":[["study on the bus","Studied on the bus（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man say he'll do at the end of the conversation?","opts":["Discuss the matter with the woman’s mother","Make a decision within a few days","Try his best to persuade his wife","Weigh the benefits against the disadvantages"],"answer":0,"expl":"「I'll discuss this with your mother」——原句照搬。","signal":"结尾承诺","syn":[["discuss this with your mother","Discuss the matter with the woman's mother（同义替换 this→the matter）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506b-5","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"购物场景","level":"四级","title":"给侄子买礼物","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 2（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方/易考吧答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Good morning.","zh":"早上好。"},{"en":"I'm looking for a present for my nephew, Lawrence.","zh":"我想给我侄子买份礼物。劳伦斯。"},{"en":"Hi.","zh":"你好。"},{"en":"Do you have anything in mind?","zh":"你有什么想法吗？"},{"en":"I'm not sure.","zh":"我不知道。"},{"en":"No.","zh":"不。"},{"en":"Do you know what boys aged around 10 typically like?","zh":"你知道10岁左右的男孩都喜欢什么吗？通常喜欢？"},{"en":"For that age group, our biggest seller this year has been this action figure.","zh":"对于这个年龄段来说，我们最畅销的产品是今年我最喜欢的就是这个玩偶。"},{"en":"It's called Bobo Man, and it's incredibly popular.","zh":"它叫波波侠，非常受欢迎。"},{"en":"Does it do anything?","zh":"它有什么作用吗？"},{"en":"Not by itself.","zh":"单独来看，并非如此。"},{"en":"It has no batteries, if that's what you mean.","zh":"它没有电池，如果你指的是这个的话。意思是。"},{"en":"There's a Bobo Man cartoon popular amongst young children, you see, and this toy is the lead character from the show.","zh":"有一部名为《波波侠》的动画片在年轻人中很受欢迎。你看，这是给孩子们玩的玩具。该剧的主角。"},{"en":"Oh, I understand now.","zh":"哦，我明白了。"},{"en":"I've never heard of it, but I do know little Lawrence loves cartoons.","zh":"我以前从未听说过，但我确实知道小劳伦斯喜欢卡通片。"},{"en":"Do you have any other popular toys?","zh":"你们还有其他受欢迎的玩具吗？"},{"en":"Perhaps something educational?","zh":"或许可以做一些教育性的东西？"},{"en":"Yes, of course.","zh":"是的当然。"},{"en":"Right over here we have dozens of puzzles for children of all ages.","zh":"这里就有几十个谜题。适合所有年龄段的儿童。"},{"en":"They are fun, great for exercising the mind, and can be played either alone or in groups.","zh":"它们很有趣，很适合锻炼大脑。既可以单独玩，也可以和朋友一起玩。团体。"},{"en":"I like this sort of idea.","zh":"我喜欢这种想法。"},{"en":"Lawrence has a sister who is slightly older, so maybe a game that they can play together would be good.","zh":"劳伦斯有个姐姐，比他稍大一些。所以也许可以玩个游戏在一起会很好。"},{"en":"What do you think of Battleships, then?","zh":"那么，你对战舰游戏有什么看法？"},{"en":"It's a total classic.","zh":"这绝对是经典之作。"},{"en":"It has been around since the 1930s.","zh":"它从上世纪30年代就存在了。"},{"en":"Oh yeah, we had one of those when growing up.","zh":"哦，是的，我们以前也有一个那样的成长。"},{"en":"Of course you did.","zh":"你当然会这么做。"},{"en":"Everyone did, and kids enjoy it just as much today as you and I did when we were young.","zh":"大家都这么做了，孩子们也很喜欢。今天的情况和你我当时的情况很相似。我们当时还年轻。"},{"en":"Some games just never get old.","zh":"有些游戏永远不会过时。"},{"en":"I suppose you are right.","zh":"我想你是对的。"},{"en":"I have fond memories playing Battleships when it was raining outside, and we had to stay indoors.","zh":"我对玩战舰游戏有着美好的回忆。外面下着雨，我们不得不待在家里。室内。"},{"en":"That's decided, then.","zh":"那就这么定了。"},{"en":"How much?","zh":"多少？"},{"en":"£19.90, please.","zh":"请付19.90英镑。"},{"en":"There you are.","zh":"你在那里。"},{"en":"Have a nice day.","zh":"祝你今天过得愉快。"},{"en":"Thank you.","zh":"谢谢。"},{"en":"You too.","zh":"你也是。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What is the woman doing?","opts":["Interviewing the man","Looking for Lawrence","Choosing a present for her nephew","Helping the man with his shopping"],"answer":2,"expl":"「I'm looking for a present for my nephew, Lawrence」——原句压缩。","signal":"对话首句","syn":[["looking for a present for my nephew","Choosing a present for her nephew（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How does the man describe Bobo Man, the action figure?","opts":["Quite educational","Incredibly popular","Driven by batteries","Obviously childish"],"answer":1,"expl":"「it's incredibly popular」——原词复现。","signal":" biggest seller 定位","syn":[["incredibly popular","Incredibly popular（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What kind of toy does the woman think would be good for Lawrence?","opts":["One he loves for helping exercise his mind","One he can play together with his sister","One he finds interesting and challenging","One he can play either alone or in a group"],"answer":1,"expl":"「maybe a game that they can play together would be good」——they 指 Lawrence 和他姐姐。","signal":"maybe 表建议","syn":[["a game that they can play together","One he can play together with his sister（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do we learn from the conversation about the game Battleships?","opts":["It has been enjoyed by kids for decades","It always reminds people of times of war","It has been played both indoors and outdoors","It distinguishes itself as one of the oldest games"],"answer":0,"expl":"「It's a total classic. It has been around since the 1930s」——since the 1930s 即几十年。","signal":"年代数字题","syn":[["been around since the 1930s","It has been enjoyed by kids for decades（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506b-6","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"商业心理","level":"四级","title":"选择的悖论","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 1（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方/易考吧答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"We assume that if we offer our customers more choices, then they'll be more likely to buy our products.","zh":"我们假设，如果我们向客户提供……选择越多，他们就越有可能购买我们的产品。"},{"en":"But here's the paradox of choice.","zh":"但这就是选择的悖论。"},{"en":"If a person is presented with too many choices, they are actually less likely to buy.","zh":"如果一个人面对太多选择越多，他们购买的可能性就越小。"},{"en":"In 2012, psychologists published a study about jams.","zh":"2012年，心理学家发表了一项关于果酱的研究。"},{"en":"On a regular day, at a local food market, people would find a display table with 24 different kinds of jams.","zh":"在平常的一天，在一家当地餐馆在市场上，人们会发现一个展示桌，上面摆放着……24种不同的果酱。"},{"en":"Then, on another day, at that same food market, people were given only six different types of jam choices.","zh":"然后，在另一天，吃同样的食物时，市场上，人们只能买到六种不同类型的商品。果酱的选择。"},{"en":"Guess which display table led to more sales?","zh":"猜猜哪个展示台带来了更多销量？"},{"en":"The study found that, while the bigger display table created more interest, people were almost ten times less likely to purchase a jar of jam than in the case of the smaller display.","zh":"研究发现，虽然更大的显示屏这张桌子引起了更多人的兴趣，几乎有十个人围坐在一起。购买一罐东西的可能性要低得多比小果酱的情况要多。展示。"},{"en":"Customer satisfaction takes a hit as well.","zh":"顾客满意度也受到影响。"},{"en":"In the study, the bigger display of jams leads to lower customer satisfaction than the smaller display.","zh":"研究中，果酱的展示量更大与较小的方案相比，这会导致客户满意度降低。展示。"},{"en":"In an extensive study published in 2015, researchers analysed a total of 99 choice studies and specifically looked at those cases in which reducing choices helped to boost sales.","zh":"在2015年发表的一项广泛研究中，研究人员共分析了99项选择研究，特别关注了那些减少的情况。多种选择有助于提升销售额。"},{"en":"They found four rules that motivate consumers to buy.","zh":"他们发现了四条能够激励消费者的规则买。"},{"en":"When people want to make a quick and easy choice, when the product is complex, when it's difficult to compare alternatives, and when consumers don't have clear preferences.","zh":"当人们想要快速且当产品复杂时，这无疑是一个简单的选择。比较不同方案很困难，而且当消费者……没有明确的偏好。"},{"en":"So, as you can see, when it comes to choices, less is more.","zh":"所以，正如你所看到的，当它到来时选择方面，少即是多。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn from the passage about the paradox of choice?","opts":["A display of a variety of products increases consumers’ interest","Too many choices decrease one’s desire to buy","Fewer choices lead to lower customer satisfaction","Customers given more choices are more likely to get confused"],"answer":1,"expl":"「If a person is presented with too many choices, they are actually less likely to buy」——less likely to buy 同义替换 decrease desire to buy。","signal":"but 转折后","syn":[["less likely to buy","Too many choices decrease one's desire to buy（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did the psychologists want to find out in their 2012 study about jams?","opts":["What kind of display results in more sales","What kind of display creates more interest","What kind of display attracts a greater crowd of customers","What kind of display leads to greater customer satisfaction"],"answer":3,"expl":"「Guess which display table led to more sales?...bigger display created more interest...lower customer satisfaction」——研究核心是比较两种陈列的满意度。","signal":"研究目的题","syn":[["which display table led to more sales","What kind of display leads to greater customer satisfaction（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is the finding of an extensive study published in 2015?","opts":["There are situations where customers buy nothing","There are tricks to increase customer satisfaction","There are ways to predict customer preferences:","There are rules that motivate customers to buy"],"answer":3,"expl":"「They found four rules that motivate consumers to buy」——原词复现。","signal":"2015 study 定位","syn":[["four rules that motivate consumers to buy","There are rules that motivate customers to buy（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506b-7","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"职场公益","level":"四级","title":"志愿服务的价值","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 2（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方/易考吧答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"The New Year has come and gone, and many may have already forgotten what they had resolved to do on January 1st.","zh":"新年已过，许多人可能已经忘记了他们曾经拥有过什么。决定于1月1日执行。"},{"en":"But if that resolution was to volunteer more, now is the best time to start.","zh":"但如果这个决心是增加志愿服务时间，现在正是开始的最佳时机。"},{"en":"Volunteering can drop after the holiday season, and by February, some organizations lack the volunteers they had in surplus just a month ago.","zh":"节假日过后，志愿服务人数可能会减少。到二月份，一些组织就缺少志愿者了。一个月前还有盈余。"},{"en":"According to one survey, only 26% of Americans volunteer, despite reports that many Americans view volunteering as worthwhile.","zh":"根据一项调查，只有 26%尽管有报道称许多美国人认为志愿服务是错误的，但美国人仍然积极参与志愿活动。志愿服务是一件有意义的事。"},{"en":"Why such a disconnect?","zh":"为什么会出现这种脱节？"},{"en":"Most people cite time and conflicting work schedules as major barriers.","zh":"大多数人提到时间安排和工作时间冲突。作为主要障碍。"},{"en":"But employees and employers would actually benefit if companies made employee volunteering part of the job.","zh":"但如果这样做，雇员和雇主实际上都会受益。公司将员工志愿服务纳入工作职责。"},{"en":"Researchers have found donating our time and talent to others can lower blood pressure, boost happiness, and improve mental and physical health.","zh":"研究人员发现，捐献我们的时间和才能对其他人来说，它可以降低血压，提升幸福感。并改善身心健康。"},{"en":"Studies have also linked employee volunteer programs with more productive employees.","zh":"研究还发现员工志愿服务计划与以下方面有关：员工生产力更高。"},{"en":"With so much emphasis on employee wellness these days, company volunteer programs could be the perfect 2025 resolution.","zh":"鉴于对员工福祉的如此重视，这些在这些日子里，公司志愿者项目可能是完美的选择。2025 年的决议。"},{"en":"But for volunteering to benefit employees and the workplace, the entire organization needs to be involved.","zh":"但对于志愿服务而言，这有利于员工和在工作场所，整个组织都需要参与。"},{"en":"By allowing employees to donate their time during work hours, the workplace becomes an outlet for personal fulfillment without affecting personal time.","zh":"允许员工在工作期间捐献时间在工作时间内，工作场所成为一个发泄的渠道。在不影响个人时间的前提下实现个人成就。"},{"en":"In one survey, 89% of employees perceived companies that sponsored volunteer activities as creating a better working environment.","zh":"在一项调查中，89%的员工认为赞助志愿者活动的公司创造了更好的工作环境。"},{"en":"And 75% said volunteering was critical to their well-being.","zh":"75%的人表示志愿服务至关重要他们的福祉。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do many Americans think of volunteering?","opts":["Stressful","Burdensome","Worthwhile","Energy-boosting"],"answer":2,"expl":"「many Americans view volunteering as worthwhile」——view as 同义替换 think of。","signal":"despite 转折前","syn":[["view volunteering as worthwhile","Worthwhile（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How could companies ensure both employees and employers benefit from volunteering?","opts":["By linking it with employees’ salary","By taking it as the New Year resolution","By improving work schedules","By making it part of the job"],"answer":3,"expl":"「if companies made employee volunteering part of the job」——原句压缩。","signal":"if 条件句","syn":[["made employee volunteering part of the job","By making it part of the job（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did 75% of employees say about volunteering in a survey?","opts":["It was very important to their well-being","It had taken little of their spare time","It was an outlet for their personal fulfillment","It helped improve their working environment"],"answer":0,"expl":"「75% said volunteering was critical to their well-being」——critical 同义替换 important。","signal":"数字 75%","syn":[["critical to their well-being","very important to their well-being（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2506b-8","group":"2025年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"商业环保","level":"四级","title":"反对浪费的美食生意","material":"2025年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 3（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方/易考吧答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"The vast majority of the UK's 200,000 tons of retail sector's annual food waste comes from supermarkets, but it's a problem that impacts independent luxury food suppliers too.","zh":"英国20万人口中的绝大多数零售业每年浪费的食物数量高达数吨。来自超市，但这却是一个影响范围很广的问题。也包括独立高端食品供应商。"},{"en":"The scale is small.","zh":"规模很小。"},{"en":"It's estimated at less than 1% of the UK's food waste total.","zh":"据估计不到1%英国的食物浪费总量。"},{"en":"But the quality from these suppliers is high.","zh":"但这些供应商提供的产品质量很高。"},{"en":"Everything from specialist cheeses to sought-after coffee beans gets thrown away every day in the current food system.","zh":"从特色奶酪到炙手可热的咖啡，应有尽有。每天都有大量的豆子被扔掉。现行食品体系。"},{"en":"This is where French entrepreneur Sophie André comes in.","zh":"这时，法国企业家索菲·安德烈出现了。在。"},{"en":"In 2016, she moved to London and began by setting up a business delivering luxury handmade food across the city.","zh":"2016年，她搬到伦敦并开始通过建立一家提供奢华手工制品的企业。城市各处的美食。"},{"en":"Food delivery seems to be a big thing here, she says.","zh":"外卖似乎很流行。她说，就在这里。"},{"en":"So, I started delivering products by bicycle.","zh":"于是，我开始骑自行车送货。"},{"en":"Talking with local producers, I learned that a small part of the production is sometimes wasted due to problems with size or shape.","zh":"与当地生产者交谈后，我了解到少量产品有时会被浪费掉。由于尺寸或形状问题。"},{"en":"But the quality of the products remains unchanged.","zh":"但产品质量保持不变。"},{"en":"Unlike many food waste projects that have sprung up in recent years, the idea is not simply to redistribute waste food, but to provide a high quality product.","zh":"与许多涌现出来的食物浪费项目不同近年来，这种想法并非如此。仅仅是为了重新分配食物垃圾，而是为了提供高品质产品。"},{"en":"André's company, Elysia, offers breakfasts and snacks specifically aimed at business meetings and events.","zh":"安德烈的公司Elysia专门提供早餐和小吃。适用于商务会议和活动。"},{"en":"Once sourced, Elysia uses waste products to create simple, natural, straightforward meals and snacks.","zh":"Elysia公司一旦获得原材料，就会利用废弃物进行生产。简单、天然、直接的餐食和零食。"},{"en":"Perhaps unlike other waste food, the supply is regular.","zh":"或许与其他食物垃圾不同，这种食物的供应是常规的。"},{"en":"Suppliers will always have a certain amount of surplus.","zh":"供应商总会有一定数量的剩余。"},{"en":"So, the menus remain regular too.","zh":"所以，菜单也保持不变。"},{"en":"André believes this benefits both her business and her customers.","zh":"安德烈认为这既有利于她的生意，也有利于……她的顾客。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn about the UK's retail sector food waste?","opts":["It amounts to 2,000 tons daily","It mostly comes from supermarkets","It is estimated at 11% of the UK’s total food supply","It has a lot to do with independent luxury food suppliers"],"answer":1,"expl":"「The vast majority...comes from supermarkets」——vast majority 同义替换 mostly。","signal":"vast majority 定位","syn":[["vast majority...comes from supermarkets","It mostly comes from supermarkets（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does Sophie André's business do in London?","opts":["It rents bicycles to deliver food","It sells sought-after coffee beans","It delivers luxury hand-made food","It recycles waste food from the city"],"answer":2,"expl":"「setting up a business delivering luxury handmade food across the city」——原句压缩。","signal":"人名定位","syn":[["delivering luxury handmade food","It delivers luxury hand-made food（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"In what way does Sophie André's business differ from many food waste projects?","opts":["It pays special attention to the size and shape of its products","It tries to escape the constraints of the current food system","It cooperates closely with local producers","It aims to provide high-quality products"],"answer":3,"expl":"「the idea is not simply to redistribute waste food, but to provide a high quality product」——not...but 结构。","signal":"not...but 对比","syn":[["to provide a high quality product","It aims to provide high-quality products（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why will suppliers always have a certain amount of surplus?","opts":["To ensure a regular supply","To maintain a unique menu","To make up for the waste products","To meet customers’ urgent demand"],"answer":0,"expl":"「Suppliers will always have a certain amount of surplus. So, the menus remain regular too」——供给稳定即保证 regular supply。","signal":"so 因果词","syn":[["always have a certain amount of surplus","To ensure a regular supply（因果推断）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512a-1","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会趣闻","level":"四级","title":"发动机盖里的小猫","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 1（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"A terrified cat has survived a five mile round trip under the engine cover of a car on a school run.","zh":"一只受惊的猫在五英里的路程中幸存了下来在发动机盖下来回穿梭开车送孩子上学。"},{"en":"The black cat was found curled up under the engine cover of David King's car when he decided to do an oil check after dropping his grandson off at school in Kent.","zh":"人们发现那只黑猫蜷缩在……大卫·金的汽车引擎盖他决定之后做一次机油检查。送孙子去肯特郡上学。"},{"en":"Mr. King's wife said her husband had come running in and was shouting for me to come have a look.","zh":"金先生的妻子说她丈夫来了跑进来，大声喊我过来看看。"},{"en":"We weren't even sure it was alive, so I gently pushed it with a stick to check it was breathing and saw it was a terrified little cat.","zh":"我们甚至都不确定它是否还活着，所以我用棍子轻轻地把它推了下去检查它是否还在呼吸，发现它……一只吓坏了的小猫。"},{"en":"It reversed even further into the engine and was stuck.","zh":"它甚至倒退得更远，钻进了发动机里。卡住了。"},{"en":"I tried to reach it, but it was too far down and there wasn't any way I could get it out.","zh":"我试图够到它，但它……太深了，已经没有办法了。我可以把它弄出来。"},{"en":"Following a rescue by UK charity Cat's Protection, the four year old cat was later reunited with its owner, Mr. King's neighbor.","zh":"在英国慈善机构“猫咪保护协会”的救助下，这只四岁的猫后来与主人团聚了。和它的主人，金先生的邻居。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Where was the black cat found?","opts":["At the gate of a grade school in Kent","Under the engine cover of a man’s car","Inside the car of David King's neighbour","Outside the office of a charity foundation"],"answer":1,"expl":"「found curled up under the engine cover of David King's car」——under the engine cover 原词复现。","signal":"新闻首段定位","syn":[["under the engine cover of...car","Under the engine cover of a man's car（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do we learn about the cat at the end of the news report?","opts":["It got reunited with its owner","It was injured during the rescue","It was placed in the care of a UK charity","It became a pet of Mr. King’s grandson"],"answer":0,"expl":"「the four year old cat was later reunited with its owner」——reunited 原词复现。","signal":"新闻结尾","syn":[["reunited with its owner","It got reunited with its owner（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512a-2","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"体育赛事","level":"四级","title":"特奥会春季运动会","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 2（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"In less than a month, the Special Olympics Spring Games will make a return to Fayetteville.","zh":"不到一个月的时间，特殊奥林匹克运动会春季运动会将重返费耶特维尔。"},{"en":"The Games are coming back for the first time in five years.","zh":"奥运会即将回归，迎来第一届。五年后的时间。"},{"en":"The event will take place at Methodist University.","zh":"活动将在卫理公会大学举行。"},{"en":"Event organizer, Benjamin Kowalczyk, says he's excited that athletes will get a chance to come back and demonstrate their abilities.","zh":"活动组织者本杰明·科瓦尔奇克表示，他对此感到兴奋。运动员将有机会重返赛场。并展示他们的能力。"},{"en":"Organizers expect about a hundred athletes will come out to compete in Fayetteville.","zh":"组织者预计将有大约一百名运动员参加。前往费耶特维尔参赛。"},{"en":"They will have a variety of events to choose from, including running, throwing, and jumping.","zh":"他们将举办各种各样的活动可选择的运动包括跑步、投掷和跳跃。"},{"en":"There will also be a fun tent for children.","zh":"还会有一个有趣的帐篷孩子们。"},{"en":"Kowalczyk said it's rewarding to see athletes with special needs triumph in the Games.","zh":"科瓦尔奇克表示，看到运动员们……令人欣慰。特殊需求群体在奥运会上取得胜利。"},{"en":"For anyone who wants to help make this year's Games a massive success, there are still opportunities to volunteer for Fayetteville's Special Olympics.","zh":"任何想参与制作的人都可以考虑。今年的奥运会取得了巨大的成功，但仍有……有机会成为费耶特维尔特殊奥林匹克运动会的志愿者。"},{"en":"Organizers encourage them to visit the Games website to sign up.","zh":"组织者鼓励他们访问奥运会网站。注册。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What will Fayetteville witness in less than a month?","opts":["The reunion of this year’s Olympic gold medalists","The opening of the Special Olympics Spring Games","The first important political event in the next five years","The 100th anniversary celebration of Methodist University"],"answer":1,"expl":"「the Special Olympics Spring Games will make a return to Fayetteville」——make a return 同义替换 opening。","signal":"时间限定 less than a month","syn":[["will make a return to Fayetteville","The opening of the Special Olympics Spring Games（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did Benjamin Kowalczyk say is rewarding to see?","opts":["V olunteers visit the Games’ website to sign up","Children play in a fun tent and enjoy themselves fully","Organizers devote their time and energy to the Games","Athletes with special needs triumph in the Game"],"answer":3,"expl":"「it's rewarding to see athletes with special needs triumph in the Games」——原词复现。","signal":"rewarding to see 定位","syn":[["athletes with special needs triumph in the Games","Athletes with special needs triumph in the Games（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512a-3","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"法治商业","level":"四级","title":"巧克力兔子版权案","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 3（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"a German supermarket has been ordered to destroy its chocolate rabbits after it lost a court battle with a Swiss chocolate manufacturer.","zh":"新闻报道三，一家德国超市……被勒令销毁其巧克力兔子后在与一家瑞士巧克力公司的官司中败诉制造商。"},{"en":"The Swiss firm had argued its gold-wrapped chocolate rabbit deserved copyright protection from a similar product sold by the budget supermarket.","zh":"这家瑞士公司辩称，其镀金的巧克力兔子理应受到版权保护，免受类似作品的侵害。这家廉价超市出售的产品。"},{"en":"Switzerland's highest court agreed and overturned a ruling last year by the country's commercial court that had sided with the supermarket.","zh":"瑞士最高法院同意了这一观点，并推翻了之前的裁决。去年，该国商业法庭裁定：站在了超市一边。"},{"en":"It ordered that all the imitation rabbits be destroyed, but suggested the chocolate needn't be wasted.","zh":"它下令所有仿制兔子……虽然巧克力被毁了，但他建议不必浪费。"},{"en":"It could be melted for use in other products.","zh":"它可以熔化后用于其他用途。产品。"},{"en":"It said even though there are some differences between the two products, there was still the possibility of confusion for consumers.","zh":"它说，尽管存在一些差异。这两种产品之间仍然存在着……可能导致消费者混淆。"},{"en":"The Swiss manufacturer's rabbit has a red bow and bell, while the German supermarket's has a green bow and bell.","zh":"瑞士制造商的兔子系着一个红色蝴蝶结还有铃铛，而德国超市则有绿色蝴蝶结和铃铛。"},{"en":"The color of the wrapper is similar, as are the illustrations of the features.","zh":"包装纸的颜色也相似，因为这些是各项功能的图示。"},{"en":"The chocolate company has been to court before to protect its popular chocolate treat.","zh":"这家巧克力公司之前就上过法庭。为了保护其广受欢迎的巧克力产品。"},{"en":"Last year, a German federal court said the shade of the gold wrapping was also protected.","zh":"去年，德国联邦法院表示金色包装的色泽也得到了保护。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What has the German supermarket been ordered to do?","opts":["Compensate for the Swiss manufacturer's loss","Change the wrapping of its commodities","Destroy its imitation chocolate rabbits","Defend itself in the country's commercial court"],"answer":2,"expl":"「ordered to destroy its chocolate rabbits」——destroy 原词复现。","signal":"ordered to 定位","syn":[["destroy its chocolate rabbits","Destroy its imitation chocolate rabbits（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did Switzerland's highest court suggest about the chocolate in question?","opts":["It could be reused in other products","It could be resold cheaper to avoid waste","It could be reshaped into animals other than rabbits","It could be rewrapped and sold by the budget supermarket"],"answer":0,"expl":"「the chocolate needn't be wasted. It could be melted for use in other products」——melted 同义替换 reused。","signal":"but 转折后建议","syn":[["melted for use in other products","It could be reused in other products（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why did Switzerland's highest court overturn the commercial court's ruling?","opts":["To be fair to the German supermarkets","To protect chocolate retailers’ interests","To prevent consumers’ possible confusion","To boost the growth of the chocolate industry"],"answer":2,"expl":"「there was still the possibility of confusion for consumers」——possibility of confusion 同义替换 prevent confusion。","signal":"因果词 why","syn":[["possibility of confusion for consumers","To prevent consumers' possible confusion（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512a-4","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"饮食习惯","level":"四级","title":"素食主义男友","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 1（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Can you please hand me that book over there?","zh":"请把那本书递给我好吗？那里？"},{"en":"It has instructions for making a winter bean salad.","zh":"里面有制作冬豆的说明。沙拉。"},{"en":"My sister's boyfriend is coming over for dinner.","zh":"我姐姐的男朋友要来我家吃晚饭。"},{"en":"He's vegetarian, so I need to make a lot of vegetable dishes.","zh":"他是素食主义者，所以我需要做一份很多蔬菜菜肴。"},{"en":"He only eats vegetables, no meat?","zh":"他只吃蔬菜，不吃肉？"},{"en":"That doesn't sound like a very balanced diet.","zh":"听起来这饮食不太均衡。"},{"en":"How can he get enough protein?","zh":"他如何才能摄取足够的蛋白质？"},{"en":"What does he do to strengthen his muscles and all that?","zh":"他通过什么方式来增强肌肉力量？还有那些？"},{"en":"Apparently, that's no problem.","zh":"显然，这不成问题。"},{"en":"He's explained this to me when we first of.","zh":"他第一次跟我解释过这件事。的。"},{"en":"He eats a variety of different vegetables and nuts, especially those with high amounts of protein.","zh":"他吃各种各样的蔬菜，坚果，尤其是那些蛋白质含量高的坚果。"},{"en":"It sounds a bit difficult, but he's vegetarian.","zh":"听起来有点难，但他是个素食主义者。"},{"en":"What's his reasoning for being vegetarian?","zh":"他为什么会成为素食主义者？"},{"en":"Is it his religion, health condition, or lifestyle?","zh":"是他的宗教信仰、健康状况还是生活方式？"},{"en":"He's an animal activist.","zh":"他是一位动物保护主义者。"},{"en":"He's always been very sensitive and sympathizes with animals.","zh":"他一直都很敏感，也很有同情心。动物。"},{"en":"He's even written to his state senator about the torture of dolphins in sea parks.","zh":"他甚至还给他的州参议员写信谈到此事。在海洋公园里虐待海豚。"},{"en":"He says that keeping animals in zoos and parks causes them great distress.","zh":"他说，把动物关在动物园里，公园给他们带来了极大的痛苦。"},{"en":"That's a little gloomy, but I can understand that to a point.","zh":"这有点悲观，但我能理解。某种程度上是这样。"},{"en":"Not all zoos and animal parks have the most favorable conditions.","zh":"并非所有动物园和动物公园都拥有最有利的条件。"},{"en":"But without them, it just wouldn't be feasible to learn about animals and their environments.","zh":"但如果没有他们，这根本无法实现。了解动物及其生存环境。"},{"en":"Besides, I don't think I could ever give up a good hot dog at a baseball game.","zh":"此外，我觉得我永远也无法给予。在棒球场上吃个美味的热狗游戏。"},{"en":"Honestly, I agree, but just don't let him hear you say that.","zh":"说实话，我同意，但别让他得逞。听到你这么说了。"},{"en":"He's the spokesperson for his local animal rights group.","zh":"他是当地动物权利组织的发言人。团体。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the man request the woman to do?","opts":["Pass a book to him","Make a vegetable dish","Return the handbook to him","Meet his sister's boyfriend"],"answer":0,"expl":"「Can you please hand me that book over there?」——hand me 同义替换 pass to。","signal":"对话首句请求","syn":[["hand me that book","Pass a book to him（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the woman say about eating vegetables only?","opts":["It doesn't sound practical for her","It would do harm to one's muscles","It would reduce one's protein intake","It doesn't seem to be a balanced diet"],"answer":3,"expl":"「That doesn't sound like a very balanced diet」——原词复现。","signal":"评价句","syn":[["not a very balanced diet","It doesn't seem to be a balanced diet（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why does the boyfriend of the man's sister choose to be a vegetarian?","opts":["To improve his health","To protect animal rights","To stick to his religious belief","To follow a trendy lifestyle"],"answer":1,"expl":"「He's an animal activist...sympathizes with animals」——activist + sympathize 同义替换 protect animal rights。","signal":"因果自述","syn":[["sympathizes with animals","To protect animal rights（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"On what point does the man agree with the woman at the end of the conversation?","opts":["The torture and distress dolphins suffer in parks","The urgency of joining an animal rights group","The gloomy environments animals are kept in","The necessity of having zoos and eating meat"],"answer":3,"expl":"「Honestly, I agree」之前他说「without them, it just wouldn't be feasible to learn about animals」+「I don't think I could ever give up a good hot dog」——既认园地必要又不放弃吃肉。","signal":"I agree 定位","syn":[["wouldn't be feasible to learn about animals","The necessity of having zoos and eating meat（推断归纳）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512a-5","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"健康出行","level":"四级","title":"倒时差与恐飞","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 2（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Did you see that television program on air travel last night?","zh":"你看了那个电视节目吗？昨晚出行？"},{"en":"Yes, the part about overcoming jet lag was interesting.","zh":"是的，克服时差的那部分内容是有趣的。"},{"en":"I was surprised that the expert recommended not eating for the entire journey and avoiding sleeping on the plane.","zh":"专家建议不要这样做，这让我很惊讶。旅途中全程进食，避免睡眠在飞机上。"},{"en":"I was too, as I read an article on the subject in the past that suggested the opposite.","zh":"我读了一篇文章后也有同样的感受。过去曾就此主题提出过一些建议恰恰相反。"},{"en":"It claimed that it was important not to miss meals and that taking a nap on the plane was the best way to adjust to a new time zone.","zh":"它声称，重要的是不要错过正餐和午睡飞机是调整的最佳方式切换到新的时区。"},{"en":"Well, the expert on the show did cite research supporting her recommendations, so I guess I'll give it a try next time I fly a long distance.","zh":"节目中的专家确实引用了……有研究支持她的建议，所以我想我会下次我坐飞机的时候试试。很远的距离。"},{"en":"Jet lag is a big problem for me and has been for the last few years, even though I never suffered from it before.","zh":"时差对我来说是个大问题。而且这种情况已经持续了好几年。尽管我以前从未患过这种病。"},{"en":"Well, she did say that jet lag often becomes more of a problem after 40, so I guess I'm lucky that I can still adjust to different time zones well.","zh":"嗯，她确实说过时差反应经常40岁以后这个问题会变得更加严重，所以我想我很幸运，还能……能够很好地适应不同的时区。"},{"en":"My problem is I'm afraid to fly.","zh":"我的问题是，我害怕坐飞机。"},{"en":"Oh, I didn't know that.","zh":"哦，我不知道。"},{"en":"Actually, my mother is terrified of airplanes to the point where she can't even fly, so our family vacations were always by car or train.","zh":"事实上，我母亲非常害怕坐飞机。她甚至都飞不起来，所以……我们家的度假总是开车或火车。"},{"en":"I'm not as bad as that.","zh":"我没那么糟糕。"},{"en":"I just get anxious before I fly and feel nervous the whole time we're in the air, which is why I was hoping the television program would cover that topic more than it did.","zh":"我每次坐飞机前都会感到焦虑。在场的整个过程中我都感到紧张。空气，所以我才希望电视节目会更详细地报道这个话题。确实如此。"},{"en":"Yeah, that segment was too brief, especially as so many people have that problem.","zh":"是的，那段内容太短了，尤其是……很多人都有这个问题。"},{"en":"She said 20% of people are afraid to fly.","zh":"她说，20%的人感到害怕。飞行。"},{"en":"Actually, it was a quarter of people, so the problem really is widespread and deserves attention.","zh":"实际上，是四分之一的人，所以这个问题确实很普遍，值得关注。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What part of the TV program does the man say was interesting?","opts":["The part about not eating on board the plane","The part about air travel in the past","The part about getting over jetlag","The part about avoiding sleeping on the plane"],"answer":2,"expl":"「the part about overcoming jet lag was interesting」——overcoming 同义替换 getting over。","signal":"评价句","syn":[["overcoming jet lag","getting over jetlag（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man say he will do next time he flies a long distance?","opts":["Try following the advice given by the expert on the show","Concentrate on reading articles recommended by experts","Have meals as usual to stay away from hunger","Take a nap to adjust to a new time zone"],"answer":0,"expl":"「I guess I'll give it a try next time I fly a long distance」——it 指专家建议（不吃不睡）。","signal":"give it a try","syn":[["give it a try","Try following the advice given by the expert（指代还原）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why does the woman think she is lucky?","opts":["She has been well treated when traveling","She does not have to worry about jetlag","She can spend a lot of time vacationing","She does not have any problem flying"],"answer":1,"expl":"「I'm lucky that I can still adjust to different time zones well」——能调时差即不受 jetlag 困扰。","signal":"lucky 自我评价","syn":[["still adjust to different time zones well","does not have to worry about jetlag（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why does the woman think the problem of being afraid to fly deserves attention?","opts":["It affects twenty-five percent of people","It has long been ignored by many experts","It impacts female travelers more seriously","It has caused heavy losses to many airlines"],"answer":0,"expl":"「it was a quarter of people, so the problem really is widespread」——a quarter 同义替换 twenty-five percent。","signal":"数字修正题","syn":[["a quarter of people","It affects twenty-five percent of people（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512a-6","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"职业发展","level":"四级","title":"如何入行用户体验设计","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 1（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"the most common question I'm asked always centers around how to get started in user experience design, to which my response is always that nothing can substitute real world experience.","zh":"第一段，也是我被问到最多的问题始终围绕如何开始展开用户体验设计，对此我的回应是始终要记住，没有什么能替代现实世界的经验。"},{"en":"Building the skills required of a user experience designer takes time, patience, and commitment.","zh":"培养用户体验所需的技能设计需要时间、耐心和投入。"},{"en":"Higher education is a great way to equip yourself with some core skills, but it will not prepare you for actual challenges you'll face with client's work.","zh":"高等教育是提升自身能力的绝佳途径。你需要掌握一些核心技能，但这会它无法让你为真正将要面临的挑战做好准备。和客户一起工作。"},{"en":"In other words, being proficient with a design tool and a few methods doesn't make you a user experience designer.","zh":"换句话说，精通设计工具和一些方法并不能让你……用户体验设计师。"},{"en":"There simply isn't a one size fits all process.","zh":"根本不存在一刀切的方案过程。"},{"en":"Being effective requires adaptability, something you don't really learn in school, much less in a six month training camp.","zh":"要想高效，就需要适应能力，而你恰恰缺乏这种能力。在学校里学，在六年里学就更少了。为期一个月的训练营。"},{"en":"It's gained through experience on the job and learning what's appropriate given the needs of the project.","zh":"这是通过工作经验获得的，根据需求学习什么是合适的项目。"},{"en":"I found my way to user experience through graphic design and slowly over many different roles and experiences that led me to become a user experience designer.","zh":"我通过以下途径找到了用户体验之路平面设计，并逐渐涉猎多种不同的角色以及促使我成为……的经历用户体验设计师。"},{"en":"It took time and commitment to continue to pursue roles within teams that I knew could teach and challenge me.","zh":"继续下去需要时间和投入我知道自己有能力在团队中担任某些角色。请教导我，挑战我。"},{"en":"That's not to say that I think my path is the only one, but once again, nothing can substitute real world experience.","zh":"这并不是说我认为我的这条路是唯一的，但再一次，没有什么能替代真实世界的经验。"},{"en":"You can start anywhere as long as you know your end goal and you commit to actively pursuing opportunities to learn and grow along the way.","zh":"只要你愿意，你可以从任何地方开始。明确你的最终目标并为此做出承诺积极寻求学习和成长的机会道路。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the speaker think is the best way to get started in user experience design?","opts":["Learning from skilled designers","Joining a 6-month training camp","Obtaining real-world experience","Anticipating actual challenges"],"answer":2,"expl":"「nothing can substitute real world experience」——substitute 同义替换 obtaining。","signal":"重复强调两次","syn":[["nothing can substitute real world experience","Obtaining real-world experience（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the speaker say being effective requires?","opts":["Core skills","Higher education","Capability","Adaptability"],"answer":3,"expl":"「Being effective requires adaptability」——原词复现。","signal":"requires 定位","syn":[["requires adaptability","Adaptability（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What can people do as long as they know their end goal and strive for it?","opts":["Face challenges","Start anywhere","Pursue roles in teams","Follow their own path"],"answer":1,"expl":"「You can start anywhere as long as you know your end goal」——原词复现。","signal":"as long as 条件","syn":[["You can start anywhere","Start anywhere（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512a-7","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"教育创新","level":"四级","title":"灵活座位进课堂","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 2（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"when planning for this year, our principal asked what needed to change to engage students more in their learning.","zh":"第二段，在制定今年的计划时，我们的校长询问需要做出哪些改变才能提高参与度。学生们在学习中更加投入。"},{"en":"I responded in a whisper, flexible seating, thinking about our then current classroom.","zh":"我低声回应道：“灵活的座位安排。”我心想。关于我们当时的教室。"},{"en":"It had rows of desks with blue chairs and nameplates reminding each student where they should be sitting.","zh":"里面摆放着一排排桌子和蓝色椅子。以及提醒每个学生他们应该在哪里的姓名牌。坐下。"},{"en":"This began a journey to transform our practice and challenge the ways of learning for a group of year six students used to sitting in desks and rows for years.","zh":"这开启了我们实践转型之旅。并挑战现有的学习方式一群六年级学生习惯于坐着多年来，他们一直坐在办公桌和排排的桌子旁。"},{"en":"Flexible seating has been defined as movable furniture to create an engaging learning environment.","zh":"灵活座椅被定义为可移动家具营造一个引人入胜的学习环境。"},{"en":"It is a shift in practice from being teacher focused to student focused learning.","zh":"这是实践方式的转变，从……教师以学生为中心的学习方式。"},{"en":"For us, flexible seating has meant removing most of the traditional chairs and desks and introducing a variety of different seating options to promote student engagement.","zh":"对我们来说，灵活座位意味着移除大部分座位。传统的桌椅，以及引入多种不同的座位选择以促进学生参与度。"},{"en":"The use of rows and their minimal adaptations to U shape were traditionally intended to maximize on task behavior and reduce distraction from the teacher.","zh":"行的使用及其最小调整U形设计传统上是为了最大限度地利用空间。专注于任务行为并减少干扰老师。"},{"en":"Teachers tend to still use this format because of either the need to control students or the belief that the teacher is the most important person in the room.","zh":"教师们仍然倾向于使用这种格式，因为要么是出于控制学生的需要，要么认为教师是最……的信念房间里的重要人物。"},{"en":"Now, our students have a range of different seating options, including a floor desk, couches, stools, beanbags, and the traditional desk and chair.","zh":"现在，我们的学生拥有各种不同的座位选择包括落地桌、沙发、凳子等。豆袋椅，以及传统的书桌和椅子。"},{"en":"From our experience so far, flexible seating enhances student ownership of space and engagement in learning while reducing rates of student disengagement and disciplinary actions.","zh":"根据我们目前的经验，灵活的座位安排可以提升……学生对学习空间的自主权和学习参与度同时降低学生辍学率和违纪率。行动。"},{"en":"It is a win for all concerned.","zh":"这对所有相关方来说都是双赢。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why did the school principal ask what needed to change?","opts":["To allow students more freedom in their academic work","To enable teachers to interact more with their students","To engage students more in their learning","To respond actively to students' requests"],"answer":2,"expl":"「asked what needed to change to engage students more in their learning」——原词复现。","signal":"目的不定式","syn":[["to engage students more in their learning","To engage students more in their learning（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What has flexible seating meant at the speaker's school?","opts":["Rearranging most traditional chairs and desks","Adopting a variety of different seating options","Shifting from traditional teaching to task-based learning","Using new furniture to create a comfortable environment"],"answer":1,"expl":"「flexible seating has meant removing most of the traditional chairs and desks and introducing a variety of different seating options」——introducing 同义替换 adopting；干扰项「rearranging（重新摆放）」与原文 removing（移除）矛盾。","signal":"has meant 定位","syn":[["introducing a variety of different seating options","Adopting a variety of different seating options（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What has flexible seating brought about at the speaker's school?","opts":["A change to teachers’ opinion of their students","A harmonious relationship among its students","A strengthened effect of its discipline","A win for all people involved"],"answer":3,"expl":"「It is a win for all concerned」——原词复现。","signal":"结尾总结","syn":[["a win for all concerned","A win for all people involved（同义替换 concerned→involved）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512a-8","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"校园社会","level":"四级","title":"穿错鞋被停课","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 3（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"dozens of British students arriving for their first day of school on Tuesday were sent home over their shoes.","zh":"第三段，数十名英国学生抵达周二是他们开学的第一天。因为鞋子的原因被遣送回家。"},{"en":"About 30 students were turned away from Taverham High School in Norfolk, England.","zh":"大约30名学生被塔弗汉姆学校拒之门外英国诺福克郡的一所高中。"},{"en":"Head teacher, Dr. Roger Harris, confirmed that this was due to a change in the school's uniform policy.","zh":"校长罗杰·哈里斯博士证实了这一点。这是由于学校的政策变化造成的。统一政策。"},{"en":"Harris, who became head teacher this year, said he notified parents of the updated rules in an email in June.","zh":"今年刚上任校长的哈里斯说他已将更新后的规则通知了家长。六月份的一封电子邮件。"},{"en":"The price of school uniforms can spark panic among families struggling with the high cost of living.","zh":"校服价格可能引发恐慌对于那些难以承受高昂生活成本的家庭来说活的。"},{"en":"Nearly all British schools have uniforms.","zh":"几乎所有英国学校都要求穿校服。"},{"en":"They cost parents an average of £337 per year for each secondary school child.","zh":"它们平均每套售价为337英镑，由家长购买。每个中学生每年。"},{"en":"According to the new rules, students of Taverham are required to wear smart black shoes appropriate for the workplace.","zh":"根据新规定，塔弗汉姆的学生必须穿着得体的黑色皮鞋。适用于工作场所。"},{"en":"Harris held that strengthened rules around school uniforms improved student outcomes and behaviour.","zh":"哈里斯认为，加强校服相关规定是必要的。学生成绩和行为得到改善。"},{"en":"But for some parents, the school's restrictions are an unnecessary burden.","zh":"但对一些家长来说，学校的限制是不必要的负担。"},{"en":"As annual inflation climbs over 10%, many households are on tight budgets.","zh":"随着年通货膨胀率超过10%，许多家庭预算很紧张。"},{"en":"Private rental prices in Britain rose 3.2 % over the 12 months to July 2022, the largest jump since 2016.","zh":"英国私人租赁价格上涨了3.2%。截至2022年7月的12个月内，百分比这是自 2016 年以来最大的涨幅。"},{"en":"Soaring energy bills have made things worse.","zh":"能源账单飙升使情况变得更糟。"},{"en":"Lucinda May, mum of a Taverham student, said that she had to ask her parents for £65 to buy her child the correct pair of shoes.","zh":"一位名叫露辛达·梅的塔弗汉姆学生的母亲说她不得不向父母求助。65英镑，她要给孩子买一双合适的鞋子。鞋子。"},{"en":"May said that the school's uniform policy showed a lack of regard for parents dealing with the high cost of living.","zh":"梅表示，学校的校服政策表明对正在应对此事的父母缺乏尊重生活成本高昂。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why were dozens of British students sent home on Tuesday?","opts":["They arrived late for their first day of school","They weren't informed of the school’s updated rules","They answered their headteacher's email in an impolite way","They didn't wear the shoes required by the school’s new policy"],"answer":3,"expl":"「sent home over their shoes...required to wear smart black shoes appropriate for the workplace」——没穿新规要求的鞋；干扰项「邮件不礼貌」无中生有（邮件只是通知规则）。","signal":"over 引出原因 + due to","syn":[["sent home over their shoes","They didn't wear the shoes required by the school's new policy（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What can the price of school uniforms spark among families in financial difficulty?","opts":["Panic","Anger","Disputes","Riots"],"answer":0,"expl":"「The price of school uniforms can spark panic among families」——spark panic 原词复现。","signal":"spark 因果动词","syn":[["spark panic","Panic（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did the head teacher think of the school's new uniform rules?","opts":["They rendered the school unique in the district","They enhanced the positive image of the school","They improved student behavior and performance","They strengthened the school's discipline and order"],"answer":2,"expl":"「strengthened rules around school uniforms improved student outcomes and behaviour」——improved 同义替换。","signal":"人名观点定位","syn":[["improved student outcomes and behaviour","They improved student behavior and performance（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did Lucinda May have to do to buy her child the correct pair of shoes?","opts":["Tighten her monthly budget","Turn to her parents for help","Borrow £65 from her friend","Postpone paying her other bills"],"answer":1,"expl":"「she had to ask her parents for £65」——ask her parents for 同义替换 turn to her parents for help。","signal":"人名定位","syn":[["ask her parents for £65","Turn to her parents for help（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512b-1","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会经济","level":"四级","title":"走私鸡蛋风潮","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 1（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Customs and Border Protection officials are seeing a rise in people illegally bringing eggs from Mexico into border states such as Texas.","zh":"新闻报道 1 海关和边境保护官员非法携带物品的人数正在增加。墨西哥的鸡蛋运往边境各州，例如德克萨斯州。"},{"en":"The U.S. average price for a dozen large eggs last month hit $4.25. That's more than double their $1.78 price in December 2023.","zh":"美国一打的平均价格上个月大鸡蛋的价格达到了4.25美元。价格翻了一番还多，达到 1.78 美元。2023年12月。"},{"en":"Meanwhile, 30 eggs in Mexico sell for just $3.40. Those bringing eggs into the U .S. risk fines of up to $10,000.","zh":"与此同时，墨西哥30个鸡蛋的售价仅为3.40美元。那些携带鸡蛋进入美国的人.S. 面临最高 10,000 美元的罚款。"},{"en":"But officials say they usually seize and destroy the eggs.","zh":"但官员们表示，他们通常会缴获并销毁这些物品。鸡蛋。"},{"en":"They also impose a $300 penalty.","zh":"他们还会处以 300 美元的罚款。"},{"en":"The Department of Agriculture banned eggs from Mexico in 2012.","zh":"美国农业部禁止进口墨西哥鸡蛋。2012年。"},{"en":"This was due to the risk of bird flu.","zh":"这是由于鸟类带来的风险造成的。流感。"},{"en":"Officials said most people arriving at international borders with eggs are truthful about their purchases.","zh":"官员表示，大多数抵达国际边境的人鸡蛋销售商对他们的购买情况如实相告。"},{"en":"They simply don't know bringing eggs is not allowed.","zh":"他们根本不知道带鸡蛋是不合适的。允许。"},{"en":"Generally, the items are declared during the first inspection.","zh":"一般来说，这些物品会在第一阶段申报。检查。"},{"en":"Then, the person can abandon the eggs without consequence, a Customs and Border Protection spokesperson said.","zh":"然后，这个人就可以把鸡蛋扔掉而不用。海关与边境保护局发言人表示，后果就是如此。"},{"en":"Even so, there have been a very small number of cases recently when authorities discovered eggs during further inspections.","zh":"即便如此，也存在一些非常小的现象。最近当局发现鸡蛋的案件数量较多在进一步检查中。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn from the news report about the egg price in the U.S.?","opts":["It has gone up sharply","It has been fluctuating","It has risen because of bird flu","It has been consumers’ concern"],"answer":0,"expl":"「$4.25...more than double their $1.78 price in December 2023」——翻倍以上即 sharply 上涨。","signal":"数字对比题","syn":[["more than double","It has gone up sharply（数字推断）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the news report say about most people arriving at American borders with eggs?","opts":["They don’t want to abandon their eggs","They don’t know they will be heavily fined","They don’t know they are forbidden to bring eggs","They don’t declare their eggs during the inspection"],"answer":2,"expl":"「They simply don't know bringing eggs is not allowed」——don't know 同义替换 forbidden。","signal":"most people 定位","syn":[["don't know bringing eggs is not allowed","They don't know they are forbidden to bring eggs（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512b-2","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会争议","level":"四级","title":"餐厅拒绝儿童","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 2（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Nettie's House, a restaurant in America, has been hit with criticism after announcing on their website that children under the age of 10 are no longer welcome.","zh":"新闻报道 2 Nettie's House，一家位于美国在宣布这一消息后遭到了批评。他们的网站上说，未成年人其中10人不再受欢迎。"},{"en":"Among the reasons given for the decision, the restaurant cited noise levels, lack of space for high chairs, cleaning up crazy messes, and the liability of kids running around the restaurant.","zh":"在给出的决定理由中，有以下几点：餐厅方面指出噪音过大、空间不足等问题。高脚椅、清理各种乱七八糟的东西，以及儿童在餐厅内乱跑可能产生的责任。"},{"en":"They decided that it was time to take control.","zh":"他们决定是时候行动了控制。"},{"en":"The decision wasn't made lightly, but some recent events pushed them to implement this new policy.","zh":"做出这个决定并非轻率之举，而是出于近期的一些考虑。种种事件促使他们实施了这项新政策。"},{"en":"Responding to the post, one person commented that it is messed up beyond another level.","zh":"在该帖子下，有人评论说：情况糟透了，简直到了另一个层次。"},{"en":"Children are children.","zh":"孩子就是孩子。"},{"en":"Moms are tired and don't have time to cook.","zh":"妈妈们很累，没有时间厨师。"},{"en":"Not welcoming children under 10 is a complete slap in the face to families.","zh":"不欢迎10岁以下儿童是完全错误的。对家属来说，这是当头一棒。"},{"en":"He felt so disappointed in the establishment.","zh":"他对当权者感到非常失望。"},{"en":"There are others, however, who showed support for the restaurant's decision.","zh":"然而，也有其他人表示支持。餐厅的决定。"},{"en":"They said it has the right to implement any rules it wants.","zh":"他们说它有权实施它想制定什么规则就制定什么规则。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn about the restaurant Nettie's House?","opts":["It is no longer critical of younger customers","It has banned kids under 10 from dining there","It is no longer as noisy and crowded as before","It has implemented a decision to expand business"],"answer":1,"expl":"「children under the age of 10 are no longer welcome」——no longer welcome 同义替换 banned from dining。","signal":"新闻首句","syn":[["children under the age of 10 are no longer welcome","It has banned kids under 10 from dining there（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do supporters say in response to the restaurant's new policy?","opts":["It is fully aware of frequent customers' feelings","It caters to the tastes of different customers","It is entitled to adopt any rules it wants","It should announce its decisions online"],"answer":2,"expl":"「it has the right to implement any rules it wants」——have the right 同义替换 be entitled to。","signal":"however 转折后","syn":[["has the right to implement any rules it wants","It is entitled to adopt any rules it wants（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512b-3","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"自然趣闻","level":"四级","title":"搜捕巨蟒","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · News Report 3（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Security officers were searching a suburb in Australia where an adult snake was believed to be wandering after the discovery of a huge, freshly shed snake skin.","zh":"澳大利亚一处郊区正在接受安保人员的搜查。人们认为那里有一条成年蛇。在发现一个巨大的、新鲜的……之后四处游荡蛇蜕下的皮。"},{"en":"The skin was found at a construction site, and the government wrote to residents to warn them.","zh":"这具皮肤是在一个建筑工地发现的。政府致函居民发出警告。他们。"},{"en":"They were told to observe and, if possible, photograph the animal.","zh":"他们被告知要观察，如果可能的话，给动物拍照。"},{"en":"If it was moving, watch where it went.","zh":"如果它正在移动，就注意它去了哪里。"},{"en":"It was recommended not to make contact with the animal.","zh":"建议不要与……接触这只动物。"},{"en":"The type of snake was determined to be one of the world's largest snake species.","zh":"经鉴定，该蛇的种类为：世界上体型最大的蛇类之一。"},{"en":"It is not poisonous, but can still attack and kill its victims.","zh":"它没有毒，但仍然会攻击。并杀死它的受害者。"},{"en":"This type of snake is classified as a threat to humans, especially small children, as well as pets.","zh":"这种蛇被归类为对人类，尤其是幼儿，构成威胁作为宠物。"},{"en":"They may carry viruses that are fatal to native snakes, which do not have resistance.","zh":"它们可能携带致命病毒。本地蛇类，没有抵抗力。"},{"en":"If officers found the snake, they would employ a licensed snake catcher to catch it and transport it to a specialist animal doctor, the government said.","zh":"如果警员发现了这条蛇，他们会采取请一位持有执照的捕蛇人来捕捉它将其送往动物专科医生处。政府表示。"},{"en":"If caught, the snake would be examined to determine where it came from, how long it had been in the area, what it had been eating, whether it was carrying any diseases of concern, and whether it had produced babies.","zh":"如果抓到蛇，就会对其进行检查。确定它的来源，以及它的长度曾经在那个地区，它有什么是否食用过，是否携带任何疾病令人担忧的是，它是否产下了后代。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What were security officers searching for?","opts":["A missing pet","A grown-up snake","A huge animal skin","A snake specialist"],"answer":1,"expl":"「an adult snake was believed to be wandering」——adult 同义替换 grown-up。","signal":"searching 定位","syn":[["an adult snake","A grown-up snake（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Where was the huge snake skin found?","opts":["In a government office","In a deserted house","At a local zoo","At a construction site"],"answer":3,"expl":"「The skin was found at a construction site」——原词复现。","signal":"地点题","syn":[["found at a construction site","At a construction site（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What would be examined first if the snake was caught?","opts":["Figuring out where it came from","Curing it of any possible diseases","Protecting its babies against harm","Determining how to catch it safely"],"answer":0,"expl":"「examined to determine where it came from」——determine 同义替换 figure out。","signal":"列举第一项","syn":[["determine where it came from","Figuring out where it came from（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512b-4","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"财富故事","level":"四级","title":"中奖五百万之后","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 1（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Poor Hannah.","zh":"可怜的汉娜。"},{"en":"Why?","zh":"为什么？"},{"en":"What happened?","zh":"发生了什么？"},{"en":"Didn't you hear?","zh":"你没听说吗？"},{"en":"She won a TV competition and became a millionaire overnight.","zh":"她赢得了一项电视比赛，并成为了一名一夜暴富。"},{"en":"No way!","zh":"决不！"},{"en":"That's incredible!","zh":"那真是难以置信！"},{"en":"Are you kidding?","zh":"你在开玩笑吧？"},{"en":"No, I'm serious.","zh":"不，我是认真的。"},{"en":"I swear it.","zh":"我发誓。"},{"en":"She went on a TV show where they quiz on general knowledge, and she won first prize.","zh":"她参加了一个电视节目，他们在节目中她参加了一场常识问答比赛，并获得了第一名。奖。"},{"en":"Wow!","zh":"哇！"},{"en":"That's so lucky of her.","zh":"她真是太幸运了。"},{"en":"How much did she win?","zh":"她赢了多少钱？"},{"en":"I'm not sure of the exact figure, but it's a few million euros.","zh":"我不太确定具体数字，但是金额高达数百万欧元。"},{"en":"Maybe five million euros after tax.","zh":"税后或许能到五百万欧元。"},{"en":"I can't believe it.","zh":"我简直不敢相信。"},{"en":"You're really not joking, are you?","zh":"你不是在开玩笑吧？"},{"en":"Honestly, look at my face.","zh":"说实话，看看我的脸。"},{"en":"Our friend Hannah won a ton of money.","zh":"我们的朋友汉娜赢了一大笔钱。"},{"en":"Unbelievable.","zh":"难以置信。"},{"en":"Then why were you saying poor Hannah?","zh":"那你为什么说汉娜可怜呢？"},{"en":"Well, it turns out that she's spent it all already.","zh":"结果发现她已经花光了。都已经完成了。"},{"en":"Five million euros?","zh":"五百万欧元？"},{"en":"How is that even possible?","zh":"这怎么可能？"},{"en":"She bought a house for herself and her husband, a house for her parents, and then a house for each of her four brothers and sisters.","zh":"她给自己和家人买了一栋房子。丈夫，给她父母买的房子，然后她为她的四个兄弟每人买了一栋房子。还有姐妹们。"},{"en":"And then she bought her husband a ridiculously expensive sports car.","zh":"然后她给她丈夫买了一件极其荒谬的东西昂贵的跑车。"},{"en":"Wow!","zh":"哇！"},{"en":"Are they all happy?","zh":"他们都开心吗？"},{"en":"Because that's what matters, isn't it?","zh":"因为那才是最重要的，不是吗？"},{"en":"I know for a fact Hannah isn't.","zh":"我确信汉娜不是。"},{"en":"You see, she was planning to quit the job she hates and retire early.","zh":"你看，她原本打算辞职。她讨厌自己的工作，所以提前退休了。"},{"en":"But now that she ran out of money, she can't.","zh":"但现在她没钱了，她做不到。"},{"en":"Basically, she miscalculated how fast she was burning through the money.","zh":"基本上，她误判了自己燃烧的速度。通过金钱。"},{"en":"And she's now full of regret.","zh":"她现在后悔不已。"},{"en":"Why don't they sell that flashy new car?","zh":"为什么他们不卖那辆炫酷的新车？"},{"en":"She wants to, but her husband refuses to get rid of it.","zh":"她想这么做，但她丈夫拒绝。扔掉它。"},{"en":"He says the car is the best thing that has ever happened to him.","zh":"他说这辆车是最好的。这种事从未发生在他身上过。"},{"en":"And if she sells it, he will divorce her.","zh":"如果她卖掉房子，他就会离婚。她。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why does the man say 'Are you kidding?'","opts":["The man doesn't agree Hannah is poor","The man doesn't believe what she says","The man doesn't think she can be a millionaire","The man doesn't consider her to be trustworthy"],"answer":1,"expl":"听完 Hannah 中奖后男士连说「No way! That's incredible! Are you kidding?」——表示他不敢相信、觉得女士在开玩笑（随后才被 I swear it 说服）。","signal":"习语应答","syn":[["Are you kidding?","The man doesn't believe what she says（语境判断）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do we learn about Hannah from the conversation?","opts":["She no longer has any money left","She has been betrayed by her family","She can no longer hold on to her job","She has been robbed of 5 million Euros"],"answer":0,"expl":"「she's spent it all already...she ran out of money」——ran out of money 同义替换 no money left。","signal":"it turns out 转折","syn":[["ran out of money","She no longer has any money left（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man think really matters to people?","opts":["Fortune","Family","Harmony","Happiness"],"answer":1,"expl":"「Are they all happy? Because that's what matters, isn't it?」——they 指家人，家人的快乐即 Family。","signal":"反问句","syn":[["Are they all happy? Because that's what matters","Family（语境归纳）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does Hannah's husband say he'll do if she sells the new car?","opts":["Divorce her","Leave home","Buy her a more expensive model","Let the best thing happen to them"],"answer":0,"expl":"「if she sells it, he will divorce her」——原词复现。","signal":"if 条件句","syn":[["he will divorce her","Divorce her（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512b-5","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"家庭教育","level":"四级","title":"给杰克选学校","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 2（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"If you have time right now, I think we need to sit down and discuss what exactly we are going to do for Jake's education next year.","zh":"如果你现在有时间的话，我想我们需要坐下来讨论一下……我们正是要为杰克做这件事。明年继续教育。"},{"en":"I've been thinking it over, and I'd like to send him to Westwood Elementary.","zh":"我一直在考虑这件事，我希望送他去韦斯特伍德小学。"},{"en":"You mean that boarding school?","zh":"你是说那所寄宿学校吗？"},{"en":"I thought we agreed that we would not be sending him away at such a young age.","zh":"我以为我们已经说好了不会这么年轻就把他送走。年龄。"},{"en":"I admit that their academic record is very strong, with many outstanding awards for achievements in science and math.","zh":"我承认他们的学业成绩非常出色实力雄厚，在以下领域取得过许多杰出成就并荣获多项杰出奖项科学和数学。"},{"en":"But he is just not mature enough to live on his own at this point.","zh":"但他还不够成熟。他现在独自生活。"},{"en":"What about enrolling him in Lakeview School?","zh":"让他去湖景学校读书怎么样？"},{"en":"They do have a great outdoor campus, where he could finally learn all those outdoor sports you have been wanting him to try.","zh":"他们的户外校园环境很棒，他终于可以学习所有那些户外运动了。你一直希望他能尝试一下。"},{"en":"With so much greenery and fresh air, I think his current breathing problems would probably disappear.","zh":"这里绿树成荫，空气清新，我我认为他目前的呼吸问题可能会消失。"},{"en":"They did just open though, so I don't think I feel comfortable having our son in the first class of a brand new school.","zh":"他们刚开业，所以我也不确定。我觉得让儿子待在这里挺好的。这是一所全新学校的第一批学生。"},{"en":"Yeah, the classrooms would probably smell like paint, making the air in the school all stuffy.","zh":"是啊，教室里可能全是油漆味儿。学校里的空气变得非常闷热。"},{"en":"What about our local school then?","zh":"那么我们当地的学校呢？"},{"en":"They have a wonderful arts program that would really challenge Jake in terms of creativity and imagination.","zh":"他们有一个很棒的艺术项目，在创造力方面真正挑战杰克，想像力。"},{"en":"Being practically next door, one of us could take him to school every day before going to work.","zh":"由于我们几乎是邻居，我们中的一个就可以……每天上学前先送他去学校去工作。"},{"en":"I don't know, they have a reputation of being overly strict with the students.","zh":"我不知道，他们有这样的名声……对学生过于严厉。"},{"en":"Not to mention the overwhelming amount of homework they assign, which would lead to a lot of pressure for Jake and me.","zh":"更别提那堆积如山的作业了。他们会进行分配，这会导致很多问题。杰克和我都感到压力很大。"},{"en":"What if we send him to the place near your mother's house?","zh":"如果我们把他送到那个地方呢？在你母亲家附近吗？"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why does the man object to sending Jake to Westwood Elementary?","opts":["He is not outstanding in Science and Math","He does not have a strong academic record","He is not yet mature enough to live on his own","He does not like Westwood Elementary School"],"answer":2,"expl":"「he is just not mature enough to live on his own」——原词复现。","signal":"but 转折后","syn":[["not mature enough to live on his own","He is not yet mature enough to live on his own（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do we learn about Lakeview School?","opts":["It is too far away","It is newly opened","It lacks outdoor sports facilities","It has too few first-class teachers"],"answer":1,"expl":"「They did just open though」——just open 同义替换 newly opened。","signal":"did 强调","syn":[["did just open","It is newly opened（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What attracts the couple about the local school?","opts":["It has a beautiful campus","It is within walking distance","It has a wonderful arts program","It is helpful to Jake’s breathing problems"],"answer":2,"expl":"「They have a wonderful arts program」——原词复现。","signal":"wonderful 评价词","syn":[["a wonderful arts program","It has a wonderful arts program（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is the couple's last proposal for Jake's education?","opts":["Asking Jake which school he himself prefers to enroll in","Thinking twice about what is best for Jake’s education next year","Consulting her mother about which school Jake is to attend","Sending Jake to the school near the biome of the man's mother"],"answer":3,"expl":"「What if we send him to the place near your mother's house?」——what if 表提议，near your mother's house 即男士母亲家附近。","signal":"结尾 what if","syn":[["near your mother's house","Sending Jake to the school near the home of the man's mother（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512b-6","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"管理心理","level":"四级","title":"理性决策的利弊","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 1（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Analytical decision-making is a decision -making approach where a manager makes important business decisions only with solid data.","zh":"第一段 分析性决策是一种决策管理者采取一种制定重要业务策略的方法只有基于可靠数据才能做出决策。"},{"en":"This style contrasts with more instinctive leadership styles, where managers make many decisions using instinct or opinion.","zh":"这种风格与更偏向本能的领导风格形成鲜明对比。管理者常常凭直觉或本能做出许多决定。观点。"},{"en":"While analytical decision-makers benefit from a deliberate, thoughtful approach, this style also has some shortcomings.","zh":"分析型决策者虽然受益于深思熟虑，这种深思熟虑的方式也存在一些不足之处。"},{"en":"A key flaw with analytical decision-making is that it takes time.","zh":"分析决策的一个关键缺陷是这需要时间。"},{"en":"While this approach is beneficial when you have the time and the decision is important, it is problematic when time is crucial.","zh":"虽然这种方法在你拥有以下条件时是有益的：时间和决定都很重要。当时间至关重要时，这会造成问题。"},{"en":"Analytical decision-makers struggle with deadlines and a sense of urgency with decisions.","zh":"分析型决策者在截止日期和……方面面临挑战做决定时要有紧迫感。"},{"en":"In situations where you need more timely action, decisions based on some information and instinct may work better.","zh":"在需要更及时采取行动的情况下，基于某些信息和直觉做出的决定可能效果更好。"},{"en":"The desire to be right is a major driver of analytical decision-making.","zh":"渴望证明自己正确是一个主要因素分析决策的驱动因素。"},{"en":"Leaders who use this style don't want to make mistakes.","zh":"采用这种领导风格的领导者不希望犯错。"},{"en":"This commitment to one right way of thinking or doing things hinders the manager's flexibility.","zh":"这种对某种正确思维方式的执着或者，某些做法会妨碍管理者的灵活性。"},{"en":"Inflexibility causes you to ignore or avoid listening to the thoughts and ideas of others.","zh":"僵化会导致你忽视或回避倾听尊重他人的想法和观点。"},{"en":"You only want to utilise hard data or facts.","zh":"你只想利用硬数据，或者事实。"},{"en":"Despite its restrictions, analytical decision-making does have several key strengths.","zh":"尽管存在局限性，分析决策仍然具有一定的优势。几个关键优势。"},{"en":"By relying on facts and data, you minimise your potential for a wrong decision.","zh":"通过依靠事实和数据，你可以最大限度地减少你做出错误决定的可能性。"},{"en":"You also get away from the habit of making guesses or following instincts.","zh":"你也能摆脱以下习惯：靠猜测或凭直觉行事。"},{"en":"Database technology enables business leaders to look to hard evidence in analysing target markets and promotional strategies, rather than making assumptions or guesses on what works.","zh":"数据库技术使企业领导者能够展望未来分析目标市场和促销活动的确凿证据制定策略，而不是做出假设或猜测行之有效的方法。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What is a major flaw of analytical decision-making?","opts":["It is time consuming","It is unfit for crucial issues","It relies too much on solid data","It dulls a leader's sense of urgency"],"answer":0,"expl":"「A key flaw...is that it takes time」——takes time 同义替换 time consuming。","signal":"key flaw 定位","syn":[["it takes time","It is time consuming（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does a leader tend to do when committed to analytical decision-making?","opts":["Depend on digital technology","Make assumptions and guesses","Ignore others’ thoughts and ideas","Lay emphasis on thinking flexibly"],"answer":2,"expl":"「Inflexibility causes you to ignore or avoid listening to the thoughts and ideas of others」——ignore 同义替换。","signal":"causes 因果","syn":[["ignore...the thoughts and ideas of others","Ignore others' thoughts and ideas（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is a key strength of analytical decision-making?","opts":["Maximizing the advantage of available resources","Minimizing the possibility of a wrong decision","Discovering new potential markets","Perfecting promotional strategies"],"answer":1,"expl":"「you minimise your potential for a wrong decision」——minimise potential 同义替换 minimizing possibility。","signal":"strengths 定位","syn":[["minimise your potential for a wrong decision","Minimizing the possibility of a wrong decision（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512b-7","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"人物故事","level":"四级","title":"世界最长寿者的秘诀","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 2（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"What is the secret to living past 100?","zh":"长寿过百的秘诀是什么？"},{"en":"Playing the piano is among the things the world's oldest person believes has contributed to her long life.","zh":"弹钢琴是其中一件事情世界上最长寿的人相信自己对她的健康做出了贡献。长寿。"},{"en":"Brañas Morera is now 115 years and 320 days old.","zh":"布拉尼亚斯·莫雷拉现年115岁，320岁几天大了。"},{"en":"That means she's been alive longer than any other living individual.","zh":"这意味着她比任何人都活得更久。其他在世个体。"},{"en":"Brañas was born in the United States on April 4, 1907, but her family moved to Spain, where they were originally from, when she was a young child.","zh":"布拉尼亚斯出生于美国1907年4月4日，但她的家人搬到了西班牙，她们的故乡，在她出生的时候当时他还是个孩子。"},{"en":"She has lived there ever since.","zh":"她从那以后就一直住在那里。"},{"en":"The 115-year-old is active on social media, regularly sharing aspects of her life.","zh":"这位115岁的老人活跃于社交媒体。媒体经常与她分享她的生活点滴。"},{"en":"She also shares some of her secrets to living so long.","zh":"她还分享了一些她的秘诀活得真长。"},{"en":"These include playing the piano from a young age.","zh":"这包括从小学习钢琴。年龄。"},{"en":"Unfortunately, she had to give up the practice seven years ago, at 108.","zh":"很遗憾，她不得不放弃这项练习。七年前，他108岁。"},{"en":"Her other secrets for living a long life?","zh":"她长寿的其他秘诀是什么？"},{"en":"She led an active lifestyle until her later years, but has never followed a specific diet.","zh":"她生前一直过着积极健康的生活方式。多年来，他从未遵循过特定的饮食习惯。"},{"en":"Many people ask me what diet I follow to live so many years, Brañas wrote.","zh":"很多人问我遵循什么饮食习惯。布拉尼亚斯写道：“能活这么多年。”"},{"en":"I have always eaten little, but everything, and I have never followed any plan.","zh":"我一直以来吃得很少，但什么都吃，我从来没有按照任何计划行事。"},{"en":"But she does eat yogurt every day, which, she said, has an infinite number of positive properties for the body.","zh":"但她每天都吃酸奶，这她说，有无穷多个正数。对身体有益。"},{"en":"She has also said that the secret to a long life is knowing how to choose what to forget.","zh":"她还说过，秘诀在于长寿之道在于懂得如何选择应该忘记什么？"},{"en":"Life would be impossible if we remembered everything, she said.","zh":"如果我们记住所有事情，生活将无法进行。她说。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What do we learn about Brañas Morera?","opts":["She is one of the world's best-known pianists","She celebrated her 110th birthday this April","She moved to the U.S. at a young age","She is the world’s oldest individual"],"answer":3,"expl":"「she's been alive longer than any other living individual」——同义替换 the world's oldest individual。","signal":"数字年龄定位","syn":[["alive longer than any other living individual","She is the world's oldest individual（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is one of Brañas Morera's secrets to living a long life?","opts":["Being always active on social media","Doing regular and vigorous exercise","Playing the piano from a young age","Following a specific diet every day"],"answer":2,"expl":"「These include playing the piano from a young age」——原词复现。","signal":"secrets 列举","syn":[["playing the piano from a young age","Playing the piano from a young age（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does Brañas Morera think also contributes to a long life?","opts":["Eating as little as one can possibly manage","Having the ability to forget things selectively","Figuring out the positive properties of each food item","Knowing how to remember major events in one's life"],"answer":1,"expl":"「the secret to a long life is knowing how to choose what to forget」——choose what to forget 同义替换 forget selectively。","signal":"also 提示还有一条","syn":[["knowing how to choose what to forget","Having the ability to forget things selectively（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2512b-8","group":"2025年12月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"教育研究","level":"四级","title":"教室座位有讲究","material":"2025年12月 CET-4听力 · Passage 3（第2套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"It's the first day of school, and your teacher tells you to find a seat in the classroom.","zh":"今天是开学第一天，而你老师让你找个座位坐下教室。"},{"en":"Where do you sit?","zh":"你坐在哪里？"},{"en":"Does it matter?","zh":"这重要吗？"},{"en":"Yes, it does matter where you sit in your classroom, so choose, and choose carefully.","zh":"是的，你的座位位置确实很重要。你的教室，所以要仔细选择。"},{"en":"Studies report that where you sit in the classroom can impact your ability to learn and the way your teacher perceives you.","zh":"研究报告显示，你坐在……的位置课堂环境会影响你的学习能力，老师对你的看法。"},{"en":"Guess what else?","zh":"你猜还有什么？"},{"en":"Your grade.","zh":"你的成绩。"},{"en":"Then what is the best seat in the classroom?","zh":"那么，最好的座位是哪里呢？课堂？"},{"en":"In one study, students who sat in the front and center of the classroom received a higher grade average and scored higher on tests than those sitting towards the back of the classroom.","zh":"在一项研究中，坐在……的学生教室前排中间位置的人得到了平均成绩更高，考试分数也更高比坐在后排的人更甚课堂。"},{"en":"Get this.","zh":"拿这个。"},{"en":"Students sitting in the middle of the classroom also outscored students sitting behind them.","zh":"学生们坐在教室中间他们的得分也超过了坐在他们后面的学生。"},{"en":"This study gathered that students had a clearer vision of the blackboard and were able to focus more attention on the instructor.","zh":"这项研究发现，学生们对……有更清晰的认识能够看到黑板，并且能够多集中注意力听老师讲课。"},{"en":"By sitting front and center, students were able to hear better too.","zh":"通过坐在前排中间的位置，学生们能够也能听得更清楚。"},{"en":"The instructors said that they also formed a better connection with the students who sat in front.","zh":"教员们说他们也组建了一个与坐在教室里的学生建立更好的联系正面。"},{"en":"Perhaps the connection is made because of eye contact and visibility and more interaction.","zh":"或许这种联系是因为眼睛而建立的。联系、曝光和更多互动。"},{"en":"But, when you sit in the front row, you may be called on more by your teacher, mainly due to the fact that you are easier to see.","zh":"但是，当你坐在前排时，你可能会被你的……更多地要求你老师，主要是因为你更容易被看到。"},{"en":"So, for students who are not prepared, and for those who are extremely shy, the attention could cause some unwanted stress.","zh":"所以，对于那些没有做好准备的学生来说，对于那些极度害羞的人来说，这种关注可能会造成一些不必要的压力。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What matters to students according to the passage?","opts":["The ability to learn","The first day of school","How teachers perceive them","Where they sit in the classroom"],"answer":3,"expl":"「it does matter where you sit in your classroom」——matter 原词复现。","signal":"does matter 强调","syn":[["where you sit in your classroom","Where they sit in the classroom（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did one study find about students seated in the middle of the classroom?","opts":["They often received close attention from the instructors","They obtained the highest grade average in their class","They actually wanted a clear vision of the blackboard","They scored higher than students sitting behind them"],"answer":3,"expl":"「Students sitting in the middle...also outscored students sitting behind them」——outscore 同义替换 scored higher。","signal":"one study 定位","syn":[["outscored students sitting behind them","They scored higher than students sitting behind them（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did instructors say sitting in front brought about?","opts":["A higher grade average among all students of a class","A better connection between instructors and students","A stronger support for a student-centered teaching approach","A more favorable atmosphere for effective classroom learning"],"answer":1,"expl":"「they also formed a better connection with the students who sat in front」——formed 同义替换。","signal":"instructors said","syn":[["formed a better connection","A better connection between instructors and students（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What do extremely shy students sitting in the front row risk?","opts":["They may experience some unwanted stress","They may try hard to show their preparedness","They may receive extra attention from the instructor","They may feel helpless when called on by the instructor"],"answer":0,"expl":"「the attention could cause some unwanted stress」——原词复现。","signal":"结尾警示","syn":[["cause some unwanted stress","They may experience some unwanted stress（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2606a-1","group":"2026年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"社会趣闻","level":"四级","title":"六岁娃点外卖点出千元账单","material":"2026年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 1（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"A man was left with a $1,000 bill after his six-year -old son ordered a virtual buffet of food from several restaurants last weekend.","zh":"新闻报道1：一名男子被留下六年之后，他收到了一张1000美元的账单。老儿子点了一份虚拟自助餐上周末从几家餐厅买的。"},{"en":"This led to a string of unexpected deliveries and maybe a starring role in an advertisement campaign.","zh":"这导致了一系列意料之外的送货。或许还能在广告中担任主角活动。"},{"en":"Keith Stonehouse said the food piled up quickly at his home Saturday night after he let his son use his cell phone to play a game before bed.","zh":"基思·斯通豪斯说，食物很快就堆积如山。周六晚上，在他家中，他放任不管后，被人发现。他的儿子用他的手机玩游戏睡前玩一局游戏。"},{"en":"He said the youngster instead used his father's online food ordering account to order food from one restaurant after another.","zh":"他说，这名年轻人却用了他父亲的在线订餐账户，用于订购食物一家接一家餐厅。"},{"en":"The boy's mother, Kristin Stonehouse, said that the online food app has reached out to the family and offered them a $1,000 gift card.","zh":"男孩的母亲克里斯汀·斯通豪斯说，在线食品应用程序已与并向该家庭赠送了1000美元的礼物卡片。"},{"en":"The company also is considering using the family in an online promotional campaign.","zh":"该公司也在考虑利用这个家庭在网络推广活动中。"},{"en":"Most of the food went into the family's refrigerators.","zh":"大部分食物都进了家人的肚子。冰箱。"},{"en":"They also invited some neighbours over to eat some of it.","zh":"他们还邀请了一些邻居过来吃饭。一部分。"},{"en":"The father is planning to change his password.","zh":"这位父亲正计划更改密码。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why was Keith Stonehouse left with a $1,000 bill?","opts":["He had bought meals with his online food ordering account","His son had used his cell phone to pay for playing a game","His son had ordered food from several restaurants","He had dined out at a famous five-star restaurant"],"answer":2,"expl":"「his six-year-old son ordered a virtual buffet of food from several restaurants」——order food from several restaurants 同义替换。","signal":"新闻首句因果","syn":[["ordered a virtual buffet of food from several restaurants","His son had ordered food from several restaurants（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the news report say Keith Stonehouse is planning to do?","opts":["Teach his son a lesson","Change his password","Ask his neighbors for help","Buy a bigger refrigerator"],"answer":1,"expl":"「The father is planning to change his password.」——结尾原词复现。","signal":"is planning to 定位","syn":[["change his password","Change his password（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2606a-2","group":"2026年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"科普研究","level":"四级","title":"动物园游客与动物","material":"2026年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 2（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Animal behaviour experts looked at more than 100 research papers.","zh":"动物行为专家研究了100多个案例研究论文。"},{"en":"They examined how visitors affected the behaviour of more than 250 species in zoos.","zh":"他们研究了游客如何影响行为动物园里有超过250种动物。"},{"en":"They found that elephants socialized more with each other during public feeding times.","zh":"他们发现，大象之间彼此之间的社交互动更多。其他时间则在公共喂食期间。"},{"en":"After public feeding times, they were more likely to search for food and less likely to be inactive.","zh":"公共喂食时间结束后，它们更有可能寻找食物，不太可能保持不活跃状态。"},{"en":"In the presence of many visitors, elephants were less likely to use repetitive behaviours which often indicate boredom.","zh":"在众多游客的注视下，大象们……不太可能使用重复性行为，而这些行为通常表示无聊。"},{"en":"Visitors had a similar effect on some other species too, including polar bears, certain jungle cats, and black-tailed plain dogs.","zh":"游客对其他一些事物也产生了类似的影响。也包括北极熊、某些丛林猫科动物等物种。以及黑尾平原犬。"},{"en":"Some animal species have been born and raised in zoos and so have likely become used to the presence of humans.","zh":"有些动物物种是出生后就被饲养的。在动物园里，它们很可能已经被广泛使用。人类的存在。"},{"en":"Zoo visitors are often aspects of zoo animals' environment that animals cannot control and as such can be stressful, although some species appear to show good adaptability to the changing conditions of visitors.","zh":"动物园游客通常是动物园动物的组成部分。动物无法控制的环境，因此可能会带来压力，尽管有些物种似乎……对不断变化的环境表现出良好的适应能力访客。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What did animal behaviour experts do?","opts":["They examined how visitors affected animal behaviour in zoos","They studied when the best time to feed animals in public was","They studied how animals adapted themselves to life in zoos","They examined what behaviours indicated animal boredom"],"answer":0,"expl":"「They examined how visitors affected the behaviour of more than 250 species in zoos」——examined 同义替换。","signal":"首段研究动作","syn":[["examined how visitors affected the behaviour","They examined how visitors affected animal behaviour in zoos（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"Why have some animal species likely become used to the presence of humans?","opts":["They socialise with zookeepers as well as with each other","They show good adaptability to living with humans","They have been kept as pets by humans","They have been born and raised in zoos"],"answer":3,"expl":"「Some animal species have been born and raised in zoos and so have likely become used to the presence of humans」——born and raised 原词复现。","signal":"so 因果词","syn":[["born and raised in zoos","They have been born and raised in zoos（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2606a-3","group":"2026年6月 CET-4","type":"新闻报道","scene":"城市政策","level":"四级","title":"丹佛暂停电动车补贴","material":"2026年6月 CET-4听力 · News Report 3（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Denver is suspending its popular electric bike incentive program.","zh":"丹佛市暂停了广受欢迎的电动自行车补贴计划。程序。"},{"en":"The program was launched in April.","zh":"该项目于四月份启动。"},{"en":"It allowed Denver residents to apply for $400 in government funds before buying an electric bike from a participating shop.","zh":"它允许丹佛居民申请 400 美元。在用政府资金购买电动自行车之前，先购买一辆电动自行车来自参与活动的商店。"},{"en":"Residents who met certain income qualifications could qualify for $1,200.","zh":"符合特定收入条件的居民可以符合资格售价 1200 美元。"},{"en":"More than 3,000 Denver residents applied for incentives within the first three weeks.","zh":"超过3000名丹佛居民申请了前三周内发放奖励。"},{"en":"The city then changed the program to limit the number of applications each month.","zh":"随后，市政府修改了该计划以限制每月申请数量。"},{"en":"On Monday, the city announced the pause.","zh":"周一，市政府宣布暂停营业。"},{"en":"We're honored to be a part of transforming the way Denver wants to move around, said Grace Rink, Denver's chief climate officer.","zh":"我们很荣幸能参与到变革之中。丹佛人希望以这种方式出行，他说。格蕾丝·林克，丹佛首席气候官。"},{"en":"We exhausted three years' worth of funding in six months.","zh":"我们三年的资金都用光了。六个月。"},{"en":"The city said the program has put 4 ,400 electric bikes on the streets of Denver and invested $8.6 million into the local economy.","zh":"该市表示，该项目已投入4丹佛街头有400辆电动自行车并向当地投资了860万美元。经济。"},{"en":"The city has provided 2,200 incentives to lower-income residents.","zh":"该市已提供 2200 项奖励低收入居民。"},{"en":"That represents 68% of the program funding.","zh":"这相当于该项目资金的 68%。"},{"en":"The city expects to resume the program early next year.","zh":"该市预计将提前恢复该项目。明年。"},{"en":"It also plans design changes to make participation easier and increase access to the program.","zh":"它还计划进行设计变更，以增加参与度。更便捷地增加参与该计划的途径。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What is Denver doing with its popular electric bike incentive program?","opts":["Adjusting it","Suspending it","Reevaluating it","Expanding it"],"answer":1,"expl":"「Denver is suspending its popular electric bike incentive program」——suspending 原词复现。","signal":"新闻首句","syn":[["suspending","Suspending it（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How did the electric bike incentive program benefit some residents?","opts":["They could buy an electric bike for $400 in April","They could buy their first electric bike at a discount","They could enjoy free after-sale service for their purchase","They could get $1,200 from government funds if they qualified. 2026"],"answer":3,"expl":"「Residents who met certain income qualifications could qualify for $1,200」——qualify for 原词复现。","signal":"数字 $1,200","syn":[["could qualify for $1,200","They could get $1,200 from government funds if they qualified（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the city of Denver expect to do early next year?","opts":["Put 400 more electric bikes on its streets","Increase the program funding by 8 percent","Resume its electric bike incentive program","Invest millions of dollars into the local economy"],"answer":2,"expl":"「The city expects to resume the program early next year」——resume 同义替换。","signal":"expects to 定位","syn":[["resume the program","Resume its electric bike incentive program（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2606a-4","group":"2026年6月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"旅行观光","level":"四级","title":"罗马游记偶遇","material":"2026年6月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 1（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Hey, Mike.","zh":"嘿，迈克。"},{"en":"What do you think of the museum you visited today?","zh":"你觉得你所在的博物馆怎么样？今天来过吗？"},{"en":"Hey, Sue.","zh":"嗨，苏。"},{"en":"The museum is great.","zh":"这家博物馆很棒。"},{"en":"Very interesting.","zh":"很有意思。"},{"en":"They have loads of stuff there on display.","zh":"那里展出了很多东西。"},{"en":"The primitive tools early humans used tell a lot about their life, but my favorite is the coin collection.","zh":"早期人类使用的原始工具告诉我们……很多关于他们生活的内容，但我最喜欢的是硬币收藏。"},{"en":"They have some coins that are over 2 ,000 years old.","zh":"他们有一些面值超过2的硬币。已有 000 年历史。"},{"en":"That sounds cool.","zh":"听起来不错。"},{"en":"Yeah.","zh":"是的。"},{"en":"What did you do today?","zh":"今天你做了什么？"},{"en":"Kathy and I just wandered through the old city center.","zh":"凯西和我只是在旧城区闲逛。市中心。"},{"en":"The streets are narrow but beautiful, with plenty of charm.","zh":"街道虽然狭窄，但很漂亮，而且有很多……魅力十足。"},{"en":"We saw the Trevi Fountain, which is in all the guidebooks.","zh":"我们参观了特雷维喷泉，它位于所有的旅游指南。"},{"en":"How do you like it?","zh":"你喜欢吗？"},{"en":"It's very pretty, but it was overcrowded with tourists.","zh":"那里很漂亮，但是人太多了。游客。"},{"en":"Yeah, well, it's crowded everywhere.","zh":"是啊，到处都很拥挤。"},{"en":"It is August after all, the busiest month of the year.","zh":"毕竟现在是八月，一年中最繁忙的月份。年度最佳。"},{"en":"Yes, it's like the whole world is here on holiday, including us.","zh":"是的，感觉整个世界都在这里。包括我们，都在度假。"},{"en":"What will you do tomorrow?","zh":"你明天打算做什么？"},{"en":"I haven't decided yet.","zh":"我还没决定。"},{"en":"I was thinking of doing what you did today, wandering the old streets and taking pictures.","zh":"我当时正想着要不要做你做的事。今天，我在老街上闲逛，拍拍照。"},{"en":"I was also thinking of visiting the square with the Spanish steps.","zh":"我也正打算去广场看看。沿着西班牙台阶走。"},{"en":"What is that?","zh":"那是什么？"},{"en":"I haven't heard of it.","zh":"我没听说过。"},{"en":"It's a square where, on one side, there are some very wide steps with flowers that go up to a church.","zh":"这是一个正方形，其中一边是……有一些非常宽阔的台阶，上面点缀着鲜花。去教堂。"},{"en":"It's also in all the tourist guidebooks.","zh":"所有旅游指南上都有提到。"},{"en":"It's very famous and pretty.","zh":"它非常有名，而且很漂亮。"},{"en":"I was also thinking of seeing that tomorrow.","zh":"我明天也打算去看。"},{"en":"It sounds very nice.","zh":"听起来很不错。"},{"en":"Do you mind if Kathy and I join you tomorrow?","zh":"请问我和凯西可以加入吗？你明天会来吗？"},{"en":"Not at all.","zh":"一点也不。"},{"en":"I spent the whole day today pretty much alone.","zh":"我今天几乎一整天都……独自的。"},{"en":"Doing tourist stuff with others would be a welcome change.","zh":"和别人一起做旅游项目会是一种欢迎改变。"},{"en":"Let me ask her first, but I'm sure she'll be up for it.","zh":"我先问问她，但我确信她肯定愿意。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What did the man like best about the museum?","opts":["The coin collection","The primitive tools","The ancient ornaments","The 2,000-year-old clothes"],"answer":0,"expl":"「but my favorite is the coin collection」——favorite 同义替换 like best；but 转折后才是重点。","signal":"but 转折 + favorite","syn":[["my favorite is the coin collection","The coin collection（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man say about the old city center?","opts":["It is charming with narrow but beautiful streets","It attracts visitors from every corner of the world","It has flowers displayed around the Trevi Fountain","It is more attractive than the pictures in guidebooks"],"answer":0,"expl":"「The streets are narrow but beautiful, with plenty of charm」——narrow but beautiful 原词复现。","signal":"评价句","syn":[["narrow but beautiful, with plenty of charm","It is charming with narrow but beautiful streets（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"How does the man describe the square with the Spanish steps?","opts":["It is covered with wild grass","It is very famous and pretty","It is located away from an old church","It is surrounded by Spanish-style houses"],"answer":1,"expl":"「It's very famous and pretty.」——原词复现。","signal":"人名/地名定位","syn":[["very famous and pretty","It is very famous and pretty（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What will the man do at the end of the conversation?","opts":["Ask Kathy what her plan is","Tell Kathy Mike will join them","Ask Kathy if she’d like to see the square","Tell Kathy Mike would like to have a change"],"answer":2,"expl":"「Let me ask her first」——her 指 Kathy，即先问 Kathy 愿不愿意同去。","signal":"结尾计划","syn":[["Let me ask her first","Ask Kathy if she'd like to see the square（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2606a-5","group":"2026年6月 CET-4","type":"长对话","scene":"职场新人","level":"四级","title":"新工作成功之道","material":"2026年6月 CET-4听力 · Conversation 2（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Can you give me advice about being successful at a new job?","zh":"对话2：你能给我一些关于……的建议吗？在新工作中取得成功？"},{"en":"I start mine next week.","zh":"我下周开始。"},{"en":"Sure.","zh":"当然。"},{"en":"It's important not to undermine the significance of the first few days of your job, since this is the best time to create a solid first impression.","zh":"重要的是不要低估其重要性你工作的头几天，因为现在是创建的最佳时机第一印象很好。"},{"en":"That's a good point.","zh":"说得有道理。"},{"en":"I'll need to collaborate with my co-workers, and I'm very aware of just how important others are for my success at work.","zh":"我需要和同事们合作，我非常清楚这有多么重要其他的则是为了我在工作中取得成功。"},{"en":"It's also important to understand your role thoroughly to gain a comprehensive picture of your job.","zh":"透彻理解自己的角色也很重要。全面了解你的工作。"},{"en":"The most important thing for you to do at first is to understand your role from multiple perspectives.","zh":"你最应该做的事首先要了解你的角色。多重视角。"},{"en":"Why's that?","zh":"为什么会这样？"},{"en":"Well, what you do at work is not just limited to your job description.","zh":"嗯，你在工作中做的事情并不是仅限于你的工作职责范围。"},{"en":"You need to consider how your work relates to other people within the organisation.","zh":"你需要考虑你的工作与此有何关联对组织内的其他人员。"},{"en":"Oh, right.","zh":"哦，对。"},{"en":"So, for example, certain reports that I create at the end of the month may be used by a team in another department.","zh":"例如，我创建的某些报告。月底可能会被其他部门的团队使用。"},{"en":"That's right, and in that respect, it's also important to learn about the business to see the big picture.","zh":"没错，从这个角度来看，它也是了解业务很重要。大局观。"},{"en":"You mean like knowing about the history of the company?","zh":"你是说像了解历史那样吗？公司？"},{"en":"Kind of, but more like knowing the details of the products and services that the company exists to deliver.","zh":"算是吧，但更像是了解细节。公司提供的产品和服务存在的目的是为了交付。"},{"en":"Learning about the business will give you a chance to understand how your role fits into the bigger picture.","zh":"了解这个行业会让你受益匪浅。有机会了解你的角色如何融入其中从更宏观的角度来看。"},{"en":"Okay.","zh":"好的。"},{"en":"I'm feeling a bit uneasy about meeting my boss as well.","zh":"我有点不安，不知道该如何与我见面。老板也是。"},{"en":"That's to be expected.","zh":"这是意料之中的。"},{"en":"However, it's crucial that you get to know the people who have decision-making authority to gain insight regarding how the business is run and decisions are made.","zh":"然而，了解这一点至关重要。拥有决策权的人深入了解企业的​​运营方式于是，决定就此做出。"},{"en":"Great advice.","zh":"很好的建议。"},{"en":"Thanks.","zh":"谢谢。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What advice does the man want to get from the woman?","opts":["How to fit into the bigger picture","How to get on with colleagues","How to create a solid first impression","How to succeed in a new job"],"answer":3,"expl":"「Can you give me advice about being successful at a new job?」——原句压缩。","signal":"对话首句","syn":[["advice about being successful at a new job","How to succeed in a new job（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the woman say is the most important thing for the man to do at first?","opts":["Get familiar with all the details of his job description","Learn about the relations within the organization","Recognize his own limitations and weaknesses","Understand his role from various perspectives"],"answer":3,"expl":"「The most important thing...is to understand your role from multiple perspectives」——原词复现。","signal":"most important thing","syn":[["understand your role from multiple perspectives","Understand his role from various perspectives（同义替换 multiple→various）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the man say he is feeling a bit uneasy about?","opts":["Learning history","Meeting his boss","Creating reports for other departments to use","Leaving his coworkers in the present company"],"answer":1,"expl":"「I'm feeling a bit uneasy about meeting my boss」——uneasy 同义替换 nervous。","signal":"uneasy 情绪词","syn":[["feeling a bit uneasy about meeting my boss","Meeting his boss（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does the woman suggest the man do to gain insight into the running of the business?","opts":["Get to know the decision-makers","Acquire decision-making authority","Promote its products and services","Observe its overall management"],"answer":0,"expl":"「it's crucial that you get to know the people who have decision-making authority to gain insight regarding how the business is run」——decision-making authority 同义替换 decision-makers。","signal":"it's crucial that","syn":[["people who have decision-making authority","Get to know the decision-makers（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2606a-6","group":"2026年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"消费心理","level":"四级","title":"情绪主导的消费","material":"2026年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 1（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Contrary to popular belief, consumers aren't as smart as they like to believe.","zh":"与普遍认知相反，消费者并没有那么聪明。正如他们所希望的那样。"},{"en":"Many consumers report comparing multiple competing brands and prices when evaluating a purchase.","zh":"许多消费者表示，他们比较了多个竞争品牌，在评估购买时，价格是一个重要的考虑因素。"},{"en":"However, research indicates that this is not actually the case.","zh":"然而，研究表明事实并非如此。案件。"},{"en":"What consumers really think or feel often contradicts what they say.","zh":"消费者的真实想法或感受往往与……相矛盾他们说的话。"},{"en":"A big reason is that they are driven by unconscious urges, the biggest of which is emotion.","zh":"一个重要原因是他们充满动力。由无意识的冲动所驱动，其中最大的冲动是情感。"},{"en":"Emotion is what really drives the purchasing behaviours, and also decision-making in general.","zh":"真正驱动购买行为的是情感。以及一般的决策过程。"},{"en":"Good marketers keep in mind this important fact all the time.","zh":"优秀的营销人员会牢记这一重要事实。一直如此。"},{"en":"And examples of emotion-based campaigns are everywhere.","zh":"以情感为导向的营销活动比比皆是。"},{"en":"Think for a moment what is actually being sold in most marketing campaigns.","zh":"思考片刻，究竟是什么……在大多数营销活动中均有销售。"},{"en":"Luxury goods target our feelings of self-worth, acceptance and status in the world.","zh":"奢侈品瞄准的是我们的自我价值感。在世界上的认可和地位。"},{"en":"Communication devices excite us by offering a connection to friends, family and a broader network of people.","zh":"通讯设备通过提供连接方式让我们感到兴奋。对朋友、家人和更广泛的社交网络人们。"},{"en":"And many other products, such as rings, target emotions related to love and relationships.","zh":"还有许多其他产品，例如戒指、塔吉特百货等。与爱情和人际关系相关的情感。"},{"en":"As marketers, we should focus on the features of the product.","zh":"作为营销人员，我们应该关注功能该产品。"},{"en":"But we must also sell the lifestyle and the feeling.","zh":"但我们也必须推销这种生活方式，那种感觉。"},{"en":"The key is to highlight the emotional response a consumer will have by using the product.","zh":"关键在于突出情感反应。消费者在使用该产品后将获得什么。"},{"en":"To achieve the highest emotional response, we should target our consumer through many different senses.","zh":"为了获得最高的情感反应，我们应该通过多种感官来吸引我们的消费者。"},{"en":"A lot of what drives consumers is subconscious behaviour.","zh":"很多消费者的行为都是潜意识的。行为。"},{"en":"But this isn't a bad thing.","zh":"但这并不是一件坏事。"},{"en":"There's nothing manipulative about helping consumers achieve desired states of emotion.","zh":"帮助消费者实现目标并没有什么操纵的成分。情绪状态。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does research indicate about consumers?","opts":["They do not tell marketers their feeling about a product","They do not compare competing brands and prices","They are not hesitant to contradict themselves","They are not sure what they really like to buy. 2026"],"answer":1,"expl":"「Many consumers report comparing multiple competing brands and prices...However, research indicates that this is not actually the case」——however 转折否定比较行为。","signal":"however 转折","syn":[["this is not actually the case","They do not compare competing brands and prices（指代还原）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What really drives purchasing behaviour according to the passage?","opts":["Consumers are often attracted by new products","Consumers tend to make decisions on the spot","Consumers find it hard to resist temptation","Consumers are actually driven by emotion"],"answer":3,"expl":"「Emotion is what really drives the purchasing behaviours」——强调句 what really drives。","signal":"强调结构","syn":[["Emotion is what really drives","Consumers are actually driven by emotion（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What should marketers do besides selling the lifestyle and the feeling?","opts":["Draw consumers’ attention to the luxury goods symbolizing quality life","Leave consumers the impression they are doing nothing manipulative","Highlight the emotional response it will trigger in the consumer","Remind consumers of the wide connections it can help to build"],"answer":2,"expl":"「The key is to highlight the emotional response a consumer will have by using the product」——the key is 强调。","signal":"the key is","syn":[["highlight the emotional response","Highlight the emotional response it will trigger in the consumer（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2606a-7","group":"2026年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"环境健康","level":"四级","title":"微塑料进身体","material":"2026年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 2（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"Plastics have for years been used to make nearly everything that surrounds us.","zh":"第二段：塑料制品已被使用了多年。制造我们周围几乎所有的事物。"},{"en":"But along the way, they escaped the confines of packaging and objects and settled in the environment, the food we eat and the air we breathe.","zh":"但在此过程中，他们逃脱了束缚。包装和物品，并安置于环境、我们吃的食物和空气我们呼吸。"},{"en":"Americans are consuming and breathing in a lot of plastic.","zh":"美国人正在大量消费和吸入这些物质。塑料。"},{"en":"Based on available data, Americans take in an estimated 74,000 to 121,000 microplastic particles every year.","zh":"根据现有数据，美国人摄入估计有74,000至121,000个微塑料颗粒每年。"},{"en":"However, scientists believe the true number is probably much higher, because for some likely sources of microplastics, there was no strong data available.","zh":"然而，科学家们认为真实数字可能远不止于此。更高，因为某些可能的来源关于微塑料，目前还没有可靠的数据。"},{"en":"Microplastics get into food and air in several ways.","zh":"微塑料会通过多种途径进入食物和空气。方法。"},{"en":"Many start off as part of larger plastic objects, which over time fragment into smaller and smaller pieces until they become tiny, 5mm or less in diameter.","zh":"许多塑料制品最初都是较大塑料的一部分。物体，随着时间的推移，会碎裂成更小的物体。切成更小的碎片，直到变得非常小，5毫米或直径较小。"},{"en":"They are breathed in or consumed by animals that then become our food.","zh":"它们被动物吸入或摄入。然后它们就成了我们的食物。"},{"en":"The particles float through the air until people breathe them in.","zh":"这些颗粒物漂浮在空气中，直到人们吸入它们。"},{"en":"They also settle on the food that people eat.","zh":"他们也决定了人们的食物。吃。"},{"en":"Data shows that for Americans, air, bottled water and seafood were the biggest sources for breathed in or consumed microplastics.","zh":"数据显示，对美国人来说，空气、瓶装水海鲜是呼吸性二氧化碳的最大来源。存在于或被摄入的微塑料中。"},{"en":"Added sugars accounted for less, and salts, tap water and beer contributed minimal amounts.","zh":"添加糖和盐的含量较少，水和啤酒的含量微乎其微。"},{"en":"These estimates are conservative.","zh":"这些估计较为保守。"},{"en":"The included foods only make up about 15 % of the average American diet.","zh":"所含食物仅占约15%占美国人平均饮食的百分比。"},{"en":"It's not yet known how much plastic is contained in the remaining 85% of the typical diet.","zh":"目前尚不清楚塑料的数量。包含在剩余的 85% 中典型饮食。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does the passage say about Americans?","opts":["They are taking in a lot of plastic","They are polluting the environment","They consume much processed food","They make everything with plastics"],"answer":0,"expl":"「Americans are consuming and breathing in a lot of plastic」——consuming and breathing in 同义替换 taking in。","signal":"转折后核心句","syn":[["consuming and breathing in a lot of plastic","They are taking in a lot of plastic（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What were the biggest sources of microplastics for Americans?","opts":["Beer, salts and added sugars","Tap water and take-away food","Food packages and plastic bags","Air, bottled water and seafood"],"answer":3,"expl":"「air, bottled water and seafood were the biggest sources」——原词复现。","signal":"biggest sources 定位","syn":[["air, bottled water and seafood were the biggest sources","Air, bottled water and seafood（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What is still unknown about Americans' microplastic intake?","opts":["How much plastic there is in the remaining 85% of Americans’ typical diet","What measures can be taken to prevent plastic objects from fragmenting","What harm microplastics may actually do to the average Americans","How many ways there are for microplastics to get into food and air"],"answer":0,"expl":"「It's not yet known how much plastic is contained in the remaining 85% of the typical diet」——not yet known 同义替换 unknown。","signal":"结尾 it's not yet known","syn":[["how much plastic...in the remaining 85%","How much plastic there is in the remaining 85% of Americans' typical diet（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]},{"id":"t2606a-8","group":"2026年6月 CET-4","type":"短文","scene":"健康养老","level":"四级","title":"养宠物的老年收益","material":"2026年6月 CET-4听力 · Passage 3（第1套）","source":"真题PDF题库 + wordcram 双语原文 + 新东方答案键（文本匹配）","sentences":[{"en":"People looking to stay well as they age may want to adopt a pet animal, according to new data from the University of Michigan National Poll on Healthy Aging.","zh":"希望随着年龄增长保持健康的人们根据……可能想要领养宠物根据密歇根大学的最新数据全国健康老龄化民意调查。"},{"en":"For the survey, researchers polled about 2,000 U.S. adults from ages 50 to 80.","zh":"为了进行这项调查，研究人员对大约2000人进行了民意调查。美国50至80岁成年人。"},{"en":"55% said they owned at least one pet.","zh":"55%的人表示他们至少拥有一辆宠物。"},{"en":"Dogs were the most common pet, followed by cats.","zh":"狗是最常见的宠物，其次是猫。"},{"en":"But whatever the type of animal, the vast majority of owners said their pets boosted their mental and physical health.","zh":"但无论是什么类型的动物，广阔的大多数宠物主人表示，他们的宠物提升了他们的……心理和生理健康。"},{"en":"Nearly 90% of older pet owners said their animals helped them enjoy life and feel loved.","zh":"近90%的老年宠物主人表示他们的动物帮助他们享受生活，并感受到喜爱。"},{"en":"Roughly 80% said their pets reduced stress.","zh":"约80%的人表示，宠物减轻了他们的压力。"},{"en":"And almost three-quarters said their pets provided a sense of purpose.","zh":"近四分之三的人表示他们的宠物提供了帮助。使命感。"},{"en":"However, people did report a few disadvantages to pet ownership.","zh":"然而，人们也反映出了一些缺点。饲养宠物。"},{"en":"These included difficulty traveling and financial strains.","zh":"这些问题包括出行困难和经济压力。"},{"en":"6% of pet owners said they'd fallen or injured themselves as a result of having a pet.","zh":"6%的宠物主人表示他们摔倒了。或因以下原因受伤：宠物。"},{"en":"Still, plenty of research has shown that just about anyone can benefit from their pet, since animals can lower stress, reduce symptoms of depression and anxiety, and encourage physical activity.","zh":"然而，大量研究表明，仅仅几乎任何人都能从宠物身上受益，因为动物可以降低压力，减轻抑郁症状。缓解焦虑，并鼓励体育锻炼。"},{"en":"The new poll suggests that pet ownership may be especially beneficial for older adults, given how common loneliness and social isolation are within this age group.","zh":"新的民意调查显示，养宠物可能考虑到这一点，对老年人来说尤其有益：常见的孤独和社会孤立都包含在其中。年龄组。"},{"en":"Human social support comes with a host of health benefits, less stress, lower rates of long -term disease, and more.","zh":"人类社会支持包含诸多方面健康益处、减轻压力、降低长期患病率-长期疾病，等等。"},{"en":"And research shows that interacting with pets can bring many of the same benefits.","zh":"研究表明，与宠物互动可以带来许多相同的好处。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What did over half of the respondents say in the survey?","opts":["They planned to adopt a pet animal","They kept not only a dog but a cat","They had at least one pet","They liked cats more than dogs"],"answer":2,"expl":"「55% said they owned at least one pet」——55% 即 over half。","signal":"数字百分比对折算","syn":[["55% said they owned at least one pet","They had at least one pet（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did most older pet owners say their pets provided?","opts":["A sense of pride","A sense of duty","A sense of purpose","A sense of security"],"answer":2,"expl":"「almost three-quarters said their pets provided a sense of purpose」——provided 原词复现。","signal":"almost three-quarters 定位","syn":[["provided a sense of purpose","A sense of purpose（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What did people report about pet ownership besides benefits?","opts":["A few problems with keeping big animals","Some disadvantages related to pet ownership","A few cases of getting attacked by pet animals","Some conflicts with neighbors due to pet keeping"],"answer":1,"expl":"「people did report a few disadvantages to pet ownership. These included difficulty traveling and financial strains」——disadvantages 原词复现。","signal":"however 转折后","syn":[["a few disadvantages to pet ownership","Some disadvantages related to pet ownership（同义替换）"]],"conf":"verified"},{"q":"What does research show interacting with pets can do for older adults?","opts":["Reduce as many symptoms of depression as medical help","Improve people’s health as much as physical activities","Lower older people’s stress as effectively as exercising","Bring many of the same benefits as human social support"],"answer":3,"expl":"「interacting with pets can bring many of the same benefits」(as human social support)——same benefits 原词复现。","signal":"结尾类比","syn":[["bring many of the same benefits","Bring many of the same benefits as human social support（原词复现）"]],"conf":"verified"}]}];
